{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GYXudPsXbBn9SoKHWvzgci","type":"tool_result","content":"/* =============================================================================\n * 10b. FILTERS  one look over the finished picture: world.filter = { look, apply, bloom, fxaa, ... } (change it any time)\n *   look 'clean'   no filter: the scene goes straight to the screen (no extra pass)\n *        'cel'     Comic cel: light in a few flat bands (bands), colors pushed (punch), ink where the picture changes\n *                  sharply (ink: strength, inkW: width) and round every character's and thing's silhouette\n *        'pixel'   square blocks (px: the block in the picture's pixels), a few levels per channel (levels), ordered\n *                  dithering between them (dither)\n *   apply 'all' | 'objects' (the characters, things and props only) | 'env' (the level only)\n *   bloom: bright parts glow; fxaa: edges smoothed. All in TSL, the same on WebGPU and WebGL 2. With a filter on, the\n *   scene draws a mask of its characters and things beside the picture (MRT), which is how a filter takes them alone\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst FX_DEFAULT = { look: 'clean', apply: 'all', bands: 4, ink: .9, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.3, px: 4, levels: 8, dither: .35, bloom: false, fxaa: false };\nconst fxOn = f => f.look === 'cel' || f.look === 'pixel' || f.bloom || f.fxaa;\nfunction makeFX(world) {\n  const { pass, mrt, output, rtt, float, vec2, vec3, vec4, uv, uniform, floor, mod, abs, max, min, mix, select, smoothstep, luminance, saturation, sRGBTransferOETF } = TSL;\n  const UF = { bands: uniform(4), ink: uniform(.9), inkW: uniform(1.5), punch: uniform(1.3), px: uniform(4), levels: uniform(8), dither: uniform(.35), apply: uniform(0), texel: uniform(new THREE.Vector2(1, 1)), qtexel: uniform(new THREE.Vector2(1, 1)) };\n  const post = new THREE.PostProcessing(PAGE.renderer); post.outputColorTransform = false;   // (the filters end in display colors themselves)\n  const scenePass = pass(world.scene, world.camera.persp); scenePass.setMRT(mrt({ output, mask: float(0) }));\n  const colTex = scenePass.getTextureNode('output'), maskTex = scenePass.getTextureNode('mask'), INK = vec3(.047, .031, .094);\n  const sceneAt = u => sRGBTransferOETF(colTex.sample(u).rgb), maskAt = u => maskTex.sample(u).r;\n  const keep = m => select(UF.apply.equal(0), float(1), select(UF.apply.equal(1), m, float(1).sub(m)));\n  function cel() {\n    const u = uv(), c = sceneAt(u), l = luminance(c);\n    const q = max(floor(l.mul(UF.bands).add(.5)), .5).div(UF.bands), banded = c.mul(q.div(max(l, .002))), punched = saturation(banded, UF.punch);\n    const o = UF.texel.mul(UF.inkW), m = maskAt(u); let edge = float(0), rim = float(0);\n    for (const d of [vec2(o.x, 0), vec2(o.x.negate(), 0), vec2(0, o.y), vec2(0, o.y.negate())]) { edge = max(edge, luminance(sceneAt(u.add(d))).sub(l)); rim = max(rim, m.sub(maskAt(u.add(d)))); }\n    return mix(c, min(max(mix(punched, INK, max(smoothstep(.16, .36, edge), rim).mul(UF.ink)), vec3(0)), vec3(1)), keep(m));\n  }\n3184:const FX_DEFAULT = { look: 'clean', apply: 'all', bands: 4, ink: .9, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.3, px: 4, levels: 8, dither: .35, bloom: false, fxaa: false };\n3184:const FX_DEFAULT = { look: 'clean', apply: 'all', bands: 4, ink: .9, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.3, px: 4, levels: 8, dither: .35, bloom: false, fxaa: false };\n3185-const fxOn = f => f.look === 'cel' || f.look === 'pixel' || f.bloom || f.fxaa;\n3186-function makeFX(world) {\n3187-  const { pass, mrt, output, rtt, float, vec2, vec3, vec4, uv, uniform, floor, mod, abs, max, min, mix, select, smoothstep, luminance, saturation, sRGBTransferOETF } = TSL;\n3280:World3D.SETTINGS = [\n43:const game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: E.World3D.INPUT, menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } });\n44-const LEVEL = { rows: [\n45-  '################',\n46-  '#t............t#',\n47-  '#..g.....==..g.#',\n48-  '#........==....#',\n49-  '#..s.....^^....#',\n--\n246:  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n247-  E.World3D.INPUT: WASD or arrows move, Space jumps, J or a click attacks, Shift dashes, E skill, Q lock, C camera.\n248-\n249-## Your own three.js\n250-E.THREE (three/webgpu), E.TSL, E.RAPIER; world.scene, world.pw (Rapier's world), E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z) (engine\n251-units to three's metres, y up). The rules: WebGPURenderer and node materials only (MeshLambertNodeMaterial,\n252-MeshToonNodeMaterial, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, TSL): never WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer or\n--\n2908:    // the player's settings (World3D.SETTINGS), taken up when they change\n2909-    const st = g.settings || {}, sk = [st.look3d, st.picture3d, st.shadows3d, st.filter3d].join();\n2910-    if (sk !== this._sk) {\n2911-      if (this._sk !== undefined) { if (st.look3d) this.look = st.look3d; if (RES.includes(st.picture3d)) this.res = st.picture3d; if (st.shadows3d !== undefined) this.shadows = !!st.shadows3d; if (st.filter3d) this.filter.look = st.filter3d; }\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"10731430-e71c-48c2-8de2-78a31a9ab19a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:35.126Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/* =============================================================================\n * 10b. FILTERS  one look over the finished picture: world.filter = { look, apply, bloom, fxaa, ... } (change it any time)\n *   look 'clean'   no filter: the scene goes straight to the screen (no extra pass)\n *        'cel'     Comic cel: light in a few flat bands (bands), colors pushed (punch), ink where the picture changes\n *                  sharply (ink: strength, inkW: width) and round every character's and thing's silhouette\n *        'pixel'   square blocks (px: the block in the picture's pixels), a few levels per channel (levels), ordered\n *                  dithering between them (dither)\n *   apply 'all' | 'objects' (the characters, things and props only) | 'env' (the level only)\n *   bloom: bright parts glow; fxaa: edges smoothed. All in TSL, the same on WebGPU and WebGL 2. With a filter on, the\n *   scene draws a mask of its characters and things beside the picture (MRT), which is how a filter takes them alone\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst FX_DEFAULT = { look: 'clean', apply: 'all', bands: 4, ink: .9, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.3, px: 4, levels: 8, dither: .35, bloom: false, fxaa: false };\nconst fxOn = f => f.look === 'cel' || f.look === 'pixel' || f.bloom || f.fxaa;\nfunction makeFX(world) {\n  const { pass, mrt, output, rtt, float, vec2, vec3, vec4, uv, uniform, floor, mod, abs, max, min, mix, select, smoothstep, luminance, saturation, sRGBTransferOETF } = TSL;\n  const UF = { bands: uniform(4), ink: uniform(.9), inkW: uniform(1.5), punch: uniform(1.3), px: uniform(4), levels: uniform(8), dither: uniform(.35), apply: uniform(0), texel: uniform(new THREE.Vector2(1, 1)), qtexel: uniform(new THREE.Vector2(1, 1)) };\n  const post = new THREE.PostProcessing(PAGE.renderer); post.outputColorTransform = false;   // (the filters end in display colors themselves)\n  const scenePass = pass(world.scene, world.camera.persp); scenePass.setMRT(mrt({ output, mask: float(0) }));\n  const colTex = scenePass.getTextureNode('output'), maskTex = scenePass.getTextureNode('mask'), INK = vec3(.047, .031, .094);\n  const sceneAt = u => sRGBTransferOETF(colTex.sample(u).rgb), maskAt = u => maskTex.sample(u).r;\n  const keep = m => select(UF.apply.equal(0), float(1), select(UF.apply.equal(1), m, float(1).sub(m)));\n  function cel() {\n    const u = uv(), c = sceneAt(u), l = luminance(c);\n    const q = max(floor(l.mul(UF.bands).add(.5)), .5).div(UF.bands), banded = c.mul(q.div(max(l, .002))), punched = saturation(banded, UF.punch);\n    const o = UF.texel.mul(UF.inkW), m = maskAt(u); let edge = float(0), rim = float(0);\n    for (const d of [vec2(o.x, 0), vec2(o.x.negate(), 0), vec2(0, o.y), vec2(0, o.y.negate())]) { edge = max(edge, luminance(sceneAt(u.add(d))).sub(l)); rim = max(rim, m.sub(maskAt(u.add(d)))); }\n    return mix(c, min(max(mix(punched, INK, max(smoothstep(.16, .36, edge), rim).mul(UF.ink)), vec3(0)), vec3(1)), keep(m));\n  }\n3184:const FX_DEFAULT = { look: 'clean', apply: 'all', bands: 4, ink: .9, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.3, px: 4, levels: 8, dither: .35, bloom: false, fxaa: false };\n3184:const FX_DEFAULT = { look: 'clean', apply: 'all', bands: 4, ink: .9, inkW: 1.5, punch: 1.3, px: 4, levels: 8, dither: .35, bloom: false, fxaa: false };\n3185-const fxOn = f => f.look === 'cel' || f.look === 'pixel' || f.bloom || f.fxaa;\n3186-function makeFX(world) {\n3187-  const { pass, mrt, output, rtt, float, vec2, vec3, vec4, uv, uniform, floor, mod, abs, max, min, mix, select, smoothstep, luminance, saturation, sRGBTransferOETF } = TSL;\n3280:World3D.SETTINGS = [\n43:const game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: E.World3D.INPUT, menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } });\n44-const LEVEL = { rows: [\n45-  '################',\n46-  '#t............t#',\n47-  '#..g.....==..g.#',\n48-  '#........==....#',\n49-  '#..s.....^^....#',\n--\n246:  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n247-  E.World3D.INPUT: WASD or arrows move, Space jumps, J or a click attacks, Shift dashes, E skill, Q lock, C camera.\n248-\n249-## Your own three.js\n250-E.THREE (three/webgpu), E.TSL, E.RAPIER; world.scene, world.pw (Rapier's world), E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z) (engine\n251-units to three's metres, y up). The rules: WebGPURenderer and node materials only (MeshLambertNodeMaterial,\n252-MeshToonNodeMaterial, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, TSL): never WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer or\n--\n2908:    // the player's settings (World3D.SETTINGS), taken up when they change\n2909-    const st = g.settings || {}, sk = [st.look3d, st.picture3d, st.shadows3d, st.filter3d].join();\n2910-    if (sk !== this._sk) {\n2911-      if (this._sk !== undefined) { if (st.look3d) this.look = st.look3d; if (RES.includes(st.picture3d)) this.res = st.picture3d; if (st.shadows3d !== undefined) this.shadows = !!st.shadows3d; if (st.filter3d) this.filter.look = st.filter3d; }","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GYXudPsXbBn9SoKHWvzgci","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
