{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggygsWRrkFxWYTd8mCNg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011mDNLC6tM8jamJNVYgxSRn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/opus55-plan-x978410/engine/dist/handoff && sed -n '1040,1105p' API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-380","description":"Read audio section of the API index"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2961,"cache_read_input_tokens":194105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2961},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"53127b6e-f35a-47c3-9fbc-b657d87fb477","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:38.900Z","request_id":"req_011CggygsJH2UXjTqz8r2MCA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011mDNLC6tM8jamJNVYgxSRn":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/opus55-plan-x978410/engine/dist/handoff && sed -n '1040,1105p' API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-380","description":"Read audio section of the API index"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011mDNLC6tM8jamJNVYgxSRn","type":"tool_result","content":"- `grid.add(o, x = o.x, y = o.y)`: put o in the bucket at (x, y)\n- `grid.build(list, xk = 'x', yk = 'y')`: clear, then add every live thing in list (skips o.dead); do it once a step\n- `grid.clear()`: empty it\n- `grid.near(x, y, r, fn)`: call fn(o) for everything in the cells touching the circle (check the exact distance yourself)\n- `grid.query(x, y, r)`: what lies within about r of (x, y), as a list (near() calls a function instead)\n- `grid.cell`: new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32): buckets things by position, to find what is near cheaply. cell: the bucket size in world units; map: the buckets\n\n## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. stop() puts the music back\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops\n\n- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon\n- `E.Backdrop.presets` †: the preset names, all ten: day, dusk, night, castle-night, city-night, desert, forest, ocean, cave, space\n- `backdrop.draw(r)` †: draw the backdrop first in draw(r), before the level; it scrolls with the camera by each layer's parallax\n- `backdrop.layers` †: its scenery layers, back to front, with their defaults filled in\n- `backdrop.sky` †: the sky's gradient colors, top to bottom\n\n## 21c. Props\n\n- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, trashcan, firedrum, sandbags, cactus, palm, mushroom` †: the names of the built-in props for r.prop(name, x, y, z, opts)\n- `E.prop(name, o = {})`: build (and cache) a prop: { frames: [sprite], glow: [sprite] | null, w, h }\n\n## 21e. Shapes\n\n- `E.SHAPES: barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed, bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, ... (25)`: the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...})\n- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there warns and keeps the first. Returns { shapes: [ids], materials: [ids], sprites: { id:\n- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turned face), band: 2 (the light: 0 dark .. 4 bright) }) -> { w, h, rgba (Uint8ClampedArra\n- `E.shapeBox(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: where a placed shape stands, as both engines collide with it: E.shapeBox(id | entry, x, y, z, { facing, scale, flip, params }) -> { x, y (its footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy (half its footprint, along its own x and y), c, s (the turn's cosine and sine) }; null for an unknown shape. map.solid makes one solid; world.shape gives it a co\n- `E.shapeInfo(id, o = {})`: what a shape draws, for tools and tests: E.shapeInfo(id, { view: 'iso', facing, scale, mats, params }) -> { w, h, ox, oy, tris, prims (its primitives), parts (each primitive's pixels on screen: 0 is never seen there), colors (distinct), pixels, bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1], rgba }; null for an unknown shape\n- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +y, its own scale applied: place it with the placement's facing, scale and flip). The \n- `E.shapeMesh({ seg })`: seg(r): the segments round a radius r (default 8 to 24)\n- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and bark's ends: uv runs 0 to 1 across each face), pos, nrm, uv (Float32Arrays: three numb\n- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item'\n\n## 21. Ui\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"317e318c-21b6-4ed1-b94d-acd9c868d2f0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:38.917Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `grid.add(o, x = o.x, y = o.y)`: put o in the bucket at (x, y)\n- `grid.build(list, xk = 'x', yk = 'y')`: clear, then add every live thing in list (skips o.dead); do it once a step\n- `grid.clear()`: empty it\n- `grid.near(x, y, r, fn)`: call fn(o) for everything in the cells touching the circle (check the exact distance yourself)\n- `grid.query(x, y, r)`: what lies within about r of (x, y), as a list (near() calls a function instead)\n- `grid.cell`: new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32): buckets things by position, to find what is near cheaply. cell: the bucket size in world units; map: the buckets\n\n## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. stop() puts the music back\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops\n\n- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon\n- `E.Backdrop.presets` †: the preset names, all ten: day, dusk, night, castle-night, city-night, desert, forest, ocean, cave, space\n- `backdrop.draw(r)` †: draw the backdrop first in draw(r), before the level; it scrolls with the camera by each layer's parallax\n- `backdrop.layers` †: its scenery layers, back to front, with their defaults filled in\n- `backdrop.sky` †: the sky's gradient colors, top to bottom\n\n## 21c. Props\n\n- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, trashcan, firedrum, sandbags, cactus, palm, mushroom` †: the names of the built-in props for r.prop(name, x, y, z, opts)\n- `E.prop(name, o = {})`: build (and cache) a prop: { frames: [sprite], glow: [sprite] | null, w, h }\n\n## 21e. Shapes\n\n- `E.SHAPES: barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed, bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, ... (25)`: the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...})\n- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there warns and keeps the first. Returns { shapes: [ids], materials: [ids], sprites: { id:\n- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turned face), band: 2 (the light: 0 dark .. 4 bright) }) -> { w, h, rgba (Uint8ClampedArra\n- `E.shapeBox(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: where a placed shape stands, as both engines collide with it: E.shapeBox(id | entry, x, y, z, { facing, scale, flip, params }) -> { x, y (its footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy (half its footprint, along its own x and y), c, s (the turn's cosine and sine) }; null for an unknown shape. map.solid makes one solid; world.shape gives it a co\n- `E.shapeInfo(id, o = {})`: what a shape draws, for tools and tests: E.shapeInfo(id, { view: 'iso', facing, scale, mats, params }) -> { w, h, ox, oy, tris, prims (its primitives), parts (each primitive's pixels on screen: 0 is never seen there), colors (distinct), pixels, bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1], rgba }; null for an unknown shape\n- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +y, its own scale applied: place it with the placement's facing, scale and flip). The \n- `E.shapeMesh({ seg })`: seg(r): the segments round a radius r (default 8 to 24)\n- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and bark's ends: uv runs 0 to 1 across each face), pos, nrm, uv (Float32Arrays: three numb\n- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item'\n\n## 21. Ui","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011mDNLC6tM8jamJNVYgxSRn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
