{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh33MMPpNWj3dfMj358H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SqkrJyc2sZQS4JhBXp84mi","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","offset":354,"limit":230},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7159,"cache_read_input_tokens":489181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7159},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"f18b5429-9a47-454f-ab76-fff9af0b0866","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:40:37.577Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh33M5mtiyqKTxsJ1d26","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SqkrJyc2sZQS4JhBXp84mi":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","offset":354,"limit":230}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SqkrJyc2sZQS4JhBXp84mi","type":"tool_result","content":"354\t   that much on every `k` (a 120 ms release). The house and trance songs use it.\n355\t5. **World3D particle ground.** In `World3D.draw` (search `g.particles.ground = (x, y, z) => this.level.floorAt`),\n356\t   use `this.o.particleGround || ((x, y, z) => this.level.floorAt(x, y, z))`. We pass `(x, y, z) => track surface\n357\t   below`, so sparks land on the track, not on the terrain 30 m below.\n358\t6. **(If needed) logarithmic depth.** If distant coplanar geometry z-fights, pass `logarithmicDepthBuffer: true` to\n359\t   `new THREE.WebGPURenderer` in `init`. Try polygon offset on the decal materials first (§3.7).\n360\t7. **Hub rule: Create + Options.** In a session the race is not pausable at all (`pausable: false`), so Options never\n361\t   opens our pause. No engine change is needed. Note it in the About screen.\n362\t\n363\tRecord every change and its reason in `SN.ABOUT.engineChanges` (shown in About and the exit interview).\n364\t\n365\t### 2.8 Determinism rules\n366\t\n367\t- The sim depends only on the seed, the track and class, the Tune values (snapshotted into each replay), and per-step\n368\t  controls. Ships update in grid order and pairs collide in index order.\n369\t- `R.hash()` is FNV-1a over the Float32 bits of every ship's `(p, u, h, |v|, energy, lap)` and every projectile's\n370\t  `(s, u)`, the same algorithm as World3D's `hashNumbers`.\n371\t- Each race records `{ seed, track, cls, mode, laps, entrants, tune, frames[] }`, with `frames` holding the human\n372\t  controls per step. Pack them as Int8 steer/pitch, Uint8 brakes, and a bit field. Run-length encode repeated frames.\n373\t  Replaying must reproduce `R.hash()` at the end (a test).\n374\t- AI uses its own RNG stream. Rigs and particles may use `Math.random` because they never feed back into the sim.\n375\t\n376\t---\n377\t## 3. Systems\n378\t\n379\t### 3.1 Track system (`20-track.js`)\n380\t\n381\t**TrackDef (data, metres; §4.3 has all four):**\n382\t\n383\t```js\n384\tSN.TRACKS.solenne = {\n385\t  id: 'solenne', name: 'PORT SOLENNE', place: 'RIVIERA SPRAWL · MEDITERRANEAN ZONE', tier: 1, theme: 'coast', song: 'solenne',\n386\t  width: 28,                       // metres, full width between the walls (per control point override: { w })\n387\t  origin: [2048, 2048, 0],         // metres, added to every point (keeps the world inside World3D's terrain square)\n388\t  points: [[x, y, z], ...],        // or [x, y, z, { w, bank, tag }]; a closed loop in driving order\n389\t  start: 230,                      // metres along the spline from points[0] to the start line (s = 0 after rebasing)\n390\t  jumps:  [{ from: 12, to: 14, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE HARBOUR STEP' }],                 // control-point indices\n391\t  tunnels:[{ a: { cp: 7, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 40 }, style: 'stone' }],\n392\t  speedPads:  [{ cp: 1, d: 120, u: 0 }, ...],   // cp + d metres along the track, u metres lateral (+ right)\n393\t  weaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 80 }, ...],          // a row of three pads across (u = -8, 0, +8), or { u } for one\n394\t  pit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 259 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },\n395\t  openEdges: [{ a: {…}, b: {…}, side: 'left' }],  // no wall: a craft can leave the track and fall (rescue)\n396\t  banks: [{ from: 15, to: 20, deg: 28 }],         // manual bank over a run of control points (else auto)\n397\t  scenery: {...}                                  // theme parameters (§4.3, §3.7)\n398\t};\n399\t```\n400\t\n401\t**Build (`SN.Track.build(def)`, deterministic, about 10 ms each):**\n402\t\n403\t1. Convert points to u (`×16`, plus the origin). Build a closed **centripetal Catmull-Rom** (α = 0.5) through them:\n404\t   App. A, the same code as `tools/trackcheck.mjs`. Sample each segment 64 times, accumulate arc length, then\n405\t   **resample at ds = 32 u (2 m)**, giving 1,900–2,520 slices. Record each control point's knot `s` exactly (needed by\n406\t   the `{cp, d}` features).\n407\t2. Rebase so that `s = 0` is at `start`. Every stored `s` is then `(raw − start) mod L`.\n408\t3. Per slice: `C` (centre), `F` (unit tangent from central differences), the plan-view curvature `κ` (signed, from the\n409\t   heading change over ±10 m), the width `w` (interpolated per control point; half width `hw = w/2`), the **bank** and\n410\t   the frame. Auto bank is `b = clamp(1600 / R_m, 0, 28)°`, signed by `κ` and smoothed over ±40 m (a 120 m radius\n411\t   gives 13°, 56 m gives 28°). A manual `banks` entry overrides it with a 60 m blend at each end. Frame:\n412\t   `R0 = normalize(cross(Zup, F))`, `U0 = cross(F, R0)`, then rotate both by the bank (§2.4).\n413\t4. Features → slice flags and lists:\n414\t   - `gap` and `drop` ranges from the jumps;\n415\t   - `tunnel` with its ceiling at 12 m;\n416\t   - `open` per side; `pit` range and side;\n417\t   - pads as rectangles in (s, u): speed pad 8 m long × 6 m wide, weapon pad 6 × 6 m;\n418\t   - **8 sectors** at equal s;\n419\t   - **grid slots**: 8 slots, 2 per row, rows 16 m apart, the first row 10 m behind the line, at `u = ∓4.5 m`,\n420\t     staggered 6 m;\n421\t   - **overpasses**: auto-detected exactly as the checker does (App. C), with the clearance stored.\n422\t5. **2D bucket grid** (cell 32 m) of slice indices for `T.query(x, y, zHint)`. It feeds particles, the terrain carve,\n423\t   scenery placement, trackside cameras and the minimap.\n424\t6. Validation (throws with the track id and the reason):\n425\t   - length within 1 % of §4.3;\n426\t   - every overpass clearance ≥ 12 m;\n427\t   - no unintended overlap;\n428\t   - every drop has a heading change ≤ 25° and every gap ≤ 10°;\n429\t   - no pad in a gap or drop;\n430\t   - a weapon pad row fits inside `hw − 1 m`;\n431\t   - the pit range has no jump.\n432\t\n433\t**Surface model (`T.surface(s, u)`):**\n434\t\n435\t| Slice kind | Surface point P, normal N | Walls |\n436\t| --- | --- | --- |\n437\t| `deck` (normal) | `P = C + R'·u`, `N = U'` | at `±hw`, unless the edge is `open` |\n438\t| `gap` (a void) | none. The craft is airborne. Below `zLip − 40 m` it is a **fall**, and a rescue follows | none |\n439\t| `drop` (step down) | the **lower deck**: flat, at the far edge's height `z1`, following the spline in plan view: `P = (C.x + R'h.x·u, C.y + R'h.y·u, z1 + bank1 tilt)`, where `R'h` is the horizontal part of `R'`, `N = up` tilted by the far edge's bank | at `±hw(s1)` along the plan path |\n440\t| `tunnel` | as deck, plus a ceiling at `h = 12 m`: clamp the craft below `12 m − 1.5 m` and cancel its upward velocity | yes |\n441\t\n442\t**`T.locate(P, sHint)`** runs 3 Newton steps: `s += dot(P − C(s), F(s))` (clamped to ±64 u a step, wrapping at L),\n443\tthen `u = dot(P − C, R')` and `h = dot(P − Psurf, N)`. It is always local to the craft's previous `s`, which makes\n444\toverpasses safe: the lower track is never \"found\" from the upper one. Each craft keeps `s` continuous. Its progress\n445\t`p` adds L on each forward wrap and subtracts on a backward one.\n446\t\n447\t**Racing line and speed profile (per track, per class, built at load):**\n448\t- *Line:* an elastic band. Start with u = 0 everywhere. Repeat 400 times over all slices:\n449\t  `mid = (P[i−1] + P[i+1]) / 2`, `u_i += 0.5·(dot(mid − C_i, R'_i) − u_i)`, clamp `|u_i| ≤ hw_i − 3.5 m`. On a gap\n450\t  approach (150 m before the lip to the far edge) pull u toward 0, weight 0.8. That gives the minimum-curvature line.\n451\t  Then compute its own plan curvature `κL`.\n452\t- *Speed:* `vmax_i = min(top_c, sqrt(alat_c / |κL_i|))`, with\n453\t  `alat_c = 640 u/s² × (top_c / 1440)^1.5 × skill` (40 m/s² at SPARK). Then a forward pass with\n454\t  `a = athr_c·(1 − (v/top_c)²)`, a backward pass with airbrake deceleration `450 u/s² × (top_c/1440)` (28 m/s² at\n455\t  SPARK), repeated 3 times around the loop. On a **gap** approach enforce `v ≥ vJump` (1360 u/s = 85 m/s for the\n456\t  Karakum gorge, whose checked minimum is 75 m/s). Gap and drop slices ignore curvature.\n457\t- These two arrays drive the AI (§3.5), autopilot, the attract mode, the bots in the tests, the medal calibration and\n458\t  the TV director's anticipation.\n459\t\n460\t**Minimap:** the plan-view polyline of `C` every 20 m, fitted to a 72 × 72 px box (aspect kept). Overpass upper\n461\tsections are drawn last and brighter.\n462\t\n463\t### 3.2 Craft physics and handling (`25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js`)\n464\t\n465\t**State per craft:** `P, V` (world, u and u/s), `F` (heading, unit), the frame `U, R`, `s, u, h, p` (track), `lap`,\n466\t`sector`, `grounded`, `airT`, `energy` (0..100), `boostT`, `boostMul`, `weapon`, `charge`, `lockT`, `shieldT`\n467\t(bulwark), `autoT`, `rollT` and `rollDir`, `rollDone`, `shiftCD`, `stagger`, `rescueT`, `elim`, `respawnT`,\n468\t`finished`, `stats` (hits, kills, wall touches, pads, rolls, best lap…), `prev` (last step's `P`, quaternion; for\n469\tdrawing).\n470\t\n471\t**Craft constants.** Length 6 m (96 u). Collision is 2 spheres of r = 22 u at ±26 u along F. Hover height\n472\t`H0 = 14 u`. Ship half width for the walls: 24 u.\n473\t\n474\t**Class (§4.2) × team stats (§4.1) give the effective numbers.** Stats run 1–10:\n475\t- `top = classTop × (0.94 + 0.012·speed)`;\n476\t- `athr = 0.55·top × (0.80 + 0.04·thrust)`;\n477\t- `steer = 1.9 rad/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`;\n478\t- `grip = 5.5/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`;\n479\t- `dmgMul = 1.35 − 0.06·shield`;\n480\t- `mass = 0.8 + 0.05·shield`.\n481\t\n482\tAll of them are also multiplied by the Tune sliders.\n483\t\n484\t**The step** (1/120 s, in this order, for each craft in grid order):\n485\t\n486\t1. **Controls in.** From the human mapping (§3.9), the AI, the replay, the autopilot or the bot. Keyboard steering\n487\t   ramps at 6/s toward ±1 so the keys feel analog. The stick passes straight through.\n488\t2. **Yaw.** `yawTarget = steer·steerRate·(1 − 0.35·v/top) + (brakeR − brakeL)·airbrakeYaw` (with\n489\t   `airbrakeYaw = 1.4 rad/s × (top/1440)^0.5`). `yawRate → yawTarget` at `steerResponse` (9/s). Rotate F about U by\n490\t   `yawRate·dt`. While `stagger > 0` (a hit), steering is ignored and the craft wobbles ±0.4 rad/s.\n491\t3. **Thrust and drag**, along F:\n492\t   - `a = thrust·athr·boostK − cd·v² − coast − brakeDrag`;\n493\t   - `cd = athr / top²` (so held thrust settles at `top`);\n494\t   - while boosting, `top·boostMul` replaces `top` in `cd` and the thrust is ×1.8;\n495\t   - `coast = 40 u/s²` when not thrusting;\n496\t   - `brakeDrag = (brakeL + brakeR)/2 × airbrakeDrag × 0.35·top`;\n497\t   - slope: add `−300 u/s² × F.z` (downhill speeds you up);\n498\t   - pitch: nose-down cuts drag by 3 %·pitch.\n499\t4. **Grip.** Split V into the along-F part and the lateral part `vl = dot(V, R)`. Then\n500\t   `vl *= exp(−grip·(1 − 0.30·max(brakeL, brakeR))·dt)` (airbrakes let it slide). Scrub:\n501\t   `|V| −= 0.12·|vl|·dt·60`. A side-shift press (cooldown 0.6 s, grounded) adds `±sideShiftSpeed` (700 u/s) to `vl`\n502\t   and plays thruster puffs.\n503\t5. **Hover / air.** Get the surface at the craft's `(s, u)`.\n504\t   - **Grounded:** surface present and `h < captureH` (64 u).\n505\t     - Spring along N: `aN = k·(Ht − h) − c·vN`, clamped to `[−magnetPull, +900]`, with `k = 220/s²`, `c = 28/s`,\n506\t       `magnetPull = 1800 u/s²` and `Ht = H0 − 4·pitch + bob` (bob is `1.2·sin(2.2 t)`).\n507\t     - Gravity is cancelled while grounded: the anti-gravity field is the source's fiction.\n508\t     - The craft's up vector U slerps to N at 12/s.\n509\t     - At crests the spring cannot pull hard enough, so `h` grows past `captureH` and the craft lifts off by itself.\n510\t       Ramps launch the same way.\n511\t   - **Airborne:** `a = −airGravity·(1 + 0.45·pitch)·Zup` (airGravity 640 u/s² = 40 m/s²). U slerps to the surface\n512\t     normal below (if one is within 200 u) or else to Zup at 2/s. `airT += dt`.\n513\t   - **Landing** (surface present, `h < H0 + 4`, `vN < 0`): impact angle `θ = atan(−vN / v)`.\n514\t     - If `θ > 25°`: energy `−(θ − 25)·0.4·dmgMul`, speed `×(1 − min(0.35, (θ − 15°)/60°))`, and a hard-landing event\n515\t       (shake, sparks, a \"THUD\").\n516\t     - Otherwise a soft landing.\n517\t     - Either way, resolve the barrel roll (step 7).\n518\t   - **Bottoming out:** `h < 5 u` → `h = 5`, `vN = max(vN, 0)`, speed `×0.996` per step, a scrape event.\n519\t6. **Integrate** `V += a·dt`, `P += V·dt`. Then `T.locate` → `s, u, h`.\n520\t7. **Barrel roll.** Triggers only when airborne with `airT > 0.08 s`:\n521\t   - a side-shift press, or\n522\t   - a steer flick (steer crosses ≤ −0.7 then ≥ +0.7, or the reverse, and back, within 0.4 s; detected in\n523\t     `01-input.js`).\n524\t\n525\t   The roll starts with `rollT = 0.45 s` toward rollDir and costs `rollCost` (10) energy. On landing:\n526\t   - a finished roll → boost (`boostMul 1.2`, 1.2 s) + \"BARREL ROLL\" event;\n527\t   - a roll still turning → \"BOTCHED\": speed ×0.75, energy −5, stagger 0.5 s.\n528\t\n529\t   The visual is a full 360° about F. Long jumps allow several rolls, each costing energy.\n530\t8. **Walls** (deck/drop, wall present on that side). `lim = hw − 24 u`. If `|u| > lim`:\n531\t   - push P back by `(|u| − lim)` along ∓R';\n532\t   - normal speed `vn = dot(V, ±R')`; if `vn > 0`, then `V −= ±R'·vn·(1 + wallBounce)` with `wallBounce` 0.35;\n533\t   - tangential scrub: `V −= F·min(v, wallFriction·vn)` with `wallFriction` 0.25;\n534\t   - **yaw nudge:** rotate F toward the track tangent by `min(0.5, 0.6·vn/v)` rad (the craft never grinds nose-first);\n535\t   - damage `wallDamage·clamp((vn − 150)/120, 0, 12)·dmgMul`;\n536\t   - scraping (in contact with `vn ≤ 150`) costs 4 energy/s while `v > 500`;\n537\t   - events `wall` / `scrape`.\n538\t\n539\t   **Open edges:** `|u| > hw + 2 m` with no wall means no surface. The craft falls, and a rescue follows (step 11).\n540\t9. **Pads and pit** (in track space, grounded only):\n541\t   - **Speed pad:** `boostT = min(2.0, max(boostT, padBoostTime))` (0.9 s), `boostMul = padBoost` (1.25). A pad\n542\t     re-arms per craft after 0.5 s.\n543\t   - **Weapon pad:** if no weapon is held, roll one (§3.4); event `pickup`.\n544\t   - **Pit strip:** `energy += pitRecharge·dt` (25/s), a green shimmer FX and a recharge sound loop.\n545\t10. **Energy.** Every damage source goes through `SN.Ship.damage(ship, amount, cause, by)`. It applies `dmgMul`.\n546\t    `shieldT > 0` (bulwark) or god mode blocks it. Below 25 % a warning plays. At 0 the craft is eliminated (§3.3\n547\t    decides between DNF and respawn).\n548\t11. **Rescue.** Triggered by:\n549\t    - a fall below the kill height (gap: `zLip − 40 m`; otherwise surface − 60 m);\n550\t    - being off an open edge for 1 s;\n551\t    - being stuck (`v < 50 u/s` for 3 s while thrusting, outside the countdown).\n552\t\n553\t    The rescue drone lifts the craft back on the centre line at `s_lastGood + 20 m` (the last grounded `s` with\n554\t    `|u| < hw`), in 2.5 s with the craft frozen. Energy −10, speed 0, event `rescue`. In OVERCLOCK the rescue costs 20\n555\t    energy.\n556\t12. **Ship–ship collisions** (`27-collide.js`, after all craft move, pairs in index order): sphere pairs. The craft are\n557\t    separated along the contact normal in inverse proportion to mass. Impulse\n558\t    `j = −(1 + 0.3)·vn / (1/m1 + 1/m2)`. Damage `0.004·|vn|` each. A `bump` event fires above 120 u/s. Ghost craft\n559\t    (hub, dev \"ghost AI\") skip this.\n560\t13. **Launch boost** (countdown): holding thrust raises the revs at 0.6/s; releasing drops them at 0.8/s.\n561\t    - At GO, revs in 0.72–0.88 → \"PERFECT START\" boost (1.0 s, ×1.25).\n562\t    - Revs above 0.95 → \"STALL\" (no thrust for 0.5 s).\n563\t    - The HUD shows a rev bar during the countdown.\n564\t\n565\t**Feel targets (checked by the physics tests; tune with the sliders until they hold):**\n566\t- 0 → 90 % of top in 2.4–3.0 s.\n567\t- Thrust-only top speed within ±2 % of `top`.\n568\t- A 56 m hairpin at SPARK is takeable at 160–190 km/h with an airbrake, touching no wall.\n569\t- Full-lock steering without airbrakes at top speed gives a drift angle of 12–20°.\n570\t- Every jump in §4.3 behaves as App. C says, at each class's top speed (gap: clears at ≥ 75 m/s, falls short below\n571\t  60 m/s).\n572\t- At 3,000 u/s nothing tunnels through a wall or the surface.\n573\t\n574\t**Visual-only motion** (computed in `62-shipkit.js` from the state, never fed back):\n575\t- roll = bank + `clamp(yawRate·0.28, ±0.5)` + barrel roll angle;\n576\t- pitch = slope + `pitch·7°` + bob;\n577\t- airbrake flaps open by `brake·60°`;\n578\t- engine glow follows thrust;\n579\t- the boost flame lengthens with `boostT`;\n580\t- the shield shell flashes on a hit;\n581\t- below 25 % energy, damage smoke and sparks.\n582\t\n583\t### 3.3 Race director and modes (`40-race.js`)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"a0fc9990-916c-447b-8db1-2424d5c2e849","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:40:37.583Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"   that much on every `k` (a 120 ms release). The house and trance songs use it.\n5. **World3D particle ground.** In `World3D.draw` (search `g.particles.ground = (x, y, z) => this.level.floorAt`),\n   use `this.o.particleGround || ((x, y, z) => this.level.floorAt(x, y, z))`. We pass `(x, y, z) => track surface\n   below`, so sparks land on the track, not on the terrain 30 m below.\n6. **(If needed) logarithmic depth.** If distant coplanar geometry z-fights, pass `logarithmicDepthBuffer: true` to\n   `new THREE.WebGPURenderer` in `init`. Try polygon offset on the decal materials first (§3.7).\n7. **Hub rule: Create + Options.** In a session the race is not pausable at all (`pausable: false`), so Options never\n   opens our pause. No engine change is needed. Note it in the About screen.\n\nRecord every change and its reason in `SN.ABOUT.engineChanges` (shown in About and the exit interview).\n\n### 2.8 Determinism rules\n\n- The sim depends only on the seed, the track and class, the Tune values (snapshotted into each replay), and per-step\n  controls. Ships update in grid order and pairs collide in index order.\n- `R.hash()` is FNV-1a over the Float32 bits of every ship's `(p, u, h, |v|, energy, lap)` and every projectile's\n  `(s, u)`, the same algorithm as World3D's `hashNumbers`.\n- Each race records `{ seed, track, cls, mode, laps, entrants, tune, frames[] }`, with `frames` holding the human\n  controls per step. Pack them as Int8 steer/pitch, Uint8 brakes, and a bit field. Run-length encode repeated frames.\n  Replaying must reproduce `R.hash()` at the end (a test).\n- AI uses its own RNG stream. Rigs and particles may use `Math.random` because they never feed back into the sim.\n\n---\n## 3. Systems\n\n### 3.1 Track system (`20-track.js`)\n\n**TrackDef (data, metres; §4.3 has all four):**\n\n```js\nSN.TRACKS.solenne = {\n  id: 'solenne', name: 'PORT SOLENNE', place: 'RIVIERA SPRAWL · MEDITERRANEAN ZONE', tier: 1, theme: 'coast', song: 'solenne',\n  width: 28,                       // metres, full width between the walls (per control point override: { w })\n  origin: [2048, 2048, 0],         // metres, added to every point (keeps the world inside World3D's terrain square)\n  points: [[x, y, z], ...],        // or [x, y, z, { w, bank, tag }]; a closed loop in driving order\n  start: 230,                      // metres along the spline from points[0] to the start line (s = 0 after rebasing)\n  jumps:  [{ from: 12, to: 14, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE HARBOUR STEP' }],                 // control-point indices\n  tunnels:[{ a: { cp: 7, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 40 }, style: 'stone' }],\n  speedPads:  [{ cp: 1, d: 120, u: 0 }, ...],   // cp + d metres along the track, u metres lateral (+ right)\n  weaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 80 }, ...],          // a row of three pads across (u = -8, 0, +8), or { u } for one\n  pit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 259 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },\n  openEdges: [{ a: {…}, b: {…}, side: 'left' }],  // no wall: a craft can leave the track and fall (rescue)\n  banks: [{ from: 15, to: 20, deg: 28 }],         // manual bank over a run of control points (else auto)\n  scenery: {...}                                  // theme parameters (§4.3, §3.7)\n};\n```\n\n**Build (`SN.Track.build(def)`, deterministic, about 10 ms each):**\n\n1. Convert points to u (`×16`, plus the origin). Build a closed **centripetal Catmull-Rom** (α = 0.5) through them:\n   App. A, the same code as `tools/trackcheck.mjs`. Sample each segment 64 times, accumulate arc length, then\n   **resample at ds = 32 u (2 m)**, giving 1,900–2,520 slices. Record each control point's knot `s` exactly (needed by\n   the `{cp, d}` features).\n2. Rebase so that `s = 0` is at `start`. Every stored `s` is then `(raw − start) mod L`.\n3. Per slice: `C` (centre), `F` (unit tangent from central differences), the plan-view curvature `κ` (signed, from the\n   heading change over ±10 m), the width `w` (interpolated per control point; half width `hw = w/2`), the **bank** and\n   the frame. Auto bank is `b = clamp(1600 / R_m, 0, 28)°`, signed by `κ` and smoothed over ±40 m (a 120 m radius\n   gives 13°, 56 m gives 28°). A manual `banks` entry overrides it with a 60 m blend at each end. Frame:\n   `R0 = normalize(cross(Zup, F))`, `U0 = cross(F, R0)`, then rotate both by the bank (§2.4).\n4. Features → slice flags and lists:\n   - `gap` and `drop` ranges from the jumps;\n   - `tunnel` with its ceiling at 12 m;\n   - `open` per side; `pit` range and side;\n   - pads as rectangles in (s, u): speed pad 8 m long × 6 m wide, weapon pad 6 × 6 m;\n   - **8 sectors** at equal s;\n   - **grid slots**: 8 slots, 2 per row, rows 16 m apart, the first row 10 m behind the line, at `u = ∓4.5 m`,\n     staggered 6 m;\n   - **overpasses**: auto-detected exactly as the checker does (App. C), with the clearance stored.\n5. **2D bucket grid** (cell 32 m) of slice indices for `T.query(x, y, zHint)`. It feeds particles, the terrain carve,\n   scenery placement, trackside cameras and the minimap.\n6. Validation (throws with the track id and the reason):\n   - length within 1 % of §4.3;\n   - every overpass clearance ≥ 12 m;\n   - no unintended overlap;\n   - every drop has a heading change ≤ 25° and every gap ≤ 10°;\n   - no pad in a gap or drop;\n   - a weapon pad row fits inside `hw − 1 m`;\n   - the pit range has no jump.\n\n**Surface model (`T.surface(s, u)`):**\n\n| Slice kind | Surface point P, normal N | Walls |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `deck` (normal) | `P = C + R'·u`, `N = U'` | at `±hw`, unless the edge is `open` |\n| `gap` (a void) | none. The craft is airborne. Below `zLip − 40 m` it is a **fall**, and a rescue follows | none |\n| `drop` (step down) | the **lower deck**: flat, at the far edge's height `z1`, following the spline in plan view: `P = (C.x + R'h.x·u, C.y + R'h.y·u, z1 + bank1 tilt)`, where `R'h` is the horizontal part of `R'`, `N = up` tilted by the far edge's bank | at `±hw(s1)` along the plan path |\n| `tunnel` | as deck, plus a ceiling at `h = 12 m`: clamp the craft below `12 m − 1.5 m` and cancel its upward velocity | yes |\n\n**`T.locate(P, sHint)`** runs 3 Newton steps: `s += dot(P − C(s), F(s))` (clamped to ±64 u a step, wrapping at L),\nthen `u = dot(P − C, R')` and `h = dot(P − Psurf, N)`. It is always local to the craft's previous `s`, which makes\noverpasses safe: the lower track is never \"found\" from the upper one. Each craft keeps `s` continuous. Its progress\n`p` adds L on each forward wrap and subtracts on a backward one.\n\n**Racing line and speed profile (per track, per class, built at load):**\n- *Line:* an elastic band. Start with u = 0 everywhere. Repeat 400 times over all slices:\n  `mid = (P[i−1] + P[i+1]) / 2`, `u_i += 0.5·(dot(mid − C_i, R'_i) − u_i)`, clamp `|u_i| ≤ hw_i − 3.5 m`. On a gap\n  approach (150 m before the lip to the far edge) pull u toward 0, weight 0.8. That gives the minimum-curvature line.\n  Then compute its own plan curvature `κL`.\n- *Speed:* `vmax_i = min(top_c, sqrt(alat_c / |κL_i|))`, with\n  `alat_c = 640 u/s² × (top_c / 1440)^1.5 × skill` (40 m/s² at SPARK). Then a forward pass with\n  `a = athr_c·(1 − (v/top_c)²)`, a backward pass with airbrake deceleration `450 u/s² × (top_c/1440)` (28 m/s² at\n  SPARK), repeated 3 times around the loop. On a **gap** approach enforce `v ≥ vJump` (1360 u/s = 85 m/s for the\n  Karakum gorge, whose checked minimum is 75 m/s). Gap and drop slices ignore curvature.\n- These two arrays drive the AI (§3.5), autopilot, the attract mode, the bots in the tests, the medal calibration and\n  the TV director's anticipation.\n\n**Minimap:** the plan-view polyline of `C` every 20 m, fitted to a 72 × 72 px box (aspect kept). Overpass upper\nsections are drawn last and brighter.\n\n### 3.2 Craft physics and handling (`25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js`)\n\n**State per craft:** `P, V` (world, u and u/s), `F` (heading, unit), the frame `U, R`, `s, u, h, p` (track), `lap`,\n`sector`, `grounded`, `airT`, `energy` (0..100), `boostT`, `boostMul`, `weapon`, `charge`, `lockT`, `shieldT`\n(bulwark), `autoT`, `rollT` and `rollDir`, `rollDone`, `shiftCD`, `stagger`, `rescueT`, `elim`, `respawnT`,\n`finished`, `stats` (hits, kills, wall touches, pads, rolls, best lap…), `prev` (last step's `P`, quaternion; for\ndrawing).\n\n**Craft constants.** Length 6 m (96 u). Collision is 2 spheres of r = 22 u at ±26 u along F. Hover height\n`H0 = 14 u`. Ship half width for the walls: 24 u.\n\n**Class (§4.2) × team stats (§4.1) give the effective numbers.** Stats run 1–10:\n- `top = classTop × (0.94 + 0.012·speed)`;\n- `athr = 0.55·top × (0.80 + 0.04·thrust)`;\n- `steer = 1.9 rad/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`;\n- `grip = 5.5/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`;\n- `dmgMul = 1.35 − 0.06·shield`;\n- `mass = 0.8 + 0.05·shield`.\n\nAll of them are also multiplied by the Tune sliders.\n\n**The step** (1/120 s, in this order, for each craft in grid order):\n\n1. **Controls in.** From the human mapping (§3.9), the AI, the replay, the autopilot or the bot. Keyboard steering\n   ramps at 6/s toward ±1 so the keys feel analog. The stick passes straight through.\n2. **Yaw.** `yawTarget = steer·steerRate·(1 − 0.35·v/top) + (brakeR − brakeL)·airbrakeYaw` (with\n   `airbrakeYaw = 1.4 rad/s × (top/1440)^0.5`). `yawRate → yawTarget` at `steerResponse` (9/s). Rotate F about U by\n   `yawRate·dt`. While `stagger > 0` (a hit), steering is ignored and the craft wobbles ±0.4 rad/s.\n3. **Thrust and drag**, along F:\n   - `a = thrust·athr·boostK − cd·v² − coast − brakeDrag`;\n   - `cd = athr / top²` (so held thrust settles at `top`);\n   - while boosting, `top·boostMul` replaces `top` in `cd` and the thrust is ×1.8;\n   - `coast = 40 u/s²` when not thrusting;\n   - `brakeDrag = (brakeL + brakeR)/2 × airbrakeDrag × 0.35·top`;\n   - slope: add `−300 u/s² × F.z` (downhill speeds you up);\n   - pitch: nose-down cuts drag by 3 %·pitch.\n4. **Grip.** Split V into the along-F part and the lateral part `vl = dot(V, R)`. Then\n   `vl *= exp(−grip·(1 − 0.30·max(brakeL, brakeR))·dt)` (airbrakes let it slide). Scrub:\n   `|V| −= 0.12·|vl|·dt·60`. A side-shift press (cooldown 0.6 s, grounded) adds `±sideShiftSpeed` (700 u/s) to `vl`\n   and plays thruster puffs.\n5. **Hover / air.** Get the surface at the craft's `(s, u)`.\n   - **Grounded:** surface present and `h < captureH` (64 u).\n     - Spring along N: `aN = k·(Ht − h) − c·vN`, clamped to `[−magnetPull, +900]`, with `k = 220/s²`, `c = 28/s`,\n       `magnetPull = 1800 u/s²` and `Ht = H0 − 4·pitch + bob` (bob is `1.2·sin(2.2 t)`).\n     - Gravity is cancelled while grounded: the anti-gravity field is the source's fiction.\n     - The craft's up vector U slerps to N at 12/s.\n     - At crests the spring cannot pull hard enough, so `h` grows past `captureH` and the craft lifts off by itself.\n       Ramps launch the same way.\n   - **Airborne:** `a = −airGravity·(1 + 0.45·pitch)·Zup` (airGravity 640 u/s² = 40 m/s²). U slerps to the surface\n     normal below (if one is within 200 u) or else to Zup at 2/s. `airT += dt`.\n   - **Landing** (surface present, `h < H0 + 4`, `vN < 0`): impact angle `θ = atan(−vN / v)`.\n     - If `θ > 25°`: energy `−(θ − 25)·0.4·dmgMul`, speed `×(1 − min(0.35, (θ − 15°)/60°))`, and a hard-landing event\n       (shake, sparks, a \"THUD\").\n     - Otherwise a soft landing.\n     - Either way, resolve the barrel roll (step 7).\n   - **Bottoming out:** `h < 5 u` → `h = 5`, `vN = max(vN, 0)`, speed `×0.996` per step, a scrape event.\n6. **Integrate** `V += a·dt`, `P += V·dt`. Then `T.locate` → `s, u, h`.\n7. **Barrel roll.** Triggers only when airborne with `airT > 0.08 s`:\n   - a side-shift press, or\n   - a steer flick (steer crosses ≤ −0.7 then ≥ +0.7, or the reverse, and back, within 0.4 s; detected in\n     `01-input.js`).\n\n   The roll starts with `rollT = 0.45 s` toward rollDir and costs `rollCost` (10) energy. On landing:\n   - a finished roll → boost (`boostMul 1.2`, 1.2 s) + \"BARREL ROLL\" event;\n   - a roll still turning → \"BOTCHED\": speed ×0.75, energy −5, stagger 0.5 s.\n\n   The visual is a full 360° about F. Long jumps allow several rolls, each costing energy.\n8. **Walls** (deck/drop, wall present on that side). `lim = hw − 24 u`. If `|u| > lim`:\n   - push P back by `(|u| − lim)` along ∓R';\n   - normal speed `vn = dot(V, ±R')`; if `vn > 0`, then `V −= ±R'·vn·(1 + wallBounce)` with `wallBounce` 0.35;\n   - tangential scrub: `V −= F·min(v, wallFriction·vn)` with `wallFriction` 0.25;\n   - **yaw nudge:** rotate F toward the track tangent by `min(0.5, 0.6·vn/v)` rad (the craft never grinds nose-first);\n   - damage `wallDamage·clamp((vn − 150)/120, 0, 12)·dmgMul`;\n   - scraping (in contact with `vn ≤ 150`) costs 4 energy/s while `v > 500`;\n   - events `wall` / `scrape`.\n\n   **Open edges:** `|u| > hw + 2 m` with no wall means no surface. The craft falls, and a rescue follows (step 11).\n9. **Pads and pit** (in track space, grounded only):\n   - **Speed pad:** `boostT = min(2.0, max(boostT, padBoostTime))` (0.9 s), `boostMul = padBoost` (1.25). A pad\n     re-arms per craft after 0.5 s.\n   - **Weapon pad:** if no weapon is held, roll one (§3.4); event `pickup`.\n   - **Pit strip:** `energy += pitRecharge·dt` (25/s), a green shimmer FX and a recharge sound loop.\n10. **Energy.** Every damage source goes through `SN.Ship.damage(ship, amount, cause, by)`. It applies `dmgMul`.\n    `shieldT > 0` (bulwark) or god mode blocks it. Below 25 % a warning plays. At 0 the craft is eliminated (§3.3\n    decides between DNF and respawn).\n11. **Rescue.** Triggered by:\n    - a fall below the kill height (gap: `zLip − 40 m`; otherwise surface − 60 m);\n    - being off an open edge for 1 s;\n    - being stuck (`v < 50 u/s` for 3 s while thrusting, outside the countdown).\n\n    The rescue drone lifts the craft back on the centre line at `s_lastGood + 20 m` (the last grounded `s` with\n    `|u| < hw`), in 2.5 s with the craft frozen. Energy −10, speed 0, event `rescue`. In OVERCLOCK the rescue costs 20\n    energy.\n12. **Ship–ship collisions** (`27-collide.js`, after all craft move, pairs in index order): sphere pairs. The craft are\n    separated along the contact normal in inverse proportion to mass. Impulse\n    `j = −(1 + 0.3)·vn / (1/m1 + 1/m2)`. Damage `0.004·|vn|` each. A `bump` event fires above 120 u/s. Ghost craft\n    (hub, dev \"ghost AI\") skip this.\n13. **Launch boost** (countdown): holding thrust raises the revs at 0.6/s; releasing drops them at 0.8/s.\n    - At GO, revs in 0.72–0.88 → \"PERFECT START\" boost (1.0 s, ×1.25).\n    - Revs above 0.95 → \"STALL\" (no thrust for 0.5 s).\n    - The HUD shows a rev bar during the countdown.\n\n**Feel targets (checked by the physics tests; tune with the sliders until they hold):**\n- 0 → 90 % of top in 2.4–3.0 s.\n- Thrust-only top speed within ±2 % of `top`.\n- A 56 m hairpin at SPARK is takeable at 160–190 km/h with an airbrake, touching no wall.\n- Full-lock steering without airbrakes at top speed gives a drift angle of 12–20°.\n- Every jump in §4.3 behaves as App. C says, at each class's top speed (gap: clears at ≥ 75 m/s, falls short below\n  60 m/s).\n- At 3,000 u/s nothing tunnels through a wall or the surface.\n\n**Visual-only motion** (computed in `62-shipkit.js` from the state, never fed back):\n- roll = bank + `clamp(yawRate·0.28, ±0.5)` + barrel roll angle;\n- pitch = slope + `pitch·7°` + bob;\n- airbrake flaps open by `brake·60°`;\n- engine glow follows thrust;\n- the boost flame lengthens with `boostT`;\n- the shield shell flashes on a hit;\n- below 25 % energy, damage smoke and sparks.\n\n### 3.3 Race director and modes (`40-race.js`)","numLines":230,"startLine":354,"totalLines":2048}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SqkrJyc2sZQS4JhBXp84mi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
