{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh34Krt53a9cTwdLenQa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found a physics flaw in the review: lateral grip was uncapped, so a top-speed craft could turn at about 11 g, and the scrub term was roughly 30× too strong. I'm capping lateral grip at 40 m/s² × class, adding a slip-angle cap, and updating the related targets and sliders next.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9036,"cache_read_input_tokens":496340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9036},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"ca8f4385-2b33-4376-98b8-6e28cb7472cc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:41:33.448Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh34KZmhK1fbnDMQcJKh","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh34Krt53a9cTwdLenQa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QGAZPuiJrstJAbrRFLLnRZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nreps=[\n(\"\"\"- `grip = 5.5/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`;\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- `grip = 5.5/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)` (how fast the slide is caught);\n- `gripMax = 640 u/s² × (top/1440)^1.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`: the most lateral acceleration the hover field gives\n  (40 m/s² at SPARK). This cap is what makes speed, lines and airbrakes matter;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"4. **Grip.** Split V into the along-F part and the lateral part `vl = dot(V, R)`. Then\n   `vl *= exp(−grip·(1 − 0.30·max(brakeL, brakeR))·dt)` (airbrakes let it slide). Scrub:\n   `|V| −= 0.12·|vl|·dt·60`. A side-shift press (cooldown 0.6 s, grounded) adds `±sideShiftSpeed` (700 u/s) to `vl`\n   and plays thruster puffs.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"4. **Grip and slide.**\n   - Split V into the along-F part and the lateral part `vl = dot(V, R)`.\n   - The lateral grip available is `gmax = gripMax·(1 + 0.6·max(brakeL, brakeR))`: the airbrake flap works as a\n     rudder, which is why airbrakes are the cornering tool.\n   - Reduce `vl` toward 0 by `min(|vl|·(1 − e^(−grip·dt)), gmax·dt)`. A turn that needs more than `gmax` (`v²/R`)\n     slides outward.\n   - **Slip cap:** if the angle between F and V exceeds `slipMax` (35°), rotate F back to 35° from V. The craft\n     slides, never spins.\n   - **Scrub:** speed `−= 0.6/s·|vl|·dt`. Sliding costs speed.\n   - **Side-shift** (a press; grounded; cooldown 0.6 s): a separate lateral velocity `vShift = ±sideShiftSpeed`\n     (768 u/s) that decays at `shiftDecay` (12/s), outside the grip cap. That gives about 4 m of sideways jump in\n     0.3 s. Thruster puffs.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"- 0 → 90 % of top in 2.4–3.0 s.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- 0 → 90 % of top in 2.2–3.0 s (it depends on the THRUST stat: 2.68 s at THRUST 5 by the formula).\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"- A 56 m hairpin at SPARK is takeable at 160–190 km/h with an airbrake, touching no wall.\n- Full-lock steering without airbrakes at top speed gives a drift angle of 12–20°.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- Lateral grip caps out at `gripMax`. At SPARK top speed, full lock with no airbrake gives a path radius of\n  180–230 m, with the nose 15–35° inside the velocity. Holding the inside airbrake fully brings it to 110–150 m and\n  bleeds 6–12 m/s² of speed.\n- The 56 m Solenne lighthouse hairpin: about 185 km/h on the racing line without airbrakes, up to about 230 km/h\n  with the inside airbrake. It is taken without touching a wall by the AI at skill 1.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"   - both airbrakes if `v > vT·1.05`;\n   - the inside airbrake (by the sign of `e`) at `|e| > 0.12 rad`, scaled up to 1 at 0.4 rad;\"\"\",\n \"\"\"   - both airbrakes if `v > vT·1.05`;\n   - the inside airbrake (the side of the turn) at `clamp((v²·|κL| − gripMax) / (0.6·gripMax), 0, 1)`, which is\n     exactly the extra grip the corner needs, plus `clamp((|e| − 0.12)/0.28, 0, 1)` when the heading error is large;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  `alat_c = 640 u/s² × (top_c / 1440)^1.5 × skill` (40 m/s² at SPARK). Then a forward pass with\"\"\",\n \"\"\"  `alat_c = gripMax_c × 1.15 × skillK` (gripMax is 40 m/s² at SPARK, §3.2; ×1.15 for the airbrakes the AI uses).\n  Then a forward pass with\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"airbrakeYaw 1.4 [0–3], airbrakeDrag 0.9 [0–2], sideShiftSpeed 700 [0–1500].\"\"\",\n \"\"\"airbrakeYaw 1.4 [0–3], airbrakeDrag 0.9 [0–2], gripMaxMul 1 [0.4–2], slipMax 35° [10–60], sideShiftSpeed 768 [0–1500], shiftDecay 12 [4–30].\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    n=s.count(a)\n    assert n==1,(n,a[:90])\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ngrep -n \"side-shift lateral 3–5 m\" /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md | cut -c1-120","description":"Fix grip model, slip cap, side-shift, feel targets, AI and sliders"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9036,"cache_read_input_tokens":496340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9036},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"01bd0be0-7c6e-4be6-9ff7-3baf05f73e58","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:41:47.870Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh34KZmhK1fbnDMQcJKh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QGAZPuiJrstJAbrRFLLnRZ":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nreps=[\n(\"\"\"- `grip = 5.5/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`;\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- `grip = 5.5/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)` (how fast the slide is caught);\n- `gripMax = 640 u/s² × (top/1440)^1.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`: the most lateral acceleration the hover field gives\n  (40 m/s² at SPARK). This cap is what makes speed, lines and airbrakes matter;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"4. **Grip.** Split V into the along-F part and the lateral part `vl = dot(V, R)`. Then\n   `vl *= exp(−grip·(1 − 0.30·max(brakeL, brakeR))·dt)` (airbrakes let it slide). Scrub:\n   `|V| −= 0.12·|vl|·dt·60`. A side-shift press (cooldown 0.6 s, grounded) adds `±sideShiftSpeed` (700 u/s) to `vl`\n   and plays thruster puffs.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"4. **Grip and slide.**\n   - Split V into the along-F part and the lateral part `vl = dot(V, R)`.\n   - The lateral grip available is `gmax = gripMax·(1 + 0.6·max(brakeL, brakeR))`: the airbrake flap works as a\n     rudder, which is why airbrakes are the cornering tool.\n   - Reduce `vl` toward 0 by `min(|vl|·(1 − e^(−grip·dt)), gmax·dt)`. A turn that needs more than `gmax` (`v²/R`)\n     slides outward.\n   - **Slip cap:** if the angle between F and V exceeds `slipMax` (35°), rotate F back to 35° from V. The craft\n     slides, never spins.\n   - **Scrub:** speed `−= 0.6/s·|vl|·dt`. Sliding costs speed.\n   - **Side-shift** (a press; grounded; cooldown 0.6 s): a separate lateral velocity `vShift = ±sideShiftSpeed`\n     (768 u/s) that decays at `shiftDecay` (12/s), outside the grip cap. That gives about 4 m of sideways jump in\n     0.3 s. Thruster puffs.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"- 0 → 90 % of top in 2.4–3.0 s.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- 0 → 90 % of top in 2.2–3.0 s (it depends on the THRUST stat: 2.68 s at THRUST 5 by the formula).\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"- A 56 m hairpin at SPARK is takeable at 160–190 km/h with an airbrake, touching no wall.\n- Full-lock steering without airbrakes at top speed gives a drift angle of 12–20°.\"\"\",\n \"\"\"- Lateral grip caps out at `gripMax`. At SPARK top speed, full lock with no airbrake gives a path radius of\n  180–230 m, with the nose 15–35° inside the velocity. Holding the inside airbrake fully brings it to 110–150 m and\n  bleeds 6–12 m/s² of speed.\n- The 56 m Solenne lighthouse hairpin: about 185 km/h on the racing line without airbrakes, up to about 230 km/h\n  with the inside airbrake. It is taken without touching a wall by the AI at skill 1.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"   - both airbrakes if `v > vT·1.05`;\n   - the inside airbrake (by the sign of `e`) at `|e| > 0.12 rad`, scaled up to 1 at 0.4 rad;\"\"\",\n \"\"\"   - both airbrakes if `v > vT·1.05`;\n   - the inside airbrake (the side of the turn) at `clamp((v²·|κL| − gripMax) / (0.6·gripMax), 0, 1)`, which is\n     exactly the extra grip the corner needs, plus `clamp((|e| − 0.12)/0.28, 0, 1)` when the heading error is large;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  `alat_c = 640 u/s² × (top_c / 1440)^1.5 × skill` (40 m/s² at SPARK). Then a forward pass with\"\"\",\n \"\"\"  `alat_c = gripMax_c × 1.15 × skillK` (gripMax is 40 m/s² at SPARK, §3.2; ×1.15 for the airbrakes the AI uses).\n  Then a forward pass with\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"airbrakeYaw 1.4 [0–3], airbrakeDrag 0.9 [0–2], sideShiftSpeed 700 [0–1500].\"\"\",\n \"\"\"airbrakeYaw 1.4 [0–3], airbrakeDrag 0.9 [0–2], gripMaxMul 1 [0.4–2], slipMax 35° [10–60], sideShiftSpeed 768 [0–1500], shiftDecay 12 [4–30].\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    n=s.count(a)\n    assert n==1,(n,a[:90])\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ngrep -n \"side-shift lateral 3–5 m\" /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md | cut -c1-120","description":"Fix grip model, slip cap, side-shift, feel targets, AI and sliders"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01QGAZPuiJrstJAbrRFLLnRZ":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work"}}}
