{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3DQi5efFoKFsb2f141","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016NG43XzUaL6TiL1RWuBvUe","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","offset":600,"limit":150},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1785,"cache_read_input_tokens":517209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1785},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"313faca7-61de-4dd9-b78f-d15cf6845b6d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:42:44.400Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3DQSTciBAqbRBmHW6C","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016NG43XzUaL6TiL1RWuBvUe":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","offset":600,"limit":150}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016NG43XzUaL6TiL1RWuBvUe","type":"tool_result","content":"600\t- below 25 % energy, damage smoke and sparks.\n601\t\n602\t### 3.3 Race director and modes (`40-race.js`)\n603\t\n604\t**Lifecycle** (`race.state`):\n605\t\n606\t1. `intro`: a 6 s flyover by the TV director (§3.6). The track card shows name, place, length, laps, class. ✕, Enter\n607\t   or a click skips it.\n608\t2. `grid`: 1.5 s, a chase cam on the player.\n609\t3. `countdown`: 3 s with lights (3-2-1-GO) on the start gantry and the HUD, the launch revs and the announcer.\n610\t4. `racing`.\n611\t5. `finished`: the player crossed the line, or was eliminated.\n612\t   - The player becomes a ghost-cam spectator (TV director) while the others finish.\n613\t   - After 8 s, or when every craft is done, unfinished craft get an estimated time\n614\t     (`t + (remaining distance / their average speed)`) and the results are sealed.\n615\t6. `results`: go to the `results` scene.\n616\t\n617\t**Laps and sectors.** A lap counts when the craft crosses `s = 0` forward after passing sectors 1…7 in order. Lap\n618\ttime, best lap and the final lap's announcer/music layer come from it. **Wrong way:** `dot(F, trackF) < −0.2` and\n619\t`v > 300 u/s` for 1.2 s → a HUD warning plus an announcer line.\n620\t\n621\t**Positions:** sorted by `finished` time, then by progress `p`, descending. The order is recomputed every step, with\n622\ta \"position changed\" event for the HUD arrows.\n623\t\n624\t**Elimination:** at energy 0 the craft explodes. In RACE/SEASON it is **DNF** (results show \"ELIMINATED\"). In\n625\tSNIPEOUT, ACADEMY and hub sessions it **respawns** 3 s later at its own `s` on the centre line, with 100 % energy and\n626\t2 s of invulnerability (blinking).\n627\t\n628\t**Modes (`rules` objects, one file section each):**\n629\t\n630\t| Mode | Field | Weapons | Rules / win | Medals |\n631\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n632\t| QUICK RACE | 8 craft (player + 7 AI) | on | laps 1–5 (default 3); place = result | gold 1st, silver 2nd, bronze 3rd |\n633\t| TIME TRIAL | solo | off (pads dark) | 3 laps; ghost of your best run (§3.13) | per track/class times (§4.3), calibrated |\n634\t| HOT LAP | solo, flying start (spawn 300 m before the line at 80 % top) | off | unlimited laps; the best lap counts; End run in the pause menu (or 10 laps) | per track/class lap times |\n635\t| SNIPEOUT | 8 craft | on, offensive-weighted table, no AUTOPILOT | +1 per hit landed, +3 per elimination, +1 bonus for a RAILSHOT elimination (\"SNIPED\"); respawns; first to target (10 or 12) or most after 5 min | 1st/2nd/3rd |\n636\t| OVERCLOCK | solo, neon skin | off; speed pads off | automatic thrust; zone n every 12 s: `top = SPARK·(0.75 + 0.06·n)`; walls ×1.5 damage; +5 energy per zone cleared; ends at 0 energy | bronze zone 10, silver 20, gold 30, \"OVERCLOCKED\" 40 |\n637\t| ACADEMY | solo (+ drones) | scripted | 11 drills (§4.5), each retried until passed | gold when every drill passed first time |\n638\t| VERSUS | 2 humans + 6 AI, split screen | on | race or snipeout, as above | per player |\n639\t| SEASON event | as its mode | as its mode | the event's target | the event's medal rule |\n640\t| GRAND PRIX | 8 craft × 4 races | on | points 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1; DNF 0; ties by best finish | champion = gold, 2nd = silver, 3rd = bronze |\n641\t| HUB SESSION | each copy: own craft + 7 AI; other humans as ghosts | on | 3 laps FLARE on a seeded track; elimination respawns; `AIHub.result({ time })` | the hub's standings |\n642\t\n643\t**Results data** (`race.results()`): place, pilot, team, time or gap, best lap, points (GP/SNIPEOUT), DNF, medal for\n644\tthe player, new records, and unlocks triggered (season).\n645\t\n646\t### 3.4 Weapons and pickups (`30-weapons.js`, `06-data-weapons.js`)\n647\t\n648\tProjectiles live in **track space**: `s, u, h` and `vs, vu`. They follow the track through curves, the way the\n649\tsource's weapons hug it. Each step they advance and wrap with `s`. They hit a craft when `|Δs| < 40 u`, `|Δu| < 34 u`\n650\tand `|Δh| < 40 u`. They hit a wall at `|u| > hw` (they explode). In gaps they fly straight on and expire. Every hit\n651\tgoes through `SN.Ship.damage` and emits `hit`. The 3D FX are in `68-fx.js`.\n652\t\n653\t| Weapon (icon colour) | Fire | Behaviour | Damage / effect | Absorb |\n654\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n655\t| **SWARM** (red) | tap | 3 rockets, lateral spread −1.5/0/+1.5 m growing at 120 u/s, speed `v_ship + 2400`, life 1.4 s | 10 each, jolt (speed ×0.9, stagger 0.2 s) | +16 |\n656\t| **SEEKER** (orange) | lock: hold the target ahead in a 25° cone within 3000 u for 0.6 s (\"LOCKED\" tone), then press | homing missile, speed `v + 2000`, steers u toward the target at 900 u/s, `s` speed matched to catch up; unlocked it flies straight | 24, spin-out stagger 0.5 s | +22 |\n657\t| **MINEFIELD** (magenta) | tap | drops 5 mines behind at 0.12 s intervals (`u` at drop, `s − 60 u`); armed after 0.3 s; live 30 s; trigger radius 40 u | 12 each, jolt | +18 |\n658\t| **CANNON** (yellow) | hold | 24 bolts at 12/s, speed `v + 4200`, ±0.5 m jitter, aim assist toward a target within ±1.5 m | 2.5 per bolt | +14 |\n659\t| **RAILSHOT** (white/cyan): the *snipe* | hold to charge 0.8 s (ring on the HUD), release to fire | hitscan along the track ahead to 4000 u. It hits the first craft within ±32 u of the aim line `u_aim(Δs) = u + Δs·tan(heading vs track)` (aim assist: ±16 u extra if charged fully). A beam is drawn in 3D | 34, big jolt; an elimination by RAILSHOT is a \"SNIPED!\" | +28 |\n660\t| **TREMOR** (green) | tap | a wave rolls forward along the surface from the user, full width, at `v + 1800` for 1.3 s. It hits each **grounded** craft it passes (airborne craft dodge it) | 26, pops the craft up 3 m, stagger 0.4 s | +30 |\n661\t| **BULWARK** (blue) | tap | invulnerable for 4 s (walls too); no pickups meanwhile | blocks everything | +12 |\n662\t| **AUTOPILOT** (teal) | tap | the AI drives for 5 s (skill 1.0); the HUD counts it down; ends early after a rescue | — | +10 |\n663\t| **NITRO** (amber) | tap | boost 2.2 s, `boostMul 1.35`, thrust ×2 | — | +10 |\n664\t| **SIPHON** (lime) | hold to aim, auto | beam to the nearest craft ahead within 1500 u (line of sight along the track) for 3 s; breaks beyond 1900 u | drains 9/s from the target into you | +20 |\n665\t\n666\t- **Absorb** (○ / Shift / right click): consumes the weapon and adds its absorb value. Hub: `absorbMul`.\n667\t- **One weapon at a time.** A pad gives nothing while a weapon is held, or while BULWARK or AUTOPILOT runs.\n668\t- **Pickup roll:** weighted by position. Pick the table by `pos ∈ {1,2}` front, `{3..5}` mid, `{6..8}` back, then\n669\t  apply `pickupLuck` (0 = uniform, 1 = table, 2 = table squared).\n670\t\n671\t  | | SWARM | SEEKER | MINE | CANNON | RAIL | TREMOR | BULWARK | AUTO | NITRO | SIPHON |\n672\t  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n673\t  | front | 2 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 3 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n674\t  | mid | 3 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 |\n675\t  | back | 2 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 1 | 3 | 3 | 2 |\n676\t  | snipeout | 3 | 3 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n677\t\n678\t  The HUD plays a 0.5 s slot-machine spin, then the announcer says the name. Rolls use `race.rng('pickup')`.\n679\t- **Warnings for the target:** a seeker lock beeps at the target and shows \"LOCK\" with an arrow at the bottom centre.\n680\t  A railshot charging aimed at you shows a thin red line.\n681\t\n682\t### 3.5 AI pilots (`35-ai.js`)\n683\t\n684\tEach AI craft produces `ShipControls` every step from the track's line and speed arrays and the race state. The same\n685\tfunction drives AUTOPILOT, the attract mode, the player bot in tests, and the medal calibration.\n686\t\n687\t1. **Look-ahead target.** `sL = s + 0.55 s·v + 300 u`. Target point `Q = C(sL) + R'(sL)·uTarget(sL)`.\n688\t   - `uTarget` = racing line `T.line` + avoidance offset + pad bias + pit bias.\n689\t   - Heading error `e` = the signed angle from F to `(Q − P)` projected on the surface plane.\n690\t   - `steer = clamp(2.2·e + 0.25·ė, −1, 1)`, plus seeded noise ±(0.05·(1 − skill)).\n691\t2. **Speed.** `vT = T.vline(s + 0.4·v)·skillK` (skillK = 0.86 + 0.14·skill, also scaling `alat`).\n692\t   - thrust if `v < vT·1.01`;\n693\t   - both airbrakes if `v > vT·1.05`;\n694\t   - the inside airbrake (the side of the turn) at `clamp((v²·|κL| − gripMax) / (0.6·gripMax), 0, 1)`, which is\n695\t     exactly the extra grip the corner needs, plus `clamp((|e| − 0.12)/0.28, 0, 1)` when the heading error is large;\n696\t   - pitch: nose-down on descents steeper than 4 %, nose-up on crests (vertical curvature) and over gaps when short of\n697\t     the landing.\n698\t3. **Avoidance and overtaking.** A craft ahead within 900 u with `|Δu| < 70 u` and closing → shift `uTarget` by\n699\t   ±110 u toward the wider side (blend 0.6 s). It returns to the line after passing. Mines seen ahead (within 1200 u)\n700\t   push `uTarget` away by 80 u. A side-shift dodges incoming weapons when skill > 0.7 (reaction 0.25 s).\n701\t4. **Pads.** A speed pad within 1500 u ahead and within 120 u of the line → bias `uTarget` onto it (skill-weighted).\n702\t   Weapon pads likewise when unarmed. Pit: if energy < 30 % and the pit is ahead within 2500 u → the pit line.\n703\t5. **Weapons (per weapon):**\n704\t   - SWARM, CANNON: a target ahead within 1800 u and `|Δu| < 60 u`.\n705\t   - SEEKER: fire when locked.\n706\t   - RAILSHOT: charge when a target is within 3500 u and `|Δu_aim| < 40 u`; release at full charge.\n707\t   - MINEFIELD: a craft behind within 1200 u, or simply in the last 30 % of a lap when leading.\n708\t   - TREMOR: ≥ 2 craft within 2500 u ahead.\n709\t   - BULWARK: a lock warning, or energy < 35 % in traffic.\n710\t   - AUTOPILOT: in a technical section (`|κ|` high) or with energy < 40 %.\n711\t   - NITRO: on a straight (`|κL| < 1/600 m` for the next 400 m).\n712\t   - SIPHON: a target ahead within 1400 u and own energy < 85.\n713\t   - Absorb instead when energy < 30 % and the weapon is defensive or useless at that moment.\n714\t   - Each pilot's `aggression` (0.4–1.3) scales reaction thresholds and hold times.\n715\t6. **Jumps.** Hold `v ≥ vJump` on gap approaches. Barrel roll when the predicted airtime is > 0.6 s, energy > 50 %\n716\t   and skill > 0.6, at chance `0.5·aggression` (attract: always).\n717\t7. **Mistakes.** For each corner (κ peak), a chance `(1 − skill)·0.15` to brake late by 0.25 s (it may scrape a wall).\n718\t8. **Rubber band** (Quick Race, Season, Versus; never Time Trial/Hot Lap/Overclock):\n719\t   `top ×= 1 + rb·clamp((p_player − p_ai)/32000, −1, 1)·0.04`, with rb from the difficulty (Easy 1.5, Normal 1.0,\n720\t   Hard 0.3) times the `aiRubberBand` slider.\n721\t9. **Difficulty** (Settings → Difficulty):\n722\t\n723\t   | | AI skill | aggression | rubber band |\n724\t   | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n725\t   | Easy | 0.86 | ×0.6 | 1.5 |\n726\t   | Normal | 0.93 | ×1.0 | 1.0 |\n727\t   | Hard | 0.99 | ×1.3 | 0.3 |\n728\t\n729\t   Each pilot has an offset (§4.1). NULL//SET pilots get +0.02.\n730\t10. **Attract cheats.** The AI may cheat freely in attract (TASK.md): infinite energy, pickups forced in rotation so\n731\t    all 10 weapons appear, a barrel roll on every jump, aggression 1.5.\n732\t\n733\t### 3.6 Cameras and the TV director (`60-render.js`)\n734\t\n735\tThe World3D camera runs in **`'fixed'`** mode. We compute a pose `{ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }` (engine units,\n736\tradians; `pitch < 0` looks down) every step into `camera.fixed`. In `onDraw` we **interpolate** between the last two\n737\tstep poses with `game.alpha` and write `world.camera.pose` (the header allows \"a last touch to camera.pose\"). Craft\n738\tmeshes are interpolated the same way (`prev` → current). Set `camera.target = { x, y, z }` to the player craft so the\n739\tsun's shadow box follows it.\n740\t\n741\t| Camera | Pose |\n742\t| --- | --- |\n743\t| **Chase** (default) | eye = `P − Fs·d + Us·hgt`, where `d = camDistance·(1 + 0.15·v/top)` (150 u) and `hgt = camHeight` (46 u). Look at `P + F·120 + U·12`. `Fs`, `Us` are F and U smoothed by slerp at `camLag` (8/s), so the camera swings, never cuts corners. `Us` blends from Zup toward the craft's U at 0.6, so the horizon tilts with the banks. `fov = camFov + camFovBoost·(v/top)²` (72° + 16°) + 6° while boosting. Shake from `game.shake` (impacts, rail hits, landings) |\n744\t| **Far chase** | d ×1.5, hgt ×1.6, fov −6° |\n745\t| **Cockpit** | eye = `P + F·20 + U·14`, look along F, full craft roll, fov 84° + boost. The craft mesh is hidden except a nose/canopy-rim \"dash\" mesh |\n746\t| **Look back** (held) | the chase eye mirrored in front of the craft looking back (`P + F·d + Us·hgt` → P) |\n747\t| **Free fly** (dev) | WASD/stick fly, Q/E or triggers up/down, mouse/right stick turn |\n748\t| **Podium / hangar orbit** | an orbit around a point (menus, results podium) |\n749\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"cfee4652-b91f-4d48-85eb-766422d4df89","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:42:44.407Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"- below 25 % energy, damage smoke and sparks.\n\n### 3.3 Race director and modes (`40-race.js`)\n\n**Lifecycle** (`race.state`):\n\n1. `intro`: a 6 s flyover by the TV director (§3.6). The track card shows name, place, length, laps, class. ✕, Enter\n   or a click skips it.\n2. `grid`: 1.5 s, a chase cam on the player.\n3. `countdown`: 3 s with lights (3-2-1-GO) on the start gantry and the HUD, the launch revs and the announcer.\n4. `racing`.\n5. `finished`: the player crossed the line, or was eliminated.\n   - The player becomes a ghost-cam spectator (TV director) while the others finish.\n   - After 8 s, or when every craft is done, unfinished craft get an estimated time\n     (`t + (remaining distance / their average speed)`) and the results are sealed.\n6. `results`: go to the `results` scene.\n\n**Laps and sectors.** A lap counts when the craft crosses `s = 0` forward after passing sectors 1…7 in order. Lap\ntime, best lap and the final lap's announcer/music layer come from it. **Wrong way:** `dot(F, trackF) < −0.2` and\n`v > 300 u/s` for 1.2 s → a HUD warning plus an announcer line.\n\n**Positions:** sorted by `finished` time, then by progress `p`, descending. The order is recomputed every step, with\na \"position changed\" event for the HUD arrows.\n\n**Elimination:** at energy 0 the craft explodes. In RACE/SEASON it is **DNF** (results show \"ELIMINATED\"). In\nSNIPEOUT, ACADEMY and hub sessions it **respawns** 3 s later at its own `s` on the centre line, with 100 % energy and\n2 s of invulnerability (blinking).\n\n**Modes (`rules` objects, one file section each):**\n\n| Mode | Field | Weapons | Rules / win | Medals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| QUICK RACE | 8 craft (player + 7 AI) | on | laps 1–5 (default 3); place = result | gold 1st, silver 2nd, bronze 3rd |\n| TIME TRIAL | solo | off (pads dark) | 3 laps; ghost of your best run (§3.13) | per track/class times (§4.3), calibrated |\n| HOT LAP | solo, flying start (spawn 300 m before the line at 80 % top) | off | unlimited laps; the best lap counts; End run in the pause menu (or 10 laps) | per track/class lap times |\n| SNIPEOUT | 8 craft | on, offensive-weighted table, no AUTOPILOT | +1 per hit landed, +3 per elimination, +1 bonus for a RAILSHOT elimination (\"SNIPED\"); respawns; first to target (10 or 12) or most after 5 min | 1st/2nd/3rd |\n| OVERCLOCK | solo, neon skin | off; speed pads off | automatic thrust; zone n every 12 s: `top = SPARK·(0.75 + 0.06·n)`; walls ×1.5 damage; +5 energy per zone cleared; ends at 0 energy | bronze zone 10, silver 20, gold 30, \"OVERCLOCKED\" 40 |\n| ACADEMY | solo (+ drones) | scripted | 11 drills (§4.5), each retried until passed | gold when every drill passed first time |\n| VERSUS | 2 humans + 6 AI, split screen | on | race or snipeout, as above | per player |\n| SEASON event | as its mode | as its mode | the event's target | the event's medal rule |\n| GRAND PRIX | 8 craft × 4 races | on | points 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1; DNF 0; ties by best finish | champion = gold, 2nd = silver, 3rd = bronze |\n| HUB SESSION | each copy: own craft + 7 AI; other humans as ghosts | on | 3 laps FLARE on a seeded track; elimination respawns; `AIHub.result({ time })` | the hub's standings |\n\n**Results data** (`race.results()`): place, pilot, team, time or gap, best lap, points (GP/SNIPEOUT), DNF, medal for\nthe player, new records, and unlocks triggered (season).\n\n### 3.4 Weapons and pickups (`30-weapons.js`, `06-data-weapons.js`)\n\nProjectiles live in **track space**: `s, u, h` and `vs, vu`. They follow the track through curves, the way the\nsource's weapons hug it. Each step they advance and wrap with `s`. They hit a craft when `|Δs| < 40 u`, `|Δu| < 34 u`\nand `|Δh| < 40 u`. They hit a wall at `|u| > hw` (they explode). In gaps they fly straight on and expire. Every hit\ngoes through `SN.Ship.damage` and emits `hit`. The 3D FX are in `68-fx.js`.\n\n| Weapon (icon colour) | Fire | Behaviour | Damage / effect | Absorb |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **SWARM** (red) | tap | 3 rockets, lateral spread −1.5/0/+1.5 m growing at 120 u/s, speed `v_ship + 2400`, life 1.4 s | 10 each, jolt (speed ×0.9, stagger 0.2 s) | +16 |\n| **SEEKER** (orange) | lock: hold the target ahead in a 25° cone within 3000 u for 0.6 s (\"LOCKED\" tone), then press | homing missile, speed `v + 2000`, steers u toward the target at 900 u/s, `s` speed matched to catch up; unlocked it flies straight | 24, spin-out stagger 0.5 s | +22 |\n| **MINEFIELD** (magenta) | tap | drops 5 mines behind at 0.12 s intervals (`u` at drop, `s − 60 u`); armed after 0.3 s; live 30 s; trigger radius 40 u | 12 each, jolt | +18 |\n| **CANNON** (yellow) | hold | 24 bolts at 12/s, speed `v + 4200`, ±0.5 m jitter, aim assist toward a target within ±1.5 m | 2.5 per bolt | +14 |\n| **RAILSHOT** (white/cyan): the *snipe* | hold to charge 0.8 s (ring on the HUD), release to fire | hitscan along the track ahead to 4000 u. It hits the first craft within ±32 u of the aim line `u_aim(Δs) = u + Δs·tan(heading vs track)` (aim assist: ±16 u extra if charged fully). A beam is drawn in 3D | 34, big jolt; an elimination by RAILSHOT is a \"SNIPED!\" | +28 |\n| **TREMOR** (green) | tap | a wave rolls forward along the surface from the user, full width, at `v + 1800` for 1.3 s. It hits each **grounded** craft it passes (airborne craft dodge it) | 26, pops the craft up 3 m, stagger 0.4 s | +30 |\n| **BULWARK** (blue) | tap | invulnerable for 4 s (walls too); no pickups meanwhile | blocks everything | +12 |\n| **AUTOPILOT** (teal) | tap | the AI drives for 5 s (skill 1.0); the HUD counts it down; ends early after a rescue | — | +10 |\n| **NITRO** (amber) | tap | boost 2.2 s, `boostMul 1.35`, thrust ×2 | — | +10 |\n| **SIPHON** (lime) | hold to aim, auto | beam to the nearest craft ahead within 1500 u (line of sight along the track) for 3 s; breaks beyond 1900 u | drains 9/s from the target into you | +20 |\n\n- **Absorb** (○ / Shift / right click): consumes the weapon and adds its absorb value. Hub: `absorbMul`.\n- **One weapon at a time.** A pad gives nothing while a weapon is held, or while BULWARK or AUTOPILOT runs.\n- **Pickup roll:** weighted by position. Pick the table by `pos ∈ {1,2}` front, `{3..5}` mid, `{6..8}` back, then\n  apply `pickupLuck` (0 = uniform, 1 = table, 2 = table squared).\n\n  | | SWARM | SEEKER | MINE | CANNON | RAIL | TREMOR | BULWARK | AUTO | NITRO | SIPHON |\n  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n  | front | 2 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 3 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n  | mid | 3 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 |\n  | back | 2 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 1 | 3 | 3 | 2 |\n  | snipeout | 3 | 3 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n\n  The HUD plays a 0.5 s slot-machine spin, then the announcer says the name. Rolls use `race.rng('pickup')`.\n- **Warnings for the target:** a seeker lock beeps at the target and shows \"LOCK\" with an arrow at the bottom centre.\n  A railshot charging aimed at you shows a thin red line.\n\n### 3.5 AI pilots (`35-ai.js`)\n\nEach AI craft produces `ShipControls` every step from the track's line and speed arrays and the race state. The same\nfunction drives AUTOPILOT, the attract mode, the player bot in tests, and the medal calibration.\n\n1. **Look-ahead target.** `sL = s + 0.55 s·v + 300 u`. Target point `Q = C(sL) + R'(sL)·uTarget(sL)`.\n   - `uTarget` = racing line `T.line` + avoidance offset + pad bias + pit bias.\n   - Heading error `e` = the signed angle from F to `(Q − P)` projected on the surface plane.\n   - `steer = clamp(2.2·e + 0.25·ė, −1, 1)`, plus seeded noise ±(0.05·(1 − skill)).\n2. **Speed.** `vT = T.vline(s + 0.4·v)·skillK` (skillK = 0.86 + 0.14·skill, also scaling `alat`).\n   - thrust if `v < vT·1.01`;\n   - both airbrakes if `v > vT·1.05`;\n   - the inside airbrake (the side of the turn) at `clamp((v²·|κL| − gripMax) / (0.6·gripMax), 0, 1)`, which is\n     exactly the extra grip the corner needs, plus `clamp((|e| − 0.12)/0.28, 0, 1)` when the heading error is large;\n   - pitch: nose-down on descents steeper than 4 %, nose-up on crests (vertical curvature) and over gaps when short of\n     the landing.\n3. **Avoidance and overtaking.** A craft ahead within 900 u with `|Δu| < 70 u` and closing → shift `uTarget` by\n   ±110 u toward the wider side (blend 0.6 s). It returns to the line after passing. Mines seen ahead (within 1200 u)\n   push `uTarget` away by 80 u. A side-shift dodges incoming weapons when skill > 0.7 (reaction 0.25 s).\n4. **Pads.** A speed pad within 1500 u ahead and within 120 u of the line → bias `uTarget` onto it (skill-weighted).\n   Weapon pads likewise when unarmed. Pit: if energy < 30 % and the pit is ahead within 2500 u → the pit line.\n5. **Weapons (per weapon):**\n   - SWARM, CANNON: a target ahead within 1800 u and `|Δu| < 60 u`.\n   - SEEKER: fire when locked.\n   - RAILSHOT: charge when a target is within 3500 u and `|Δu_aim| < 40 u`; release at full charge.\n   - MINEFIELD: a craft behind within 1200 u, or simply in the last 30 % of a lap when leading.\n   - TREMOR: ≥ 2 craft within 2500 u ahead.\n   - BULWARK: a lock warning, or energy < 35 % in traffic.\n   - AUTOPILOT: in a technical section (`|κ|` high) or with energy < 40 %.\n   - NITRO: on a straight (`|κL| < 1/600 m` for the next 400 m).\n   - SIPHON: a target ahead within 1400 u and own energy < 85.\n   - Absorb instead when energy < 30 % and the weapon is defensive or useless at that moment.\n   - Each pilot's `aggression` (0.4–1.3) scales reaction thresholds and hold times.\n6. **Jumps.** Hold `v ≥ vJump` on gap approaches. Barrel roll when the predicted airtime is > 0.6 s, energy > 50 %\n   and skill > 0.6, at chance `0.5·aggression` (attract: always).\n7. **Mistakes.** For each corner (κ peak), a chance `(1 − skill)·0.15` to brake late by 0.25 s (it may scrape a wall).\n8. **Rubber band** (Quick Race, Season, Versus; never Time Trial/Hot Lap/Overclock):\n   `top ×= 1 + rb·clamp((p_player − p_ai)/32000, −1, 1)·0.04`, with rb from the difficulty (Easy 1.5, Normal 1.0,\n   Hard 0.3) times the `aiRubberBand` slider.\n9. **Difficulty** (Settings → Difficulty):\n\n   | | AI skill | aggression | rubber band |\n   | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n   | Easy | 0.86 | ×0.6 | 1.5 |\n   | Normal | 0.93 | ×1.0 | 1.0 |\n   | Hard | 0.99 | ×1.3 | 0.3 |\n\n   Each pilot has an offset (§4.1). NULL//SET pilots get +0.02.\n10. **Attract cheats.** The AI may cheat freely in attract (TASK.md): infinite energy, pickups forced in rotation so\n    all 10 weapons appear, a barrel roll on every jump, aggression 1.5.\n\n### 3.6 Cameras and the TV director (`60-render.js`)\n\nThe World3D camera runs in **`'fixed'`** mode. We compute a pose `{ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }` (engine units,\nradians; `pitch < 0` looks down) every step into `camera.fixed`. In `onDraw` we **interpolate** between the last two\nstep poses with `game.alpha` and write `world.camera.pose` (the header allows \"a last touch to camera.pose\"). Craft\nmeshes are interpolated the same way (`prev` → current). Set `camera.target = { x, y, z }` to the player craft so the\nsun's shadow box follows it.\n\n| Camera | Pose |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Chase** (default) | eye = `P − Fs·d + Us·hgt`, where `d = camDistance·(1 + 0.15·v/top)` (150 u) and `hgt = camHeight` (46 u). Look at `P + F·120 + U·12`. `Fs`, `Us` are F and U smoothed by slerp at `camLag` (8/s), so the camera swings, never cuts corners. `Us` blends from Zup toward the craft's U at 0.6, so the horizon tilts with the banks. `fov = camFov + camFovBoost·(v/top)²` (72° + 16°) + 6° while boosting. Shake from `game.shake` (impacts, rail hits, landings) |\n| **Far chase** | d ×1.5, hgt ×1.6, fov −6° |\n| **Cockpit** | eye = `P + F·20 + U·14`, look along F, full craft roll, fov 84° + boost. The craft mesh is hidden except a nose/canopy-rim \"dash\" mesh |\n| **Look back** (held) | the chase eye mirrored in front of the craft looking back (`P + F·d + Us·hgt` → P) |\n| **Free fly** (dev) | WASD/stick fly, Q/E or triggers up/down, mouse/right stick turn |\n| **Podium / hangar orbit** | an orbit around a point (menus, results podium) |\n","numLines":150,"startLine":600,"totalLines":2068}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016NG43XzUaL6TiL1RWuBvUe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
