{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VtWFSPYuhMSemm24iXmUfn","type":"tool_result","content":"750\tRoll sign: verify with a screenshot on Karakum's spiral, a right-hand banked turn. The horizon must tilt the way the\n751\ttrack does. If it is inverted, negate the roll in one place (`SN.cam.rollSign`).\n752\t\n753\t**TV director** (intro flyover, attract, replay, spectating, podium intro):\n754\t- **Camera spots** are built at load every ~200 m. Each is `C(s) + R'·side·(hw + 15…30 m) + Zup·(6…20 m)`, on the\n755\t  outside of curves, alternating sides on straights. Skip a spot if the terrain (`world.ground`) is above it, or if it\n756\t  is inside another track section (`T.query`). Tunnel spots go 2 m under the ceiling, 4 m from the wall. Overpass\n757\t  spots look up from the lower deck. Each spot stores `s`.\n758\t- **Shots:**\n759\t  - `trackside`: fixed eye, looking at the target, with the FOV narrowing (40→20°) as the target nears;\n760\t  - `heli`: 40 m up, 60 m back, following;\n761\t  - `chase`;\n762\t  - `nose`;\n763\t  - `low`: 1 m above the surface ahead, looking back at the target;\n764\t  - `flyby`: along the line 30 m ahead of the target, looking back.\n765\t- **Logic:**\n766\t  - target = the player (spectate/replay) or the most interesting craft (attract: leader, a close fight within 300 u,\n767\t    a weapon fired in the last 2 s, a jump);\n768\t  - pick the spot 150–900 u ahead of the target with a clear line (raycast against the track only), hold 2.5–6 s, and\n769\t    cut when the target passes the spot by 400 u;\n770\t  - every third cut is heli, chase, nose or low;\n771\t  - events cut early: an elimination, a railshot or a jump launch;\n772\t  - never cut twice within 1.2 s.\n773\t- **Intro flyover:** 6 s along the line from `s = −900 m` to the grid at 2.5× the target speed, then a 1 s whip onto\n774\t  the grid.\n775\t\n776\t### 3.7 Rendering (`60-render.js`, `62-shipkit.js`, `64-trackmesh.js`, `66-scenery.js`, `68-fx.js`)\n777\t\n778\t**Worlds.** `World3D.init(game)` runs once (boot). Then:\n779\t- **Hangar world**, made at boot. A small `level` (text rows):\n780\t  - a 24 × 16 tile hall: floor `{ floor: 0 }`, a turntable `{ mark: 'turntable' }` and a podium of three raised floors\n781\t    (`{ floor: 24 }` 1st, `{ floor: 16 }` 2nd, `{ floor: 8 }` 3rd, marks `p1 p2 p3`);\n782\t  - `torch: false`, our own lights: 3 coloured spots plus team-coloured neon strips (our meshes);\n783\t  - camera `'fixed'`, `fog: false`.\n784\t\n785\t  It is used by the menus, team select (the craft on the turntable), results/podium (pilots as rig **cards** via\n786\t  `world.hero({ rig })` posed `cheer` / `wave` / `hips`) and the ending.\n787\t- **Track world**, one per track, made by the `loading` scene. At most one is alive besides the hangar: dispose the\n788\t  previous with `world.dispose()`. Boot makes PORT SOLENNE's, so the title and attract start at once.\n789\t\n790\t```js\n791\tnew E.World3D(game, {\n792\t  terrain: { size: 65536 /* 4 km */, height: theme.height, color: theme.color, far: 26000, cell: 64, rock: theme.rock, bottom: -3000 },\n793\t  sky: theme.sky, fog: theme.fog, ambient: theme.ambient, sun: Object.assign({ shadow: true, area: 900 }, theme.sun),\n794\t  torchLights: 0, lights: 4, glowLights: 8, shadows: game.settings.shadows3d !== false,\n795\t  filter: { look: game.settings.filter3d || 'clean', bloom: game.settings.bloom !== false },\n796\t  camera: { mode: 'fixed', far: 26000, near: 4 }, particleGround: (x, y, z) => track.groundBelow(x, y, z),\n797\t  onDraw: (w, r) => SN.render.onDraw(w, r)\n798\t});\n799\t```\n800\t\n801\t**Terrain carving.** `theme.height(x, y)` = the theme's natural height, combined with a **corridor grid** (cell 16 m,\n802\tbuilt from the slices at load):\n803\t- near the track: `min(natural, deckZ − clearance(d))`, where `clearance` grows from 3 m at the edge to 0 at 60 m, so\n804\t  the ground falls away under elevated decks and meets the track at grade;\n805\t- under tunnel slices: `max(natural, ceilZ + 4 m)`, so the rock covers the tunnel;\n806\t- portal frames hide the seams.\n807\t\n808\tKeep `height()` fast: it is a few grid lookups and noise (`E.noise2`).\n809\t\n810\t**Materials** (make them all when the world is made, never mid-race):\n811\t- `MeshLambertNodeMaterial({ vertexColors: true })` for the track surface, walls and scenery;\n812\t- `MeshBasicNodeMaterial` for emissive neon, pads, engine glow and beams. They are bright, so the bloom catches them.\n813\t  Set `fog: false` on the overclock skin;\n814\t- `MeshToonNodeMaterial` for the craft hulls;\n815\t- transparent additive materials for the shield shells, ghosts and beams.\n816\t\n817\tTextures are canvases drawn pixel by pixel at 64–256 px (`NearestFilter`, the engine's native crisp look): track\n818\tpanels, lane dashes, chevrons, sponsor boards, team logos, window grids. **Pads and painted markings** use\n819\t`polygonOffset` (factor −2, units −2) and sit 1 u above the surface. That avoids z-fighting at distance.\n820\t\n821\t**Track meshes** (`64-trackmesh.js`), built in chunks of 40 slices (80 m) for frustum culling:\n822\t- **Surface:** 6 lateral strips. Vertex colours: dark graphite panels `#22252c`/`#2a2e36` alternating every 8 m,\n823\t  bright edge lines, centre dashes, a tint per theme. The grid boxes and the start/finish chequer are painted near\n824\t  `s = 0`.\n825\t- **Walls:** 1.6 m barrier panels with a glowing top strip in the theme's neon (`#29c8e8` coast, `#ffb347` desert,\n826\t  `#ff3ab4` city, `#7af0ff` arctic). On the outside of curves, **directional chevrons** (emissive arrows pointing the\n827\t  way of the turn) every 6 m. Open edges have no wall but a dashed hazard line on the edge.\n828\t- **Underside and supports:**\n829\t  - the deck's underside and thickness (1.2 m), so the deck reads as a bridge;\n830\t  - pylons every 40 m where the deck is more than 4 m above the terrain, at the deck edges; skipped where they would\n831\t    stand in another section's driving envelope;\n832\t  - overpass decks get piers outside the lower deck's walls.\n833\t- **Tunnels:** a 10-segment arch to 12 m, ribs every 12 m, emissive light strips along both upper sides, portal\n834\t  facades by style (stone arches, neon frames, ice). Three world lights follow the player through tunnels (warm,\n835\t  cool, theme).\n836\t- **Pads:**\n837\t  - speed pad: an 8 × 6 m quad with 3 chevrons whose colours cycle front to back at 6 Hz (vertex colours rewritten\n838\t    each frame or a UV scroll), cyan `#3ad8ff`;\n839\t  - weapon pad: a 6 × 6 m amber `#ffb000` quad with a pulsing triangle sigil and a light post at the edge;\n840\t  - pit strip: green `#3aff8a` with \"+\" marks and a gantry sign PIT.\n841\t- **Gantries:** the start/finish gantry has the 3-light start lights (red → green), a timing board (canvas texture\n842\t  showing the race time) and team flags. Sponsor gantries go every ~350 m over the track. Each track also has a\n843\t  landmark arch.\n844\t- **Drop and gap edges:** the lip face (a vertical face), the far-edge face, and a hazard stripe painted on the lip.\n845\t- **Overclock skin:** a second material set per chunk. Black surface with an emissive grid (lines every 4 m, colour\n846\t  `hsl(zone·37°, 100%, 60%)`), neon wall lines, scenery hidden, terrain hidden by fog (`fog` near 150 m, far 600 m,\n847\t  black), sky black with slow colour pulses, bloom up.\n848\t\n849\t**Craft (`62-shipkit.js`)**, built from code as BufferGeometry, flat-shaded, 200–600 triangles each:\n850\t- **Hull:** lofted through 6 cross-sections (an octagon scaled per section, from the needle nose to the tail), with\n851\t  per-design profiles;\n852\t- **canopy:** dark glossy, with an emissive rim;\n853\t- **wings:** flat wedges, swept, with team-coloured tips;\n854\t- **fins:** 0–2;\n855\t- **engine pods:** 1–3, cylinders with emissive inner discs (team engine colour);\n856\t- **airbrake flaps:** 2 hinged boxes at the rear sides (rotate);\n857\t- **livery** by vertex colour per part (primary, secondary, accent stripe), the race number, and the team logo\n858\t  (a 32 px canvas decal on the top);\n859\t- **exhaust trail:** a ribbon of the last 0.35 s of tail positions, alpha fading, team colour;\n860\t- **boost flame:** a cone that grows;\n861\t- **shield shell:** an ellipsoid at opacity 0 that flashes to 0.6 on a hit, bulwark-blue for BULWARK;\n862\t- **explosion:** 8 hull shards flying ballistically for 1.5 s, plus `particles.explosion` and a light flash;\n863\t- **rescue drone:** a 4-rotor drone mesh with a tractor beam cone.\n864\t\n865\tThe six designs are in §4.1. **Ghosts** (hub players, time-trial ghost) use the same mesh in a transparent additive\n866\tmaterial (opacity 0.35) tinted with the seat or ghost colour, plus a name tag.\n867\t\n868\t**Effects (`68-fx.js`)**:\n869\t- wall sparks via `game.particles.sparks` at the contact point;\n870\t- dust and spray on landings (`dust`; water spray at Solenne and Borealis);\n871\t- weapon visuals: rocket meshes with smoke trails, the seeker's spiral trail, mines (spinning spheres, blinking red),\n872\t  cannon tracers, the rail beam (a 0.6 m white-cyan cylinder fading over 0.4 s, plus a screen flash), the tremor wave\n873\t  (a glowing band of quads riding the surface), the bulwark hex bubble, the autopilot ring, nitro flames, the siphon\n874\t  zigzag beam;\n875\t- **speed lines** in the HUD (screen-space streaks from the centre, density ∝ `(v/top)²`, more while boosting);\n876\t- weather: Borealis snow (instanced flakes near the camera), Karakum heat-haze dust, Meridian light rain (streak\n877\t  particles), Solenne sea spray.\n878\t\n879\t**Split screen.** `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'rows' })` with `world.addCamera({ mode: 'fixed', far: 26000 })`.\n880\tEach viewport's `camera.fixed` is set from its own player's chase or cockpit cam. World3D turns filters off while\n881\tsplit, which is expected.\n882\t\n883\t**Warm-up.** In `loading`, after everything is built, do one hidden frame with every pooled mesh visible in front of\n884\tthe camera (each weapon FX, both skins, ghosts), call `world.prepare()`, then hide them. No shader stalls mid-race.\n885\t\n886\t### 3.8 HUD (`70-hud.js`): pixel art at game resolution, anchored to `r.W × r.H`\n887\t\n888\tLayout at 427 × 240 (16:9; everything is anchored and scales with `HUD size`):\n889\t- **Top left:** POSITION as a big number (`E.font.title`, scale 4) plus `/8` small. LAP `2/3` below it. In SNIPEOUT\n890\t  this is the points table (top 4) instead.\n891\t- **Top centre:** the race time `1:23.45`. On a lap: the lap time with ±delta vs best (green/red), held 3 s.\n892\t  \"FINAL LAP\" banner.\n893\t- **Top right:** the minimap (72 px), craft as team-coloured dots, the player blinking, ghosts hollow.\n894\t- **Bottom left:** the weapon slot. A 24 × 24 pixel icon per weapon (§4.4), its name, and prompts `□ FIRE  ○ ABSORB`\n895\t  drawn with the glyph icons (§3.9). The pickup roll spin. The railshot charge ring. The autopilot/bulwark countdown.\n896\t- **Bottom right:**\n897\t  - speed: a segmented bar of 24 segments, cyan → white → magenta in boost, with km/h at scale 2;\n898\t  - energy: 20 segments, green > 50 %, yellow > 25 %, red and blinking below; it shakes on damage; \"PIT\" hint when\n899\t    low;\n900\t  - the boost indicator.\n901\t- **Centre:**\n902\t  - the countdown digits (scale 6, pop tween);\n903\t  - the rev bar during the countdown;\n904\t  - **callouts:** weapon names, PERFECT START, BARREL ROLL, SNIPED!, ELIMINATED, WRONG WAY, PERFECT LAP, NEW RECORD,\n905\t    ZONE n. They pop with scale and alpha, last 1.2 s, and stack at most 2;\n906\t  - the lock reticle on the projected target (`world.project`), a rotating bracket that turns red when locked;\n907\t  - the incoming-lock arrow at the bottom centre.\n908\t- **Name tags:** pilot name and position above craft within 2500 u (projected), fading with distance.\n909\t- **Radio box:** a small portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`, 28 px) and a subtitle line at the top left under the position\n910\t  for pilot banter and the announcer (§3.10).\n911\t- **Split screen:** per viewport a compact HUD (position, lap, speed, energy, weapon) via `r.viewport`. Countdown and\n912\t  results go over the whole screen in `scene.hud(r)`.\n913\t- **Overclock:** ZONE number (scale 4), the zone progress bar (12 s), speed, energy. No position or lap.\n914\t- **Hub session:** the ghost players' names and live positions.\n915\t- The HUD stays clear of `game.cornerArea()` when the corner shows (it is hidden in play).\n916\t\n917\t### 3.9 Front-end, UI and UX: 10-foot and controller-first (`75-ui.js`, `55-glyphs.js`, `01-input.js`)\n918\t\n919\t**Rules for every screen** (TASK.md: a TV at 10 feet, no dense web-style data screens):"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"d85e1512-a883-4b9d-9623-18ad97bcdfb5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:42:56.979Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"Roll sign: verify with a screenshot on Karakum's spiral, a right-hand banked turn. The horizon must tilt the way the\ntrack does. If it is inverted, negate the roll in one place (`SN.cam.rollSign`).\n\n**TV director** (intro flyover, attract, replay, spectating, podium intro):\n- **Camera spots** are built at load every ~200 m. Each is `C(s) + R'·side·(hw + 15…30 m) + Zup·(6…20 m)`, on the\n  outside of curves, alternating sides on straights. Skip a spot if the terrain (`world.ground`) is above it, or if it\n  is inside another track section (`T.query`). Tunnel spots go 2 m under the ceiling, 4 m from the wall. Overpass\n  spots look up from the lower deck. Each spot stores `s`.\n- **Shots:**\n  - `trackside`: fixed eye, looking at the target, with the FOV narrowing (40→20°) as the target nears;\n  - `heli`: 40 m up, 60 m back, following;\n  - `chase`;\n  - `nose`;\n  - `low`: 1 m above the surface ahead, looking back at the target;\n  - `flyby`: along the line 30 m ahead of the target, looking back.\n- **Logic:**\n  - target = the player (spectate/replay) or the most interesting craft (attract: leader, a close fight within 300 u,\n    a weapon fired in the last 2 s, a jump);\n  - pick the spot 150–900 u ahead of the target with a clear line (raycast against the track only), hold 2.5–6 s, and\n    cut when the target passes the spot by 400 u;\n  - every third cut is heli, chase, nose or low;\n  - events cut early: an elimination, a railshot or a jump launch;\n  - never cut twice within 1.2 s.\n- **Intro flyover:** 6 s along the line from `s = −900 m` to the grid at 2.5× the target speed, then a 1 s whip onto\n  the grid.\n\n### 3.7 Rendering (`60-render.js`, `62-shipkit.js`, `64-trackmesh.js`, `66-scenery.js`, `68-fx.js`)\n\n**Worlds.** `World3D.init(game)` runs once (boot). Then:\n- **Hangar world**, made at boot. A small `level` (text rows):\n  - a 24 × 16 tile hall: floor `{ floor: 0 }`, a turntable `{ mark: 'turntable' }` and a podium of three raised floors\n    (`{ floor: 24 }` 1st, `{ floor: 16 }` 2nd, `{ floor: 8 }` 3rd, marks `p1 p2 p3`);\n  - `torch: false`, our own lights: 3 coloured spots plus team-coloured neon strips (our meshes);\n  - camera `'fixed'`, `fog: false`.\n\n  It is used by the menus, team select (the craft on the turntable), results/podium (pilots as rig **cards** via\n  `world.hero({ rig })` posed `cheer` / `wave` / `hips`) and the ending.\n- **Track world**, one per track, made by the `loading` scene. At most one is alive besides the hangar: dispose the\n  previous with `world.dispose()`. Boot makes PORT SOLENNE's, so the title and attract start at once.\n\n```js\nnew E.World3D(game, {\n  terrain: { size: 65536 /* 4 km */, height: theme.height, color: theme.color, far: 26000, cell: 64, rock: theme.rock, bottom: -3000 },\n  sky: theme.sky, fog: theme.fog, ambient: theme.ambient, sun: Object.assign({ shadow: true, area: 900 }, theme.sun),\n  torchLights: 0, lights: 4, glowLights: 8, shadows: game.settings.shadows3d !== false,\n  filter: { look: game.settings.filter3d || 'clean', bloom: game.settings.bloom !== false },\n  camera: { mode: 'fixed', far: 26000, near: 4 }, particleGround: (x, y, z) => track.groundBelow(x, y, z),\n  onDraw: (w, r) => SN.render.onDraw(w, r)\n});\n```\n\n**Terrain carving.** `theme.height(x, y)` = the theme's natural height, combined with a **corridor grid** (cell 16 m,\nbuilt from the slices at load):\n- near the track: `min(natural, deckZ − clearance(d))`, where `clearance` grows from 3 m at the edge to 0 at 60 m, so\n  the ground falls away under elevated decks and meets the track at grade;\n- under tunnel slices: `max(natural, ceilZ + 4 m)`, so the rock covers the tunnel;\n- portal frames hide the seams.\n\nKeep `height()` fast: it is a few grid lookups and noise (`E.noise2`).\n\n**Materials** (make them all when the world is made, never mid-race):\n- `MeshLambertNodeMaterial({ vertexColors: true })` for the track surface, walls and scenery;\n- `MeshBasicNodeMaterial` for emissive neon, pads, engine glow and beams. They are bright, so the bloom catches them.\n  Set `fog: false` on the overclock skin;\n- `MeshToonNodeMaterial` for the craft hulls;\n- transparent additive materials for the shield shells, ghosts and beams.\n\nTextures are canvases drawn pixel by pixel at 64–256 px (`NearestFilter`, the engine's native crisp look): track\npanels, lane dashes, chevrons, sponsor boards, team logos, window grids. **Pads and painted markings** use\n`polygonOffset` (factor −2, units −2) and sit 1 u above the surface. That avoids z-fighting at distance.\n\n**Track meshes** (`64-trackmesh.js`), built in chunks of 40 slices (80 m) for frustum culling:\n- **Surface:** 6 lateral strips. Vertex colours: dark graphite panels `#22252c`/`#2a2e36` alternating every 8 m,\n  bright edge lines, centre dashes, a tint per theme. The grid boxes and the start/finish chequer are painted near\n  `s = 0`.\n- **Walls:** 1.6 m barrier panels with a glowing top strip in the theme's neon (`#29c8e8` coast, `#ffb347` desert,\n  `#ff3ab4` city, `#7af0ff` arctic). On the outside of curves, **directional chevrons** (emissive arrows pointing the\n  way of the turn) every 6 m. Open edges have no wall but a dashed hazard line on the edge.\n- **Underside and supports:**\n  - the deck's underside and thickness (1.2 m), so the deck reads as a bridge;\n  - pylons every 40 m where the deck is more than 4 m above the terrain, at the deck edges; skipped where they would\n    stand in another section's driving envelope;\n  - overpass decks get piers outside the lower deck's walls.\n- **Tunnels:** a 10-segment arch to 12 m, ribs every 12 m, emissive light strips along both upper sides, portal\n  facades by style (stone arches, neon frames, ice). Three world lights follow the player through tunnels (warm,\n  cool, theme).\n- **Pads:**\n  - speed pad: an 8 × 6 m quad with 3 chevrons whose colours cycle front to back at 6 Hz (vertex colours rewritten\n    each frame or a UV scroll), cyan `#3ad8ff`;\n  - weapon pad: a 6 × 6 m amber `#ffb000` quad with a pulsing triangle sigil and a light post at the edge;\n  - pit strip: green `#3aff8a` with \"+\" marks and a gantry sign PIT.\n- **Gantries:** the start/finish gantry has the 3-light start lights (red → green), a timing board (canvas texture\n  showing the race time) and team flags. Sponsor gantries go every ~350 m over the track. Each track also has a\n  landmark arch.\n- **Drop and gap edges:** the lip face (a vertical face), the far-edge face, and a hazard stripe painted on the lip.\n- **Overclock skin:** a second material set per chunk. Black surface with an emissive grid (lines every 4 m, colour\n  `hsl(zone·37°, 100%, 60%)`), neon wall lines, scenery hidden, terrain hidden by fog (`fog` near 150 m, far 600 m,\n  black), sky black with slow colour pulses, bloom up.\n\n**Craft (`62-shipkit.js`)**, built from code as BufferGeometry, flat-shaded, 200–600 triangles each:\n- **Hull:** lofted through 6 cross-sections (an octagon scaled per section, from the needle nose to the tail), with\n  per-design profiles;\n- **canopy:** dark glossy, with an emissive rim;\n- **wings:** flat wedges, swept, with team-coloured tips;\n- **fins:** 0–2;\n- **engine pods:** 1–3, cylinders with emissive inner discs (team engine colour);\n- **airbrake flaps:** 2 hinged boxes at the rear sides (rotate);\n- **livery** by vertex colour per part (primary, secondary, accent stripe), the race number, and the team logo\n  (a 32 px canvas decal on the top);\n- **exhaust trail:** a ribbon of the last 0.35 s of tail positions, alpha fading, team colour;\n- **boost flame:** a cone that grows;\n- **shield shell:** an ellipsoid at opacity 0 that flashes to 0.6 on a hit, bulwark-blue for BULWARK;\n- **explosion:** 8 hull shards flying ballistically for 1.5 s, plus `particles.explosion` and a light flash;\n- **rescue drone:** a 4-rotor drone mesh with a tractor beam cone.\n\nThe six designs are in §4.1. **Ghosts** (hub players, time-trial ghost) use the same mesh in a transparent additive\nmaterial (opacity 0.35) tinted with the seat or ghost colour, plus a name tag.\n\n**Effects (`68-fx.js`)**:\n- wall sparks via `game.particles.sparks` at the contact point;\n- dust and spray on landings (`dust`; water spray at Solenne and Borealis);\n- weapon visuals: rocket meshes with smoke trails, the seeker's spiral trail, mines (spinning spheres, blinking red),\n  cannon tracers, the rail beam (a 0.6 m white-cyan cylinder fading over 0.4 s, plus a screen flash), the tremor wave\n  (a glowing band of quads riding the surface), the bulwark hex bubble, the autopilot ring, nitro flames, the siphon\n  zigzag beam;\n- **speed lines** in the HUD (screen-space streaks from the centre, density ∝ `(v/top)²`, more while boosting);\n- weather: Borealis snow (instanced flakes near the camera), Karakum heat-haze dust, Meridian light rain (streak\n  particles), Solenne sea spray.\n\n**Split screen.** `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'rows' })` with `world.addCamera({ mode: 'fixed', far: 26000 })`.\nEach viewport's `camera.fixed` is set from its own player's chase or cockpit cam. World3D turns filters off while\nsplit, which is expected.\n\n**Warm-up.** In `loading`, after everything is built, do one hidden frame with every pooled mesh visible in front of\nthe camera (each weapon FX, both skins, ghosts), call `world.prepare()`, then hide them. No shader stalls mid-race.\n\n### 3.8 HUD (`70-hud.js`): pixel art at game resolution, anchored to `r.W × r.H`\n\nLayout at 427 × 240 (16:9; everything is anchored and scales with `HUD size`):\n- **Top left:** POSITION as a big number (`E.font.title`, scale 4) plus `/8` small. LAP `2/3` below it. In SNIPEOUT\n  this is the points table (top 4) instead.\n- **Top centre:** the race time `1:23.45`. On a lap: the lap time with ±delta vs best (green/red), held 3 s.\n  \"FINAL LAP\" banner.\n- **Top right:** the minimap (72 px), craft as team-coloured dots, the player blinking, ghosts hollow.\n- **Bottom left:** the weapon slot. A 24 × 24 pixel icon per weapon (§4.4), its name, and prompts `□ FIRE  ○ ABSORB`\n  drawn with the glyph icons (§3.9). The pickup roll spin. The railshot charge ring. The autopilot/bulwark countdown.\n- **Bottom right:**\n  - speed: a segmented bar of 24 segments, cyan → white → magenta in boost, with km/h at scale 2;\n  - energy: 20 segments, green > 50 %, yellow > 25 %, red and blinking below; it shakes on damage; \"PIT\" hint when\n    low;\n  - the boost indicator.\n- **Centre:**\n  - the countdown digits (scale 6, pop tween);\n  - the rev bar during the countdown;\n  - **callouts:** weapon names, PERFECT START, BARREL ROLL, SNIPED!, ELIMINATED, WRONG WAY, PERFECT LAP, NEW RECORD,\n    ZONE n. They pop with scale and alpha, last 1.2 s, and stack at most 2;\n  - the lock reticle on the projected target (`world.project`), a rotating bracket that turns red when locked;\n  - the incoming-lock arrow at the bottom centre.\n- **Name tags:** pilot name and position above craft within 2500 u (projected), fading with distance.\n- **Radio box:** a small portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`, 28 px) and a subtitle line at the top left under the position\n  for pilot banter and the announcer (§3.10).\n- **Split screen:** per viewport a compact HUD (position, lap, speed, energy, weapon) via `r.viewport`. Countdown and\n  results go over the whole screen in `scene.hud(r)`.\n- **Overclock:** ZONE number (scale 4), the zone progress bar (12 s), speed, energy. No position or lap.\n- **Hub session:** the ghost players' names and live positions.\n- The HUD stays clear of `game.cornerArea()` when the corner shows (it is hidden in play).\n\n### 3.9 Front-end, UI and UX: 10-foot and controller-first (`75-ui.js`, `55-glyphs.js`, `01-input.js`)\n\n**Rules for every screen** (TASK.md: a TV at 10 feet, no dense web-style data screens):","numLines":170,"startLine":750,"totalLines":2068}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VtWFSPYuhMSemm24iXmUfn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
