{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FKsacmrwzzdkGBKqpd1oWG","type":"tool_result","content":"925\t\n926\t**Rules for every screen** (TASK.md: a TV at 10 feet, no dense web-style data screens):\n927\t- At most 6 focusable items per screen.\n928\t- Labels at font scale ≥ 2 (14 px of 240). Titles at scale 3–4. Body text at scale 2, at most 3 lines.\n929\t- One focus at a time. It is drawn as a thick animated chevron frame plus a colour shift plus a 1 px \"scanline\"\n930\t  shimmer. It is never shown by colour alone (TASK and engine rule).\n931\t- Navigation:\n932\t  - d-pad, stick or arrows (WASD too in menus) move the focus, with `input.repeat` when held;\n933\t  - ✕, Enter or Space confirms; ○, Esc or Backspace goes back;\n934\t  - L1/R1, Q/E or the mouse wheel switch tabs or pages;\n935\t  - **mouse hover moves the focus**, a left click activates, and every screen has a clickable BACK chip at the bottom\n936\t    left.\n937\t- **A prompt bar** at the bottom of every screen shows the actions for the **last device used**\n938\t  (`input.lastDevice`):\n939\t  - gamepad: glyph icons;\n940\t  - keyboard: keycaps;\n941\t  - mouse: mouse icons (left click SELECT, BACK chip).\n942\t\n943\t  It switches the moment another device is touched.\n944\t- **Glyph icons (`55-glyphs.js`):**\n945\t  - **PlayStation** (the default): ✕ blue `#7cb2e8`, ○ red `#ff6b6b`, □ pink `#ff79c6`, △ green `#3fd8a6`, drawn in\n946\t    dark discs of 11 px; L1/R1/L2/R2 as rounded tabs with text; Options and Create as pill icons; the d-pad and stick\n947\t    as small icons.\n948\t  - **Xbox** (Settings → Button symbols): A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow; LB/RB/LT/RT; Menu and View.\n949\t  - **Keyboard:** keycaps sized to the label from `input.label(action, 'keyboard')`.\n950\t  - **Mouse:** a mouse with the left or right button lit.\n951\t\n952\t  `SN.glyph.draw(g, action, x, y, { device })` returns the width drawn. **Never hard-code key names.** Always go\n953\t  through `input.label` and the actual bindings (rebinding works).\n954\t- Animations: menu tiles slide in with `game.tween` (0.18 s, `outBack`), focus chevrons pulse, background light\n955\t  streaks drift, and screen changes use the engine's `'wipe'` fade (0.25 s).\n956\t\n957\t**Input mapping (`01-input.js`).** The game's preset, in this order (the order matters for the engine's half-keyboard\n958\tsplit, §3.16):\n959\t\n960\t```js\n961\tSN.INPUT = {\n962\t  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n963\t  start: ['Enter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'Space', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'],\n964\t  thrust: ['KeyW', 'Pad0'], fire: ['Space', 'Mouse0', 'Pad2'], absorb: ['ShiftLeft', 'Mouse2', 'Pad1'],\n965\t  brakeL: ['KeyQ', 'Pad6'], brakeR: ['KeyE', 'Pad7'], camera: ['KeyC', 'Pad3'], shiftL: ['KeyZ', 'Pad4'], shiftR: ['KeyX', 'Pad5'],\n966\t  brake: ['KeyS'], lookBack: ['KeyB', 'Pad11']\n967\t};\n968\t```\n969\t\n970\t- In a race, **steer and pitch are not read from up/down/left/right as actions**:\n971\t  - steer = `input.padMove[0]` (analog) + digital A/D/←/→/d-pad (ramped);\n972\t  - pitch = `−input.padMove[1]` + ↑/↓/d-pad (stick up = nose down).\n973\t\n974\t  W and S are therefore only thrust and brake in a race, while still moving the menu focus elsewhere.\n975\t- Airbrakes: `max(input.value('brakeL'), down('brake'))` (analog L2/R2 via engine edit 3).\n976\t- Double-tapping Q or E (within 0.25 s) = side-shift.\n977\t- Mouse buttons fire and absorb in a race.\n978\t- The **virtual pad** `SN.vpad[playerIndex]` (analog values) is merged into the controls. The tests' bots, the\n979\t  autopilot and the attract mode drive craft through it, the same path as a human.\n980\t- The menu's Controls screen names the actions:\n981\t  `menu: { controls: { thrust: 'Thrust', fire: 'Fire weapon', absorb: 'Absorb weapon', brakeL: 'Airbrake left',\n982\t  brakeR: 'Airbrake right', brake: 'Both airbrakes', shiftL: 'Side-shift / roll left', shiftR: 'Side-shift / roll right',\n983\t  camera: 'Camera', lookBack: 'Look back' } }`.\n984\t\n985\t**Screens:**\n986\t\n987\t| Screen | Contents (10-foot: big, few, focused) |\n988\t| --- | --- |\n989\t| **Title** | The Solenne track world in a slow TV-director flyby. The SNIPEOUT HD logo: `E.font.title` scale 5, chrome gradient `['#ffffff', '#9ff4ff', '#29c8e8', '#1a2a4a']`, with a pixel \"HD\" badge and an animated light sweep. The tagline. \"PRESS ✕ / ENTER\" pulsing (glyph of the last device). The version (`E.versionLabel()`) small at the bottom right. Idle for 10 s → attract |\n990\t| **Touch-only notice** (§3.16) | Over the title: \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" (scale 2, centred, in a panel) and one big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). No touch controls anywhere. The attract still starts after 10 s, and a tap returns to this notice |\n991\t| **Main menu** | Hangar world (the player's last craft on the turntable). A vertical list of 6 big tiles: **SEASON · QUICK RACE · CHALLENGES ▸ · VERSUS · ACADEMY · OPTIONS ▸**. CHALLENGES opens TIME TRIAL / HOT LAP / SNIPEOUT / OVERCLOCK; OPTIONS opens SETTINGS / CONTROLS / HOW TO PLAY / RECORDS / ABOUT / DEV MODE. When an autosave exists, the first tile reads **CONTINUE SEASON** (it loads `saves.latest()` and opens the season hub) |\n992\t| **Class select** | 4 tiles in a row: SPARK / FLARE / STORM / SINGULARITY, with a top-speed figure and a lock icon plus the unlock hint (\"WIN THE ROOKIE LICENCE\") |\n993\t| **Track select** | One big card at a time (←/→ or L1/R1 or the wheel or a click on the arrows): the track outline at 150 px drawn with px.line, the name (scale 3), place, length, a difficulty pip row, your best time, and a one-line blurb. The hangar background tints to the theme |\n994\t| **Team and pilot select** | The craft on the turntable (mouse drag rotates it, the right stick rotates). Team name (scale 3) and logo. **4 stat bars** (SPEED, THRUST, HANDLING, SHIELD) as 10-segment bars. One-line bio. The pilot toggle (2 pilots, portraits via `rig.drawPortrait` at 48 px). ←/→ change team |\n995\t| **Laps / confirm** | A summary card (mode, class, track, team, laps), START RACE |\n996\t| **Loading** | The track name card, a progress bar, and one tip line (\"Absorb a weapon you can't use: shield is worth more than a miss.\") |\n997\t| **Race** | the HUD (§3.8) |\n998\t| **Results** | The top 8 as **one row per craft**: position, team colour chip, pilot, time or gap, best-lap star. The player's row is highlighted. Medal and record banners. Actions: CONTINUE · RETRY · REPLAY · MENU. A podium cutaway (hangar world, top 3 pilot cards cheering, confetti) plays first for 4 s when the player is top 3 |\n999\t| **Season hub** | 4 columns (ROOKIE LICENCE, AUTHORITY NOTICE, STORM WARNING, GRAND PRIX), each with 2–4 event tiles: mode icon, track, medal earned. Locked columns are dimmed with the rule shown. Before an event's first run, a briefing (§3.11) |\n1000\t| **GP standings** | Between races: 8 rows, points, the gap to the leader, NEXT RACE |\n1001\t| **How to play** | 5 pages (L1/R1): CONTROLS (the controller diagram drawn in pixels, or the keyboard map, by device), RACING (pads, pitch, airbrakes, side-shift, rolls), WEAPONS (10 icons with a one-line effect each, two pages), ENERGY (walls, damage, pit lane, absorb, elimination), MODES |\n1002\t| **Records** | per track: best race and best lap per class, pilot name. One track per page |\n1003\t| **About / Credits** | §3.18 |\n1004\t\n1005\t### 3.10 Audio (`50-audio.js`, `10-data-music.js`): all synthesized, no files\n1006\t\n1007\t**Music:** the engine's tracker (`game.audio.music(song, { sync: true })`) with the §2.7 extensions. Songs are data:\n1008\t`{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks: [{ name, wave, vol, lp, uni, det, pan, notes, on }] }`. **Layers** (`audio.layer(name, vol,\n1009\tfade)`) make the music react:\n1010\t- the countdown has pads and bass only;\n1011\t- the drums come in at GO;\n1012\t- the lead comes in on the final lap;\n1013\t- after the race, everything but the pads fades out;\n1014\t- Overclock adds a layer every 2 zones and runs `audio.tempo(min(176, bpm + 3·zone))`.\n1015\t\n1016\tWhen a race starts, a \"now playing\" toast shows (`♪ STACKLINE — NULLPOINT`). Fictional artists, all original.\n1017\t\n1018\t| Song (id) | Where | BPM / key | Character |\n1019\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1020\t| `zero` \"Zero Crossing\" by HALCYON DRIFT | title, menus | 112, D minor | airy pads, a soft arpeggio, a broken beat |\n1021\t| `solenne` \"Riviera Burn\" by SOLSTICE 9 | Port Solenne | 128, A minor | sunny electro-house, four-on-the-floor, offbeat open hats, a pumping saw bass, a pluck lead |\n1022\t| `karakum` \"Sandglass\" by DUNE//CODE | Karakum Spire | 140, E Phrygian | big beat, breakbeat drums (k/s pattern), a distorted acid bass (`lp` env), a call-and-response lead |\n1023\t| `meridian` \"Stackline\" by NULLPOINT | Meridian Stack | 172 (half-time feel), F minor | drum'n'bass breaks, a reese bass (`uni: 3, det: 18` saw, lowpass), stabs |\n1024\t| `borealis` \"Polar Vector\" by AURORA SYSTEMS | Borealis Vault | 136, B minor | trance: rolling 16th bass, a supersaw lead, a long riser every 8 bars |\n1025\t| `overclock` \"Clock Skew\" by THE AUTHORITY | Overclock | 120 → 176 | minimal techno that adds a layer per 2 zones |\n1026\t| stings | lap, final lap, win, podium, eliminated, unlock, medal | — | 1–3 s motifs (`audio.sting`) |\n1027\t\n1028\tExample, the start of `solenne`, to set the format and the bar:\n1029\t\n1030\t```js\n1031\tSN.SONGS.solenne = { bpm: 128, steps: 4, tracks: [\n1032\t  { name: 'kick',  wave: 'drums', vol: .22, notes: 'k . . . k . . . k . . . k . . . | k . . . k . . . k . . . k . k .' },\n1033\t  { name: 'hats',  wave: 'drums', vol: .10, notes: '. . o . . . o . . . o . . . o h | . . o . . . o . . . o . . h o h' },\n1034\t  { name: 'clap',  wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: '. . . . p . . . . . . . p . . . | . . . . p . . . . . . . p . p .' },\n1035\t  { name: 'bass',  wave: 'saw', vol: .16, lp: { f: 300, q: 9, env: 1800, dec: .12 },\n1036\t    notes: 'A1 . A2 . A1 A2 . A1 . A2 . A1 G2 . A2! . | F1 . F2 . F1 F2 . F1 . F2 . F1 E2 . F2! .' },\n1037\t  { name: 'pad',   wave: 'saw', vol: .05, uni: 3, det: 14, lp: { f: 1400, q: 1 }, notes: 'A3 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - | F3 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -' },\n1038\t  { name: 'lead',  wave: 'pulse', vol: .07, on: false, notes: 'E5 . C5 . A4 . C5 E5 . G5 . E5 . C5 . . | F5 . C5 . A4 . C5 F5 . A5 . F5 . E5 . .' }\n1039\t] };\n1040\t```\n1041\t\n1042\tEach song needs at least 16 bars of material (A/B sections, a breakdown) so that a 3-minute race doesn't drone.\n1043\t\n1044\t**SFX** (`audio.define` voices, plus our own WebAudio graphs on the effects bus where a voice can't do it). These\n1045\tnames are referenced by events (§2.5):\n1046\t\n1047\t| Group | Sounds |\n1048\t| --- | --- |\n1049\t| UI | `ui_move` (short pulse blip), `ui_ok` (two-tone up), `ui_back` (down), `ui_locked` (buzz), `ui_tab` (click) |\n1050\t| Race | `count_beep`, `count_go` (chord), `lap` (chime), `final_lap` (a rising sting), `finish` (fanfare), `wrongway` (siren blip), `pos_up` / `pos_down` (tiny arps) |\n1051\t| Craft | engine hum (continuous, below), `boost_pad` (whoosh plus a pitch sweep), `pickup_roll` (a ticking arp), `weapon_pad` (sparkle), `airbrake` (filtered noise hiss, looped while braking), `sideshift` (puff), `roll` (a whirr), `roll_boost`, `botch`, `land_soft`, `land_hard` (thud plus clank), `wall_hit` (metal bang, pitch by impact), `scrape` (looped band-passed noise, volume by speed), `bump`, `pit_charge` (looped rising tone), `low_shield` (beep every 0.8 s), `explode` (noise boom plus a sub drop), `eliminated`, `respawn`, `rescue` (drone whine) |\n1052\t| Weapons | `swarm_fire`, `seeker_lock` (beeps faster to a solid tone), `seeker_fire`, `mine_drop`, `cannon_fire`, `rail_charge` (a rising whine), `rail_fire` (crack plus a long zap), `tremor` (sub rumble), `bulwark_on/off`, `autopilot_on/off`, `nitro`, `siphon` (a crackling loop), `absorb` (a reverse whoosh with a chime), `hit_light`, `hit_heavy` |\n1053\t\n1054\t**Engine hum.** The four nearest craft each get a persistent graph: saw + detuned square → lowpass → gain →\n1055\tStereoPanner → the effects bus.\n1056\t- `f = 48 + 120·(v/top)` Hz with a thrust wobble.\n1057\t- Cutoff `500 + 2500·(v/top)` (+1500 in boost).\n1058\t- Others: volume by distance (1/(1 + d/800 u)), Doppler pitch `×clamp(1 + vRel/6000, .85, 1.15)`, pan by the screen\n1059\t  x of `world.project`.\n1060\t- The player's hum is louder and centred.\n1061\t- In a split screen: player 1 pans left, player 2 right.\n1062\t- All of it is muted on pause, on `game.audio.muted`, and on the hub's `end`.\n1063\t\n1064\t**Gibberish voice (Animalese/Simlish style), `SN.Voice.say(text, voice)`:**\n1065\t- Every word is turned into syllables seeded by the word's hash, so the same word always sounds the same (\"SEEKER\"\n1066\t  is always \"see-kra\").\n1067\t- Syllable count = `max(1, round(letters / 2.6))`.\n1068\t- Each syllable is a consonant burst (noise, band-passed at 2–5 kHz, 18 ms; picked by the word's letters) followed by\n1069\t  a vowel: a saw at `f0` through two band-pass \"formants\" `[F1, F2]` from a 5-vowel table (a: 800/1200, e: 400/2000,\n1070\t  i: 300/2300, o: 450/800, u: 325/700), lasting `70–110 ms / speed`.\n1071\t- Pitch: per-syllable jitter ±8 %; down 12 % at a full stop, up 18 % at \"?\", +10 % and louder at \"!\".\n1072\t- Breathiness: 15 % noise.\n1073\t- `say()` returns its duration. Subtitles and dialog pages wait on it. Headless, it is computed without sound.\n1074\t\n1075\t| Voice | f0 | Speed | Use |\n1076\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1077\t| ANNOUNCER (race control's \"ORACLE\") | 205 Hz | 0.85 | calm, slightly ring-modulated (×0.4 at 60 Hz) |\n1078\t| pilots | 95–240 Hz | 1.0–1.3 | per pilot: radio banter, podium |\n1079\t| principals | 110–190 Hz | 0.9 | briefings |\n1080\t| KAI-ZERO | 140 Hz | 1.1 | bitcrushed (a WaveShaper step curve) |\n1081\t\n1082\t`E.Dialog` boxes use `voice: null` (no letter blips) and call `SN.Voice.say` per page.\n1083\t\n1084\t**Announcer lines** (each spoken as gibberish **and** shown as a subtitle, Settings → Subtitles):"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"4b0f6ef9-f14a-45ae-878f-c190f33c2f91","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:43:18.845Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**Rules for every screen** (TASK.md: a TV at 10 feet, no dense web-style data screens):\n- At most 6 focusable items per screen.\n- Labels at font scale ≥ 2 (14 px of 240). Titles at scale 3–4. Body text at scale 2, at most 3 lines.\n- One focus at a time. It is drawn as a thick animated chevron frame plus a colour shift plus a 1 px \"scanline\"\n  shimmer. It is never shown by colour alone (TASK and engine rule).\n- Navigation:\n  - d-pad, stick or arrows (WASD too in menus) move the focus, with `input.repeat` when held;\n  - ✕, Enter or Space confirms; ○, Esc or Backspace goes back;\n  - L1/R1, Q/E or the mouse wheel switch tabs or pages;\n  - **mouse hover moves the focus**, a left click activates, and every screen has a clickable BACK chip at the bottom\n    left.\n- **A prompt bar** at the bottom of every screen shows the actions for the **last device used**\n  (`input.lastDevice`):\n  - gamepad: glyph icons;\n  - keyboard: keycaps;\n  - mouse: mouse icons (left click SELECT, BACK chip).\n\n  It switches the moment another device is touched.\n- **Glyph icons (`55-glyphs.js`):**\n  - **PlayStation** (the default): ✕ blue `#7cb2e8`, ○ red `#ff6b6b`, □ pink `#ff79c6`, △ green `#3fd8a6`, drawn in\n    dark discs of 11 px; L1/R1/L2/R2 as rounded tabs with text; Options and Create as pill icons; the d-pad and stick\n    as small icons.\n  - **Xbox** (Settings → Button symbols): A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow; LB/RB/LT/RT; Menu and View.\n  - **Keyboard:** keycaps sized to the label from `input.label(action, 'keyboard')`.\n  - **Mouse:** a mouse with the left or right button lit.\n\n  `SN.glyph.draw(g, action, x, y, { device })` returns the width drawn. **Never hard-code key names.** Always go\n  through `input.label` and the actual bindings (rebinding works).\n- Animations: menu tiles slide in with `game.tween` (0.18 s, `outBack`), focus chevrons pulse, background light\n  streaks drift, and screen changes use the engine's `'wipe'` fade (0.25 s).\n\n**Input mapping (`01-input.js`).** The game's preset, in this order (the order matters for the engine's half-keyboard\nsplit, §3.16):\n\n```js\nSN.INPUT = {\n  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n  start: ['Enter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'Space', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'],\n  thrust: ['KeyW', 'Pad0'], fire: ['Space', 'Mouse0', 'Pad2'], absorb: ['ShiftLeft', 'Mouse2', 'Pad1'],\n  brakeL: ['KeyQ', 'Pad6'], brakeR: ['KeyE', 'Pad7'], camera: ['KeyC', 'Pad3'], shiftL: ['KeyZ', 'Pad4'], shiftR: ['KeyX', 'Pad5'],\n  brake: ['KeyS'], lookBack: ['KeyB', 'Pad11']\n};\n```\n\n- In a race, **steer and pitch are not read from up/down/left/right as actions**:\n  - steer = `input.padMove[0]` (analog) + digital A/D/←/→/d-pad (ramped);\n  - pitch = `−input.padMove[1]` + ↑/↓/d-pad (stick up = nose down).\n\n  W and S are therefore only thrust and brake in a race, while still moving the menu focus elsewhere.\n- Airbrakes: `max(input.value('brakeL'), down('brake'))` (analog L2/R2 via engine edit 3).\n- Double-tapping Q or E (within 0.25 s) = side-shift.\n- Mouse buttons fire and absorb in a race.\n- The **virtual pad** `SN.vpad[playerIndex]` (analog values) is merged into the controls. The tests' bots, the\n  autopilot and the attract mode drive craft through it, the same path as a human.\n- The menu's Controls screen names the actions:\n  `menu: { controls: { thrust: 'Thrust', fire: 'Fire weapon', absorb: 'Absorb weapon', brakeL: 'Airbrake left',\n  brakeR: 'Airbrake right', brake: 'Both airbrakes', shiftL: 'Side-shift / roll left', shiftR: 'Side-shift / roll right',\n  camera: 'Camera', lookBack: 'Look back' } }`.\n\n**Screens:**\n\n| Screen | Contents (10-foot: big, few, focused) |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Title** | The Solenne track world in a slow TV-director flyby. The SNIPEOUT HD logo: `E.font.title` scale 5, chrome gradient `['#ffffff', '#9ff4ff', '#29c8e8', '#1a2a4a']`, with a pixel \"HD\" badge and an animated light sweep. The tagline. \"PRESS ✕ / ENTER\" pulsing (glyph of the last device). The version (`E.versionLabel()`) small at the bottom right. Idle for 10 s → attract |\n| **Touch-only notice** (§3.16) | Over the title: \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" (scale 2, centred, in a panel) and one big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). No touch controls anywhere. The attract still starts after 10 s, and a tap returns to this notice |\n| **Main menu** | Hangar world (the player's last craft on the turntable). A vertical list of 6 big tiles: **SEASON · QUICK RACE · CHALLENGES ▸ · VERSUS · ACADEMY · OPTIONS ▸**. CHALLENGES opens TIME TRIAL / HOT LAP / SNIPEOUT / OVERCLOCK; OPTIONS opens SETTINGS / CONTROLS / HOW TO PLAY / RECORDS / ABOUT / DEV MODE. When an autosave exists, the first tile reads **CONTINUE SEASON** (it loads `saves.latest()` and opens the season hub) |\n| **Class select** | 4 tiles in a row: SPARK / FLARE / STORM / SINGULARITY, with a top-speed figure and a lock icon plus the unlock hint (\"WIN THE ROOKIE LICENCE\") |\n| **Track select** | One big card at a time (←/→ or L1/R1 or the wheel or a click on the arrows): the track outline at 150 px drawn with px.line, the name (scale 3), place, length, a difficulty pip row, your best time, and a one-line blurb. The hangar background tints to the theme |\n| **Team and pilot select** | The craft on the turntable (mouse drag rotates it, the right stick rotates). Team name (scale 3) and logo. **4 stat bars** (SPEED, THRUST, HANDLING, SHIELD) as 10-segment bars. One-line bio. The pilot toggle (2 pilots, portraits via `rig.drawPortrait` at 48 px). ←/→ change team |\n| **Laps / confirm** | A summary card (mode, class, track, team, laps), START RACE |\n| **Loading** | The track name card, a progress bar, and one tip line (\"Absorb a weapon you can't use: shield is worth more than a miss.\") |\n| **Race** | the HUD (§3.8) |\n| **Results** | The top 8 as **one row per craft**: position, team colour chip, pilot, time or gap, best-lap star. The player's row is highlighted. Medal and record banners. Actions: CONTINUE · RETRY · REPLAY · MENU. A podium cutaway (hangar world, top 3 pilot cards cheering, confetti) plays first for 4 s when the player is top 3 |\n| **Season hub** | 4 columns (ROOKIE LICENCE, AUTHORITY NOTICE, STORM WARNING, GRAND PRIX), each with 2–4 event tiles: mode icon, track, medal earned. Locked columns are dimmed with the rule shown. Before an event's first run, a briefing (§3.11) |\n| **GP standings** | Between races: 8 rows, points, the gap to the leader, NEXT RACE |\n| **How to play** | 5 pages (L1/R1): CONTROLS (the controller diagram drawn in pixels, or the keyboard map, by device), RACING (pads, pitch, airbrakes, side-shift, rolls), WEAPONS (10 icons with a one-line effect each, two pages), ENERGY (walls, damage, pit lane, absorb, elimination), MODES |\n| **Records** | per track: best race and best lap per class, pilot name. One track per page |\n| **About / Credits** | §3.18 |\n\n### 3.10 Audio (`50-audio.js`, `10-data-music.js`): all synthesized, no files\n\n**Music:** the engine's tracker (`game.audio.music(song, { sync: true })`) with the §2.7 extensions. Songs are data:\n`{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks: [{ name, wave, vol, lp, uni, det, pan, notes, on }] }`. **Layers** (`audio.layer(name, vol,\nfade)`) make the music react:\n- the countdown has pads and bass only;\n- the drums come in at GO;\n- the lead comes in on the final lap;\n- after the race, everything but the pads fades out;\n- Overclock adds a layer every 2 zones and runs `audio.tempo(min(176, bpm + 3·zone))`.\n\nWhen a race starts, a \"now playing\" toast shows (`♪ STACKLINE — NULLPOINT`). Fictional artists, all original.\n\n| Song (id) | Where | BPM / key | Character |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `zero` \"Zero Crossing\" by HALCYON DRIFT | title, menus | 112, D minor | airy pads, a soft arpeggio, a broken beat |\n| `solenne` \"Riviera Burn\" by SOLSTICE 9 | Port Solenne | 128, A minor | sunny electro-house, four-on-the-floor, offbeat open hats, a pumping saw bass, a pluck lead |\n| `karakum` \"Sandglass\" by DUNE//CODE | Karakum Spire | 140, E Phrygian | big beat, breakbeat drums (k/s pattern), a distorted acid bass (`lp` env), a call-and-response lead |\n| `meridian` \"Stackline\" by NULLPOINT | Meridian Stack | 172 (half-time feel), F minor | drum'n'bass breaks, a reese bass (`uni: 3, det: 18` saw, lowpass), stabs |\n| `borealis` \"Polar Vector\" by AURORA SYSTEMS | Borealis Vault | 136, B minor | trance: rolling 16th bass, a supersaw lead, a long riser every 8 bars |\n| `overclock` \"Clock Skew\" by THE AUTHORITY | Overclock | 120 → 176 | minimal techno that adds a layer per 2 zones |\n| stings | lap, final lap, win, podium, eliminated, unlock, medal | — | 1–3 s motifs (`audio.sting`) |\n\nExample, the start of `solenne`, to set the format and the bar:\n\n```js\nSN.SONGS.solenne = { bpm: 128, steps: 4, tracks: [\n  { name: 'kick',  wave: 'drums', vol: .22, notes: 'k . . . k . . . k . . . k . . . | k . . . k . . . k . . . k . k .' },\n  { name: 'hats',  wave: 'drums', vol: .10, notes: '. . o . . . o . . . o . . . o h | . . o . . . o . . . o . . h o h' },\n  { name: 'clap',  wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: '. . . . p . . . . . . . p . . . | . . . . p . . . . . . . p . p .' },\n  { name: 'bass',  wave: 'saw', vol: .16, lp: { f: 300, q: 9, env: 1800, dec: .12 },\n    notes: 'A1 . A2 . A1 A2 . A1 . A2 . A1 G2 . A2! . | F1 . F2 . F1 F2 . F1 . F2 . F1 E2 . F2! .' },\n  { name: 'pad',   wave: 'saw', vol: .05, uni: 3, det: 14, lp: { f: 1400, q: 1 }, notes: 'A3 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - | F3 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -' },\n  { name: 'lead',  wave: 'pulse', vol: .07, on: false, notes: 'E5 . C5 . A4 . C5 E5 . G5 . E5 . C5 . . | F5 . C5 . A4 . C5 F5 . A5 . F5 . E5 . .' }\n] };\n```\n\nEach song needs at least 16 bars of material (A/B sections, a breakdown) so that a 3-minute race doesn't drone.\n\n**SFX** (`audio.define` voices, plus our own WebAudio graphs on the effects bus where a voice can't do it). These\nnames are referenced by events (§2.5):\n\n| Group | Sounds |\n| --- | --- |\n| UI | `ui_move` (short pulse blip), `ui_ok` (two-tone up), `ui_back` (down), `ui_locked` (buzz), `ui_tab` (click) |\n| Race | `count_beep`, `count_go` (chord), `lap` (chime), `final_lap` (a rising sting), `finish` (fanfare), `wrongway` (siren blip), `pos_up` / `pos_down` (tiny arps) |\n| Craft | engine hum (continuous, below), `boost_pad` (whoosh plus a pitch sweep), `pickup_roll` (a ticking arp), `weapon_pad` (sparkle), `airbrake` (filtered noise hiss, looped while braking), `sideshift` (puff), `roll` (a whirr), `roll_boost`, `botch`, `land_soft`, `land_hard` (thud plus clank), `wall_hit` (metal bang, pitch by impact), `scrape` (looped band-passed noise, volume by speed), `bump`, `pit_charge` (looped rising tone), `low_shield` (beep every 0.8 s), `explode` (noise boom plus a sub drop), `eliminated`, `respawn`, `rescue` (drone whine) |\n| Weapons | `swarm_fire`, `seeker_lock` (beeps faster to a solid tone), `seeker_fire`, `mine_drop`, `cannon_fire`, `rail_charge` (a rising whine), `rail_fire` (crack plus a long zap), `tremor` (sub rumble), `bulwark_on/off`, `autopilot_on/off`, `nitro`, `siphon` (a crackling loop), `absorb` (a reverse whoosh with a chime), `hit_light`, `hit_heavy` |\n\n**Engine hum.** The four nearest craft each get a persistent graph: saw + detuned square → lowpass → gain →\nStereoPanner → the effects bus.\n- `f = 48 + 120·(v/top)` Hz with a thrust wobble.\n- Cutoff `500 + 2500·(v/top)` (+1500 in boost).\n- Others: volume by distance (1/(1 + d/800 u)), Doppler pitch `×clamp(1 + vRel/6000, .85, 1.15)`, pan by the screen\n  x of `world.project`.\n- The player's hum is louder and centred.\n- In a split screen: player 1 pans left, player 2 right.\n- All of it is muted on pause, on `game.audio.muted`, and on the hub's `end`.\n\n**Gibberish voice (Animalese/Simlish style), `SN.Voice.say(text, voice)`:**\n- Every word is turned into syllables seeded by the word's hash, so the same word always sounds the same (\"SEEKER\"\n  is always \"see-kra\").\n- Syllable count = `max(1, round(letters / 2.6))`.\n- Each syllable is a consonant burst (noise, band-passed at 2–5 kHz, 18 ms; picked by the word's letters) followed by\n  a vowel: a saw at `f0` through two band-pass \"formants\" `[F1, F2]` from a 5-vowel table (a: 800/1200, e: 400/2000,\n  i: 300/2300, o: 450/800, u: 325/700), lasting `70–110 ms / speed`.\n- Pitch: per-syllable jitter ±8 %; down 12 % at a full stop, up 18 % at \"?\", +10 % and louder at \"!\".\n- Breathiness: 15 % noise.\n- `say()` returns its duration. Subtitles and dialog pages wait on it. Headless, it is computed without sound.\n\n| Voice | f0 | Speed | Use |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ANNOUNCER (race control's \"ORACLE\") | 205 Hz | 0.85 | calm, slightly ring-modulated (×0.4 at 60 Hz) |\n| pilots | 95–240 Hz | 1.0–1.3 | per pilot: radio banter, podium |\n| principals | 110–190 Hz | 0.9 | briefings |\n| KAI-ZERO | 140 Hz | 1.1 | bitcrushed (a WaveShaper step curve) |\n\n`E.Dialog` boxes use `voice: null` (no letter blips) and call `SN.Voice.say` per page.\n\n**Announcer lines** (each spoken as gibberish **and** shown as a subtitle, Settings → Subtitles):","numLines":160,"startLine":925,"totalLines":2075}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FKsacmrwzzdkGBKqpd1oWG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
