{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3GDM3v5pFMPNRCNypm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QpAACwXoSaCdXRkSQsoyib","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","offset":1084,"limit":140},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8988,"cache_read_input_tokens":531727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8988},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"c1073b86-f36e-4ed0-ab8d-aefc4501c413","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:43:32.183Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3GD2D1z8fzKkyXS2E6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QpAACwXoSaCdXRkSQsoyib":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","offset":1084,"limit":140}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QpAACwXoSaCdXRkSQsoyib","type":"tool_result","content":"1084\t**Announcer lines** (each spoken as gibberish **and** shown as a subtitle, Settings → Subtitles):\n1085\t- every weapon name on pickup;\n1086\t- \"THREE\", \"TWO\", \"ONE\", \"GO\";\n1087\t- \"FINAL LAP\", \"PERFECT START\", \"BARREL ROLL\", \"SNIPED\", \"ELIMINATED\", \"WRONG WAY\", \"NEW LAP RECORD\";\n1088\t- \"ZONE {n}\", \"OVERCLOCKED\", \"RACE OVER\", \"WINNER\".\n1089\t\n1090\t### 3.11 Narrative and writing style (`09-data-story.js`)\n1091\t\n1092\tThe source's register: clipped, corporate, cool, a little ironic. It sounds like a league that sells speed like\n1093\tmineral water. Race control speaks in capitals and in rules. Teams speak like brochures. Pilots are terse and\n1094\tcompetitive. Sponsors are absurd and deadpan. No melodrama, no jokes that wink at the player. Everything is\n1095\toriginal: invented league, teams, people and brands.\n1096\t\n1097\t- **The league:** the **Hoverline Championship**, Season 2161, run by the **Hoverline Authority** (\"THE AUTHORITY\").\n1098\t  Its race-control intelligence is called **ORACLE**.\n1099\t  - Announcement style: `AUTHORITY NOTICE 0417 — ROOKIE LICENCE GRANTED. CLASS: SPARK. GRAVITY: OPTIONAL.`\n1100\t- **Team copy** (one line each, §4.1). Example:\n1101\t  `HAMMERHEAD HEAVY INDUSTRIES builds cranes, bridges and the occasional champion. All three survive impact.`\n1102\t- **Track copy.** Example: `PORT SOLENNE. Old stone, new money. The harbour lights are on a sponsorship contract.`\n1103\t- **Sponsor boards** (canvas textures, §4.6):\n1104\t  - `QWIK-FUEL — FILL UP. FALL UP.`\n1105\t  - `OKTA NOODLE — EAT AT 600 KM/H`\n1106\t  - `HALCYON BANK — YOUR MONEY, FASTER`\n1107\t  - `DO NOT LOOK DIRECTLY AT THE FUTURE`\n1108\t  - `AXON AIR — BREATHE PREMIUM`\n1109\t  - `VANTA PAINTS — DARKER THAN NOTHING`\n1110\t- **Story beats (the Season).** You are a test pilot signed to a race seat with your chosen team. Your team principal\n1111\t  briefs you. The rival collective NULL//SET (pilot KAI-ZERO) needles you. The Authority watches. The beats are listed\n1112\t  per event in §4.5.\n1113\t\n1114\t  The arc:\n1115\t  1. you are a rookie;\n1116\t  2. you get noticed;\n1117\t  3. a sponsor ultimatum, and NULL//SET's overclocking scandal (which is why OVERCLOCK trials exist);\n1118\t  4. the STORM class promotion;\n1119\t  5. the Grand Prix showdown;\n1120\t  6. champion, and SINGULARITY unlocked, with a deadpan Authority sign-off.\n1121\t\n1122\t### 3.12 Season, progression, saves (`08-data-season.js`, `78-season-ui.js`)\n1123\t\n1124\t- **Tiers:**\n1125\t  - Tier 1 (SPARK) is open from the start.\n1126\t  - Tier 2 (FLARE) opens with 3 medals in tier 1, which also **unlocks the FLARE class** everywhere.\n1127\t  - Tier 3 (STORM) opens with 3 medals in tier 2 and unlocks STORM.\n1128\t  - The GRAND PRIX opens with both tier-3 events at bronze or better.\n1129\t  - Winning the GP (any medal) **unlocks SINGULARITY**, the CHAMPION livery (gold trim on every team's craft, a\n1130\t    toggle in team select) and the ending.\n1131\t- Events can be replayed to improve a medal. The best medal is kept.\n1132\t- **Saves:** `game.saves` autosaves after every event and GP race. `game.saves.write` returns\n1133\t  `{ data, place: 'SEASON 2161', level: 'TIER 2' }`:\n1134\t\n1135\t  ```js\n1136\t  data = { v: 1, medals: { [eventId]: 'gold'|'silver'|'bronze' }, gp: { round, points: {pilotId: n}, done }, unlocked: { classes: [...], champion: bool },\n1137\t           seen: { [briefingId]: true }, records: { 'track/cls/mode': { ms, pilot } }, ghosts: { 'track/cls/mode': base64 }, team, pilot }\n1138\t  ```\n1139\t\n1140\t  `menu: { saves: true }` is **not** used (no save points). CONTINUE on the main menu loads `saves.latest()`. In a hub\n1141\t  session, storage is the hub's in-memory one, so nothing persists. That is expected.\n1142\t\n1143\t### 3.13 Replays, ghosts, records (`45-replay.js`)\n1144\t\n1145\t- **Replay** = re-simulate from the race's `{ seed, …, tune, frames }` (§2.8). The `replay` scene runs the sim at\n1146\t  `timeScale` 1, 2 or 4 (R1/L1, or a click on the speed chip) with the TV director (△ cycles: TV, chase, cockpit,\n1147\t  heli). A **click on any craft in the picture** (a hit test via `world.project` within 18 px) follows that craft.\n1148\t  ✕ pauses, ○ exits. On the last frame, assert that `R.hash()` equals the recorded hash. In dev builds, show \"REPLAY\n1149\t  DESYNC\" if not (a test guarantees it doesn't happen).\n1150\t- **Ghosts** (TIME TRIAL, HOT LAP): record the player's `(s, u, h, yaw relative to the track, roll)` at 20 Hz,\n1151\t  quantised to Int16, base64 in the save. Play back interpolated, as a translucent craft. The ghost never collides.\n1152\t  Save it only on a new best.\n1153\t- **Records:** best race and best lap per track/class/mode, with the pilot name. The NEW RECORD callout plus the\n1154\t  announcer.\n1155\t\n1156\t### 3.14 Attract mode (`85-attract.js`)\n1157\t\n1158\t- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the title or any front-end screen (`input.anyPressed()`, any `move()` above the\n1159\t  dead zone, any mouse move or click, or any key). The clock resets on input. It runs on touch-only devices too.\n1160\t- **Playlist** (loops; each segment 25–40 s, loading the track world in between behind a \"DEMO\" card):\n1161\t  1. a SPARK race at Port Solenne with 8 AI, weapons forced in rotation (all 10 weapons appear across the loop), a\n1162\t     barrel roll on the jump;\n1163\t  2. a STORM SNIPEOUT at Meridian Stack, with eliminations and respawns, and the Stack Drop;\n1164\t  3. OVERCLOCK at Karakum Spire, an AI from zone 1 jumping to zone 14 at one zone per 2 s, skin and music climbing;\n1165\t  4. a FLARE race at Borealis Vault, the Vault jump and the ice tunnel;\n1166\t  5. a 6 s title card with the logo and \"PRESS START\".\n1167\t\n1168\t  Each segment uses the TV director plus occasional chase and cockpit cuts.\n1169\t- **Cheats allowed:** infinite energy, forced pickups, no rescues, AI aggression 1.5.\n1170\t- **Overlay:** a \"DEMO\" chip at the top centre, the logo small at the top left, and \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" blinking at the\n1171\t  bottom (the glyph of the last device). The HUD stays minimal: position list and weapon callouts, so the features\n1172\t  read.\n1173\t- **Exit:** **any** input (key, pad button, stick, mouse button, a click, a touch) returns to the title within one\n1174\t  step. The input is consumed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it doesn't also select anything. The race world stays loaded\n1175\t  for the title.\n1176\t\n1177\t### 3.15 Dev mode and live tuning (`80-dev.js`, `SN.Tune` in `00-core.js`)\n1178\t\n1179\t- **Reach:** the pause menu item **Dev mode**. It is present in every race mode except hub sessions. Front-end\n1180\t  screens get it through OPTIONS ▸ DEV MODE, so it is reachable without a race too. The panel opens over the paused\n1181\t  game. ○ or Esc closes it back to the pause menu, and Options resumes. Controller, keyboard and mouse all work (the\n1182\t  §3.9 widget kit). Tabs switch with L1/R1, Q/E, or a click on a tab.\n1183\t- **Tune registry:** `SN.Tune.def(key, { def, min, max, step, label, group })`. Read values with `SN.Tune.T[key]`.\n1184\t  `SN.Tune.reset(key?)` restores one or all defaults. Values live in memory for the session (a \"RESET ALL TO\n1185\t  DEFAULTS\" button is always visible). Every replay snapshots them.\n1186\t\n1187\t| Tab | Contents |\n1188\t| --- | --- |\n1189\t| **CHEATS** | God mode (no damage) · Infinite weapon · Give weapon ◀ name ▶ (applies on ✕) · AI weapons off · Freeze AI · Ghost AI (no collisions) · Refill energy · Energy to 10 % · Skip to final lap · Win now (finish 1st / max points / zone +10) · Eliminate all AI · Unlock everything · Reset season progress (asks first, in-panel) |\n1190\t| **TUNING** (live sliders, ◀ ▶ adjust, hold to speed up, mouse drag on the bar, a reset ↺ per row, RESET ALL) | **Handling:** thrustMul 1 [0.5–2], topSpeedMul 1 [0.6–1.6], dragMul 1 [0.5–2], steerRate 1.9 [0.8–3.5], steerResponse 9 [2–20], gripMul 1 [0.3–2], airbrakeYaw 1.4 [0–3], airbrakeDrag 0.9 [0–2], gripMaxMul 1 [0.4–2], slipMax 35° [10–60], scrubK 0.35 [0–1], sideShiftSpeed 768 [0–1500], shiftDecay 12 [4–30]. **Hover:** hoverHeight 14 [6–30], hoverStiffness 220 [60–600], hoverDamping 28 [5–60], magnetPull 1800 [600–4000], airGravity 640 [200–1500], pitchEffect 1 [0–2]. **Walls & energy:** wallBounce 0.35 [0–1], wallFriction 0.25 [0–1], wallDamage 1 [0–3], pitRecharge 25 [0–100], rollCost 10 [0–30], rollBoost 1.2 [1–1.6]. **Pads & weapons:** padBoost 1.25 [1–1.8], padBoostTime 0.9 [0.2–2.5], weaponDamageMul 1 [0–3], absorbMul 1 [0–3], pickupLuck 1 [0–2]. **AI:** aiSkill 1 [0.5–1.2], aiRubberBand 1 [0–2], aiAggression 1 [0–2]. **Camera:** camDistance 150 [60–300], camHeight 46 [10–120], camFov 72 [50–100], camFovBoost 16 [0–40], camLag 8 [1–20] |\n1191\t| **WORLD** | Time scale (0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2) · Teleport: lap position % slider + GO · Free camera · Overclock zone +1 · Weather on/off · HUD on/off · Debug overlay (centre line, slice frames, racing line coloured by target speed, craft collision spheres, pad rectangles, AI targets, camera spots) |\n1192\t| **INFO** | live: s, u, h, p, speed (u/s and km/h), energy, lap, sector, position, airborne time, slice index, surface kind, seed, `R.hash()`, World3D backend and `world.stats` (calls, tris, ms), steps per second |\n1193\t\n1194\t### 3.16 Multiplayer: local split screen and AI Hub sessions\n1195\t\n1196\t**Local (the game on its own): VERSUS for 2 players on one machine.**\n1197\t- On the VERSUS screen, `game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`: player 2 presses Start on another pad, or 2 on the keyboard.\n1198\t- With two on the keyboard, the engine splits it with `Input.halfKeys` in our preset order (§3.9):\n1199\t  - **P1:** W/S pitch, A/D steer, F thrust, G fire, H absorb, R/T airbrakes, Y camera, V/B side-shift;\n1200\t  - **P2:** ↑/↓ pitch, ←/→ steer, `.` thrust, `/` fire, `,` absorb, L/`;` airbrakes, `'` camera, K/N side-shift.\n1201\t\n1202\t  Show both layouts on the join screen with keycap glyphs.\n1203\t- Both pick teams in turn, then choose RACE or SNIPEOUT, class and track. Split rows, with a compact HUD per\n1204\t  viewport.\n1205\t- Each player's prompts use their own device (`players[i].label()`). A pause says \"P2 PAUSED\" (engine).\n1206\t\n1207\t**AI Hub (`90-hub.js`): mode `ghost`**, following the protocol (`lib/hub/README.md`, client 1.4.0). Everyone races the\n1208\tsame seeded event on their own device and sees the others as ghosts.\n1209\t1. **Tags** in `<head>` (§2.3): players `1-4`, mode `ghost`, minutes `3`, goal and howto ≤ 60/80 characters.\n1210\t2. **`AIHub.active`** → the boot goes straight to the `session` scene: no title, menus, attract or prompts. The engine\n1211\t   options for the session: `autoPause: false`, the race `pausable: false`, `menu.quit: false`.\n1212\t3. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If `null`, run the game normally.\n1213\t4. **The event:**\n1214\t   - track = `['solenne', 'karakum', 'meridian', 'borealis'][floor(AIHub.rng('event')() * 4)]`;\n1215\t   - class FLARE, 3 laps;\n1216\t   - race seed = `floor(AIHub.rng('race')() * 2^32)`;\n1217\t   - each human's team by seat (`['kestrel', 'soratek', 'volta', 'caldera'][seat]`), livery accent = seat colour;\n1218\t   - grid: the humans take slots by seat at the back of the grid (slots 5–8), and AI fill slots 1–4 plus any free\n1219\t     slots (8 − N AI);\n1220\t   - every copy simulates its own craft plus the AI. The other humans are **ghosts**: drawn from messages, never\n1221\t     collided with or targeted.\n1222\t5. **Own card** (`card: true`): the session scene shows a 3D grid shot of the chosen track with the players' craft\n1223\t   lined up in seat colours, the names, the ready ticks from the `card` event, the time left (`left`), the goal, and"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"83453767-a3e9-4d3d-9280-df073a852270","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:43:32.194Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"**Announcer lines** (each spoken as gibberish **and** shown as a subtitle, Settings → Subtitles):\n- every weapon name on pickup;\n- \"THREE\", \"TWO\", \"ONE\", \"GO\";\n- \"FINAL LAP\", \"PERFECT START\", \"BARREL ROLL\", \"SNIPED\", \"ELIMINATED\", \"WRONG WAY\", \"NEW LAP RECORD\";\n- \"ZONE {n}\", \"OVERCLOCKED\", \"RACE OVER\", \"WINNER\".\n\n### 3.11 Narrative and writing style (`09-data-story.js`)\n\nThe source's register: clipped, corporate, cool, a little ironic. It sounds like a league that sells speed like\nmineral water. Race control speaks in capitals and in rules. Teams speak like brochures. Pilots are terse and\ncompetitive. Sponsors are absurd and deadpan. No melodrama, no jokes that wink at the player. Everything is\noriginal: invented league, teams, people and brands.\n\n- **The league:** the **Hoverline Championship**, Season 2161, run by the **Hoverline Authority** (\"THE AUTHORITY\").\n  Its race-control intelligence is called **ORACLE**.\n  - Announcement style: `AUTHORITY NOTICE 0417 — ROOKIE LICENCE GRANTED. CLASS: SPARK. GRAVITY: OPTIONAL.`\n- **Team copy** (one line each, §4.1). Example:\n  `HAMMERHEAD HEAVY INDUSTRIES builds cranes, bridges and the occasional champion. All three survive impact.`\n- **Track copy.** Example: `PORT SOLENNE. Old stone, new money. The harbour lights are on a sponsorship contract.`\n- **Sponsor boards** (canvas textures, §4.6):\n  - `QWIK-FUEL — FILL UP. FALL UP.`\n  - `OKTA NOODLE — EAT AT 600 KM/H`\n  - `HALCYON BANK — YOUR MONEY, FASTER`\n  - `DO NOT LOOK DIRECTLY AT THE FUTURE`\n  - `AXON AIR — BREATHE PREMIUM`\n  - `VANTA PAINTS — DARKER THAN NOTHING`\n- **Story beats (the Season).** You are a test pilot signed to a race seat with your chosen team. Your team principal\n  briefs you. The rival collective NULL//SET (pilot KAI-ZERO) needles you. The Authority watches. The beats are listed\n  per event in §4.5.\n\n  The arc:\n  1. you are a rookie;\n  2. you get noticed;\n  3. a sponsor ultimatum, and NULL//SET's overclocking scandal (which is why OVERCLOCK trials exist);\n  4. the STORM class promotion;\n  5. the Grand Prix showdown;\n  6. champion, and SINGULARITY unlocked, with a deadpan Authority sign-off.\n\n### 3.12 Season, progression, saves (`08-data-season.js`, `78-season-ui.js`)\n\n- **Tiers:**\n  - Tier 1 (SPARK) is open from the start.\n  - Tier 2 (FLARE) opens with 3 medals in tier 1, which also **unlocks the FLARE class** everywhere.\n  - Tier 3 (STORM) opens with 3 medals in tier 2 and unlocks STORM.\n  - The GRAND PRIX opens with both tier-3 events at bronze or better.\n  - Winning the GP (any medal) **unlocks SINGULARITY**, the CHAMPION livery (gold trim on every team's craft, a\n    toggle in team select) and the ending.\n- Events can be replayed to improve a medal. The best medal is kept.\n- **Saves:** `game.saves` autosaves after every event and GP race. `game.saves.write` returns\n  `{ data, place: 'SEASON 2161', level: 'TIER 2' }`:\n\n  ```js\n  data = { v: 1, medals: { [eventId]: 'gold'|'silver'|'bronze' }, gp: { round, points: {pilotId: n}, done }, unlocked: { classes: [...], champion: bool },\n           seen: { [briefingId]: true }, records: { 'track/cls/mode': { ms, pilot } }, ghosts: { 'track/cls/mode': base64 }, team, pilot }\n  ```\n\n  `menu: { saves: true }` is **not** used (no save points). CONTINUE on the main menu loads `saves.latest()`. In a hub\n  session, storage is the hub's in-memory one, so nothing persists. That is expected.\n\n### 3.13 Replays, ghosts, records (`45-replay.js`)\n\n- **Replay** = re-simulate from the race's `{ seed, …, tune, frames }` (§2.8). The `replay` scene runs the sim at\n  `timeScale` 1, 2 or 4 (R1/L1, or a click on the speed chip) with the TV director (△ cycles: TV, chase, cockpit,\n  heli). A **click on any craft in the picture** (a hit test via `world.project` within 18 px) follows that craft.\n  ✕ pauses, ○ exits. On the last frame, assert that `R.hash()` equals the recorded hash. In dev builds, show \"REPLAY\n  DESYNC\" if not (a test guarantees it doesn't happen).\n- **Ghosts** (TIME TRIAL, HOT LAP): record the player's `(s, u, h, yaw relative to the track, roll)` at 20 Hz,\n  quantised to Int16, base64 in the save. Play back interpolated, as a translucent craft. The ghost never collides.\n  Save it only on a new best.\n- **Records:** best race and best lap per track/class/mode, with the pilot name. The NEW RECORD callout plus the\n  announcer.\n\n### 3.14 Attract mode (`85-attract.js`)\n\n- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the title or any front-end screen (`input.anyPressed()`, any `move()` above the\n  dead zone, any mouse move or click, or any key). The clock resets on input. It runs on touch-only devices too.\n- **Playlist** (loops; each segment 25–40 s, loading the track world in between behind a \"DEMO\" card):\n  1. a SPARK race at Port Solenne with 8 AI, weapons forced in rotation (all 10 weapons appear across the loop), a\n     barrel roll on the jump;\n  2. a STORM SNIPEOUT at Meridian Stack, with eliminations and respawns, and the Stack Drop;\n  3. OVERCLOCK at Karakum Spire, an AI from zone 1 jumping to zone 14 at one zone per 2 s, skin and music climbing;\n  4. a FLARE race at Borealis Vault, the Vault jump and the ice tunnel;\n  5. a 6 s title card with the logo and \"PRESS START\".\n\n  Each segment uses the TV director plus occasional chase and cockpit cuts.\n- **Cheats allowed:** infinite energy, forced pickups, no rescues, AI aggression 1.5.\n- **Overlay:** a \"DEMO\" chip at the top centre, the logo small at the top left, and \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" blinking at the\n  bottom (the glyph of the last device). The HUD stays minimal: position list and weapon callouts, so the features\n  read.\n- **Exit:** **any** input (key, pad button, stick, mouse button, a click, a touch) returns to the title within one\n  step. The input is consumed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it doesn't also select anything. The race world stays loaded\n  for the title.\n\n### 3.15 Dev mode and live tuning (`80-dev.js`, `SN.Tune` in `00-core.js`)\n\n- **Reach:** the pause menu item **Dev mode**. It is present in every race mode except hub sessions. Front-end\n  screens get it through OPTIONS ▸ DEV MODE, so it is reachable without a race too. The panel opens over the paused\n  game. ○ or Esc closes it back to the pause menu, and Options resumes. Controller, keyboard and mouse all work (the\n  §3.9 widget kit). Tabs switch with L1/R1, Q/E, or a click on a tab.\n- **Tune registry:** `SN.Tune.def(key, { def, min, max, step, label, group })`. Read values with `SN.Tune.T[key]`.\n  `SN.Tune.reset(key?)` restores one or all defaults. Values live in memory for the session (a \"RESET ALL TO\n  DEFAULTS\" button is always visible). Every replay snapshots them.\n\n| Tab | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| **CHEATS** | God mode (no damage) · Infinite weapon · Give weapon ◀ name ▶ (applies on ✕) · AI weapons off · Freeze AI · Ghost AI (no collisions) · Refill energy · Energy to 10 % · Skip to final lap · Win now (finish 1st / max points / zone +10) · Eliminate all AI · Unlock everything · Reset season progress (asks first, in-panel) |\n| **TUNING** (live sliders, ◀ ▶ adjust, hold to speed up, mouse drag on the bar, a reset ↺ per row, RESET ALL) | **Handling:** thrustMul 1 [0.5–2], topSpeedMul 1 [0.6–1.6], dragMul 1 [0.5–2], steerRate 1.9 [0.8–3.5], steerResponse 9 [2–20], gripMul 1 [0.3–2], airbrakeYaw 1.4 [0–3], airbrakeDrag 0.9 [0–2], gripMaxMul 1 [0.4–2], slipMax 35° [10–60], scrubK 0.35 [0–1], sideShiftSpeed 768 [0–1500], shiftDecay 12 [4–30]. **Hover:** hoverHeight 14 [6–30], hoverStiffness 220 [60–600], hoverDamping 28 [5–60], magnetPull 1800 [600–4000], airGravity 640 [200–1500], pitchEffect 1 [0–2]. **Walls & energy:** wallBounce 0.35 [0–1], wallFriction 0.25 [0–1], wallDamage 1 [0–3], pitRecharge 25 [0–100], rollCost 10 [0–30], rollBoost 1.2 [1–1.6]. **Pads & weapons:** padBoost 1.25 [1–1.8], padBoostTime 0.9 [0.2–2.5], weaponDamageMul 1 [0–3], absorbMul 1 [0–3], pickupLuck 1 [0–2]. **AI:** aiSkill 1 [0.5–1.2], aiRubberBand 1 [0–2], aiAggression 1 [0–2]. **Camera:** camDistance 150 [60–300], camHeight 46 [10–120], camFov 72 [50–100], camFovBoost 16 [0–40], camLag 8 [1–20] |\n| **WORLD** | Time scale (0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2) · Teleport: lap position % slider + GO · Free camera · Overclock zone +1 · Weather on/off · HUD on/off · Debug overlay (centre line, slice frames, racing line coloured by target speed, craft collision spheres, pad rectangles, AI targets, camera spots) |\n| **INFO** | live: s, u, h, p, speed (u/s and km/h), energy, lap, sector, position, airborne time, slice index, surface kind, seed, `R.hash()`, World3D backend and `world.stats` (calls, tris, ms), steps per second |\n\n### 3.16 Multiplayer: local split screen and AI Hub sessions\n\n**Local (the game on its own): VERSUS for 2 players on one machine.**\n- On the VERSUS screen, `game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`: player 2 presses Start on another pad, or 2 on the keyboard.\n- With two on the keyboard, the engine splits it with `Input.halfKeys` in our preset order (§3.9):\n  - **P1:** W/S pitch, A/D steer, F thrust, G fire, H absorb, R/T airbrakes, Y camera, V/B side-shift;\n  - **P2:** ↑/↓ pitch, ←/→ steer, `.` thrust, `/` fire, `,` absorb, L/`;` airbrakes, `'` camera, K/N side-shift.\n\n  Show both layouts on the join screen with keycap glyphs.\n- Both pick teams in turn, then choose RACE or SNIPEOUT, class and track. Split rows, with a compact HUD per\n  viewport.\n- Each player's prompts use their own device (`players[i].label()`). A pause says \"P2 PAUSED\" (engine).\n\n**AI Hub (`90-hub.js`): mode `ghost`**, following the protocol (`lib/hub/README.md`, client 1.4.0). Everyone races the\nsame seeded event on their own device and sees the others as ghosts.\n1. **Tags** in `<head>` (§2.3): players `1-4`, mode `ghost`, minutes `3`, goal and howto ≤ 60/80 characters.\n2. **`AIHub.active`** → the boot goes straight to the `session` scene: no title, menus, attract or prompts. The engine\n   options for the session: `autoPause: false`, the race `pausable: false`, `menu.quit: false`.\n3. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If `null`, run the game normally.\n4. **The event:**\n   - track = `['solenne', 'karakum', 'meridian', 'borealis'][floor(AIHub.rng('event')() * 4)]`;\n   - class FLARE, 3 laps;\n   - race seed = `floor(AIHub.rng('race')() * 2^32)`;\n   - each human's team by seat (`['kestrel', 'soratek', 'volta', 'caldera'][seat]`), livery accent = seat colour;\n   - grid: the humans take slots by seat at the back of the grid (slots 5–8), and AI fill slots 1–4 plus any free\n     slots (8 − N AI);\n   - every copy simulates its own craft plus the AI. The other humans are **ghosts**: drawn from messages, never\n     collided with or targeted.\n5. **Own card** (`card: true`): the session scene shows a 3D grid shot of the chosen track with the players' craft\n   lined up in seat colours, the names, the ready ticks from the `card` event, the time left (`left`), the goal, and","numLines":140,"startLine":1084,"totalLines":2075}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QpAACwXoSaCdXRkSQsoyib","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
