{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014mXYhukzBSH4a3cZF85yGg","type":"tool_result","content":"1226\t   this player's controls (the glyphs of the device seen so far, keyboard by default).\n1227\t   - **Ready:** Enter, ✕ or a tap/click on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n1228\t   - **More time:** △, M, or a tap/click on MORE TIME → `AIHub.answer('more')`; pressing again takes it back.\n1229\t   - No `Math.random` on the card (use `AIHub.rng('card')` if needed). No menus or choices.\n1230\t6. Call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as the world is built and warm (boot plus the track loading), with no key press.\n1231\t7. **`start`**: the countdown lights follow `AIHub.time()` (−3000 → 0 ms), and the launch revs work. Racing begins\n1232\t   when `AIHub.time() ≥ 0`. The race clock is `AIHub.time()`.\n1233\t8. **Ghost traffic:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', p, u, h, y, r, v, lap, fin }, { reliable: false })` at 10 Hz (well under\n1234\t   20/s), plus `{ t: 'done', ms }` reliable on finishing.\n1235\t   - On `message`, update that ghost: interpolate toward the latest, 0.1 s behind. Draw it as a ghost craft (§3.7)\n1236\t     with the name in the seat colour, and add it to the HUD standings.\n1237\t   - On `leave`, remove it.\n1238\t9. **Progress:** about once a second, `AIHub.progress({ score: Math.round(p / 16), label: 'LAP 2/3 · 3RD' })`.\n1239\t10. **Result:**\n1240\t    - on finishing: `AIHub.result({ time: finishMs, stats: { 'Best lap': '0:41.22', 'Place vs AI': '2nd' },\n1241\t      awards: [...] })`;\n1242\t    - eliminations respawn in sessions, so everyone can finish;\n1243\t    - on `time-up`, if not finished: `AIHub.result({ score: Math.round(p / 16) })` at once.\n1244\t11. **`end`:** stop the sim, stop all input (ignore `game.input`), stop music, engine hums and SFX, and show \"ROUND\n1245\t    OVER\" with the standings from the event. The hub removes the page.\n1246\t12. **Rules:** network only through the hub (the CDN module loads are the game's own files); no `alert`, `confirm`,\n1247\t    `prompt` or `window.open` (none anywhere in the game); no chat or custom names. Restart and quit do nothing in a\n1248\t    session (the items are hidden).\n1249\t\n1250\t### 3.17 Settings: the game's own, beside the engine's standard ones\n1251\t\n1252\t`new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [...] } })`, groups `Game` and `Display`:\n1253\t- **Difficulty:** Easy / Normal / Hard.\n1254\t- **Speed units:** km/h / mph.\n1255\t- **Default camera:** Chase / Far chase / Cockpit.\n1256\t- **HUD size:** Normal / Large (×1.25).\n1257\t- **Subtitles:** on / off. They cover the announcer and radio; dialog boxes are always text.\n1258\t- **Announcer voice:** on / off.\n1259\t- **Speed lines:** on / off.\n1260\t- **Neon glow** (`bloom`): on / off.\n1261\t- **Picture** (`picture3d`): PIXELS (the engine's native default) / BALANCED / **HD**. HD is World3D's `'full'`.\n1262\t- **Shadows** (`shadows3d`): on / off.\n1263\t- **Filter** (`filter3d`): None / Comic cel / Pixel.\n1264\t- **Button symbols:** PlayStation (default) / Xbox. This is the engine's `glyphs`, moved to Display (§2.7.1).\n1265\t\n1266\tWorld3D reads `picture3d`, `shadows3d` and `filter3d` by those keys. Define them ourselves (same keys, values and\n1267\tlabels), because `E.World3D.SETTINGS` does not exist yet when `new E.Game` runs (§2.3). The engine provides the rest:\n1268\tvolume, music, effects, reduce motion, shake, flashes, full screen, frame rate, and the Controls screen (rebinding,\n1269\tdead zone, vibration).\n1270\t\n1271\t### 3.18 About / Credits and the exit interview (`11-data-about.js`)\n1272\t\n1273\t`SN.ABOUT` is the single source for the **About / Credits** screen (OPTIONS ▸ ABOUT, and after the ending credits) and\n1274\tfor `tools/exit-interview.mjs`, which writes `../exit-interview.json` in exactly TASK.md's shape and checks it parses.\n1275\t\n1276\tThe screen pages (L1/R1), each page big-type and short:\n1277\t1. **SOURCE INFORMATION:** every TASK.md field, \"unknown\" where it can't be confirmed. Planned values:\n1278\t   - Date: 2026-11-03 17:47:28\n1279\t   - Source: Wipeout HD (Studio Liverpool / Sony, 2008)\n1280\t   - Plan: PLAN.md\n1281\t   - Genre and perspective: anti-gravity combat racing; third-person chase camera with cockpit view and trackside TV\n1282\t     cameras\n1283\t   - Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine + my-3D2dge 3D v0.85.2, three.js r182 (WebGPU/WebGL 2), Rapier 0.19.3,\n1284\t     AI Hub client 1.4.0\n1285\t   - Art direction: the engine's native style (pixel-resolution 3D, toon/lambert light, pixel HUD and fonts) plus new\n1286\t     procedural craft, tracks and neon\n1287\t   - Animation: the engine's rigs and tweens, plus procedural craft animation\n1288\t   - Audio: synthesized music, SFX and gibberish voices\n1289\t   - Online: AI Hub ghost sessions; local split screen\n1290\t   - Testing; research; environment; model; usage\n1291\t2. **TESTING FEEDBACK:** the 4 answers.\n1292\t3. **ENGINE FEEDBACK:** the 6 answers, including the §2.7 changes.\n1293\t4. **PROMPT FEEDBACK:** the 4 answers.\n1294\t5. **CREDITS:**\n1295\t   - \"Snipeout HD. An original game inspired by Wipeout HD (not affiliated with Sony Interactive Entertainment).\"\n1296\t   - Engine credits (my-3D2dge, three.js MIT, Rapier Apache-2.0), \"all music, sound and voices synthesized in code\",\n1297\t     \"built by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5\".\n1298\t   - The fictional teams and artists, with a note that they are fictional.\n1299\t\n1300\tThe builder fills in the feedback answers truthfully at the end of the build (M12). The chat reply repeats them, as\n1301\tTASK.md demands. The `aiHub` block for the exit interview:\n1302\t\n1303\t```json\n1304\t{ \"name\": \"Snipeout HD\", \"tagline\": \"Anti-gravity. Anti-everyone.\",\n1305\t  \"description\": \"An anti-gravity combat racer: thread banked neon tracks at 600 km/h, snipe rivals with ten weapons and survive Overclock. Season, time trials, split screen and AI Hub ghost races.\",\n1306\t  \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"Racing\", \"source\": \"Wipeout HD\", \"series\": \"Wipeout\", \"players\": \"1–4\",\n1307\t  \"controls\": \"Stick or A/D steer · ✕ or W thrust · L2/R2 or Q/E airbrakes · □ or Space fire · ○ or Shift absorb\",\n1308\t  \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"racing\", \"sci-fi\", \"vehicles\", \"arcade\", \"versus\"] }\n1309\t```\n1310\t\n1311\t---\n1312\t\n1313\t## 4. Content\n1314\t\n1315\t### 4.1 Teams, craft, pilots, principals (`05-data-teams.js`)\n1316\t\n1317\tStats run 1–10 (§3.2 turns them into physics). The totals are close (22–24). NULL//SET trades shield for speed, which\n1318\tmakes it the rival.\n1319\t\n1320\t| Team (base) | SPD | THR | HND | SHD | Livery: primary / secondary / accent / engine glow | Craft and silhouette | One-line copy |\n1321\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1322\t| **KESTREL DYNAMICS** (Oslo) | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | `#f2f5f8` / `#29c8e8` / `#1a2a4a` / `#7af0ff` | **KD-9 FJORD:** a dart hull, swept delta wings, twin canted tail fins, 2 engines | \"Precision is a form of courage. Kestrel has been brave since 2109.\" |\n1323\t| **HAMMERHEAD HEAVY INDUSTRIES** (Lagos) | 6 | 4 | 3 | 9 | `#ff7a1a` / `#2b2d33` / `#ffd23f` / `#ffb347` | **HH ANVIL:** a wide flat slab hull, twin hammerhead nose pods, stub wings, 3 engines | \"Builds cranes, bridges and the occasional champion. All three survive impact.\" |\n1324\t| **SORA-TEK** (Osaka) | 5 | 6 | 9 | 4 | `#f7f7f7` / `#e0213a` / `#16161c` / `#ff5a6e` | **ST TSUBAME:** a narrow needle hull, forward canards, one central fin, long swept wings, 1 large engine | \"Sora-Tek does not turn corners. Corners are informed of a change in direction.\" |\n1325\t| **VOLTA NERO** (Turin) | 9 | 4 | 4 | 5 | `#141418` / `#e8b84a` / `#c8202a` / `#ffd36a` | **VN SAETTA:** a very long needle nose, a big rear-mounted engine, small rear wings, twin low fins | \"Straight lines, beautifully. Everything else, eventually.\" |\n1326\t| **CALDERA SYSTEMS** (Santiago) | 5 | 9 | 5 | 5 | `#d8361c` / `#6a2bd8` / `#24202a` / `#ff6a2a` | **CS VOLCÁN:** a twin-boom catamaran, two big engines on the booms, a centre pilot pod | \"Geothermal engineering. Zero to everything in four seconds.\" |\n1327\t| **NULL//SET** (Berlin; a collective) | 8 | 7 | 5 | 3 | `#0b0b0e` / `#6aff3a` / `#ff2a8a` / `#6aff3a` | **N//S GHOSTLINE:** a faceted stealth wedge, no fins, 2 flat slot engines | \"No sponsor. No logo. No comment.\" |\n1328\t\n1329\tCraft geometry parameters (ShipKit). Lengths in u; the full length is 96 u for all designs, so they share collision.\n1330\t\n1331\t| Craft | Hull sections (half-width w, height h at 0 / 20 / 40 / 60 / 80 / 100 % of length) | Wings (span, sweep) | Fins | Engines (count, radius) |\n1332\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1333\t| FJORD | w 2/9/14/16/14/10, h 2/6/9/9/8/6 | span 30, sweep 40° | 2 canted 20° | 2 × r5 |\n1334\t| ANVIL | w 10/16/18/18/18/16, h 3/6/7/7/7/6, plus 2 nose pods r5 at ±14 | span 22, sweep 10° | 0 | 3 × r4 |\n1335\t| TSUBAME | w 1/6/10/12/10/8, h 2/5/7/8/7/5, plus canards (span 10 at 25 %) | span 36, sweep 50° | 1 tall | 1 × r7 |\n1336\t| SAETTA | w 1/4/8/12/14/12, h 1/4/6/8/9/8 | span 20, sweep 30° (rear) | 2 low | 1 × r9 |\n1337\t| VOLCÁN | two booms w 6 at ±15, a pod w 7 in the centre (front 70 %) | span 34, straight, joining the booms | 2 on the booms | 2 × r7 |\n1338\t| GHOSTLINE | a faceted wedge: w 4/12/18/20/20/18, h 2/4/6/6/5/3 (flat-shaded facets) | none (the wedge is the wing) | 0 | 2 slots 14 × 3 |\n1339\t\n1340\t**Pilots** (2 per team, 12 in all). Each has two Humanoid rigs: helmeted for the race and podium cards, bare-headed\n1341\tfor portraits. Common rig options: `{ size: 1.3, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth:\n1342\tprimary, coat: secondary, pants: accent, trim: secondary, glove: accent, boot: '#1a1a20' } }` and the helmet\n1343\t`hat: { style: 'helmet', color: secondary }`. Voice `f0` is for §3.10. `skill` is an offset on the difficulty's AI\n1344\tskill.\n1345\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"bc3029ed-bb8b-4bd8-b114-6ecef4177bf8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:43:48.411Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"   this player's controls (the glyphs of the device seen so far, keyboard by default).\n   - **Ready:** Enter, ✕ or a tap/click on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n   - **More time:** △, M, or a tap/click on MORE TIME → `AIHub.answer('more')`; pressing again takes it back.\n   - No `Math.random` on the card (use `AIHub.rng('card')` if needed). No menus or choices.\n6. Call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as the world is built and warm (boot plus the track loading), with no key press.\n7. **`start`**: the countdown lights follow `AIHub.time()` (−3000 → 0 ms), and the launch revs work. Racing begins\n   when `AIHub.time() ≥ 0`. The race clock is `AIHub.time()`.\n8. **Ghost traffic:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', p, u, h, y, r, v, lap, fin }, { reliable: false })` at 10 Hz (well under\n   20/s), plus `{ t: 'done', ms }` reliable on finishing.\n   - On `message`, update that ghost: interpolate toward the latest, 0.1 s behind. Draw it as a ghost craft (§3.7)\n     with the name in the seat colour, and add it to the HUD standings.\n   - On `leave`, remove it.\n9. **Progress:** about once a second, `AIHub.progress({ score: Math.round(p / 16), label: 'LAP 2/3 · 3RD' })`.\n10. **Result:**\n    - on finishing: `AIHub.result({ time: finishMs, stats: { 'Best lap': '0:41.22', 'Place vs AI': '2nd' },\n      awards: [...] })`;\n    - eliminations respawn in sessions, so everyone can finish;\n    - on `time-up`, if not finished: `AIHub.result({ score: Math.round(p / 16) })` at once.\n11. **`end`:** stop the sim, stop all input (ignore `game.input`), stop music, engine hums and SFX, and show \"ROUND\n    OVER\" with the standings from the event. The hub removes the page.\n12. **Rules:** network only through the hub (the CDN module loads are the game's own files); no `alert`, `confirm`,\n    `prompt` or `window.open` (none anywhere in the game); no chat or custom names. Restart and quit do nothing in a\n    session (the items are hidden).\n\n### 3.17 Settings: the game's own, beside the engine's standard ones\n\n`new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [...] } })`, groups `Game` and `Display`:\n- **Difficulty:** Easy / Normal / Hard.\n- **Speed units:** km/h / mph.\n- **Default camera:** Chase / Far chase / Cockpit.\n- **HUD size:** Normal / Large (×1.25).\n- **Subtitles:** on / off. They cover the announcer and radio; dialog boxes are always text.\n- **Announcer voice:** on / off.\n- **Speed lines:** on / off.\n- **Neon glow** (`bloom`): on / off.\n- **Picture** (`picture3d`): PIXELS (the engine's native default) / BALANCED / **HD**. HD is World3D's `'full'`.\n- **Shadows** (`shadows3d`): on / off.\n- **Filter** (`filter3d`): None / Comic cel / Pixel.\n- **Button symbols:** PlayStation (default) / Xbox. This is the engine's `glyphs`, moved to Display (§2.7.1).\n\nWorld3D reads `picture3d`, `shadows3d` and `filter3d` by those keys. Define them ourselves (same keys, values and\nlabels), because `E.World3D.SETTINGS` does not exist yet when `new E.Game` runs (§2.3). The engine provides the rest:\nvolume, music, effects, reduce motion, shake, flashes, full screen, frame rate, and the Controls screen (rebinding,\ndead zone, vibration).\n\n### 3.18 About / Credits and the exit interview (`11-data-about.js`)\n\n`SN.ABOUT` is the single source for the **About / Credits** screen (OPTIONS ▸ ABOUT, and after the ending credits) and\nfor `tools/exit-interview.mjs`, which writes `../exit-interview.json` in exactly TASK.md's shape and checks it parses.\n\nThe screen pages (L1/R1), each page big-type and short:\n1. **SOURCE INFORMATION:** every TASK.md field, \"unknown\" where it can't be confirmed. Planned values:\n   - Date: 2026-11-03 17:47:28\n   - Source: Wipeout HD (Studio Liverpool / Sony, 2008)\n   - Plan: PLAN.md\n   - Genre and perspective: anti-gravity combat racing; third-person chase camera with cockpit view and trackside TV\n     cameras\n   - Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine + my-3D2dge 3D v0.85.2, three.js r182 (WebGPU/WebGL 2), Rapier 0.19.3,\n     AI Hub client 1.4.0\n   - Art direction: the engine's native style (pixel-resolution 3D, toon/lambert light, pixel HUD and fonts) plus new\n     procedural craft, tracks and neon\n   - Animation: the engine's rigs and tweens, plus procedural craft animation\n   - Audio: synthesized music, SFX and gibberish voices\n   - Online: AI Hub ghost sessions; local split screen\n   - Testing; research; environment; model; usage\n2. **TESTING FEEDBACK:** the 4 answers.\n3. **ENGINE FEEDBACK:** the 6 answers, including the §2.7 changes.\n4. **PROMPT FEEDBACK:** the 4 answers.\n5. **CREDITS:**\n   - \"Snipeout HD. An original game inspired by Wipeout HD (not affiliated with Sony Interactive Entertainment).\"\n   - Engine credits (my-3D2dge, three.js MIT, Rapier Apache-2.0), \"all music, sound and voices synthesized in code\",\n     \"built by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5\".\n   - The fictional teams and artists, with a note that they are fictional.\n\nThe builder fills in the feedback answers truthfully at the end of the build (M12). The chat reply repeats them, as\nTASK.md demands. The `aiHub` block for the exit interview:\n\n```json\n{ \"name\": \"Snipeout HD\", \"tagline\": \"Anti-gravity. Anti-everyone.\",\n  \"description\": \"An anti-gravity combat racer: thread banked neon tracks at 600 km/h, snipe rivals with ten weapons and survive Overclock. Season, time trials, split screen and AI Hub ghost races.\",\n  \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"Racing\", \"source\": \"Wipeout HD\", \"series\": \"Wipeout\", \"players\": \"1–4\",\n  \"controls\": \"Stick or A/D steer · ✕ or W thrust · L2/R2 or Q/E airbrakes · □ or Space fire · ○ or Shift absorb\",\n  \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"racing\", \"sci-fi\", \"vehicles\", \"arcade\", \"versus\"] }\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Content\n\n### 4.1 Teams, craft, pilots, principals (`05-data-teams.js`)\n\nStats run 1–10 (§3.2 turns them into physics). The totals are close (22–24). NULL//SET trades shield for speed, which\nmakes it the rival.\n\n| Team (base) | SPD | THR | HND | SHD | Livery: primary / secondary / accent / engine glow | Craft and silhouette | One-line copy |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **KESTREL DYNAMICS** (Oslo) | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | `#f2f5f8` / `#29c8e8` / `#1a2a4a` / `#7af0ff` | **KD-9 FJORD:** a dart hull, swept delta wings, twin canted tail fins, 2 engines | \"Precision is a form of courage. Kestrel has been brave since 2109.\" |\n| **HAMMERHEAD HEAVY INDUSTRIES** (Lagos) | 6 | 4 | 3 | 9 | `#ff7a1a` / `#2b2d33` / `#ffd23f` / `#ffb347` | **HH ANVIL:** a wide flat slab hull, twin hammerhead nose pods, stub wings, 3 engines | \"Builds cranes, bridges and the occasional champion. All three survive impact.\" |\n| **SORA-TEK** (Osaka) | 5 | 6 | 9 | 4 | `#f7f7f7` / `#e0213a` / `#16161c` / `#ff5a6e` | **ST TSUBAME:** a narrow needle hull, forward canards, one central fin, long swept wings, 1 large engine | \"Sora-Tek does not turn corners. Corners are informed of a change in direction.\" |\n| **VOLTA NERO** (Turin) | 9 | 4 | 4 | 5 | `#141418` / `#e8b84a` / `#c8202a` / `#ffd36a` | **VN SAETTA:** a very long needle nose, a big rear-mounted engine, small rear wings, twin low fins | \"Straight lines, beautifully. Everything else, eventually.\" |\n| **CALDERA SYSTEMS** (Santiago) | 5 | 9 | 5 | 5 | `#d8361c` / `#6a2bd8` / `#24202a` / `#ff6a2a` | **CS VOLCÁN:** a twin-boom catamaran, two big engines on the booms, a centre pilot pod | \"Geothermal engineering. Zero to everything in four seconds.\" |\n| **NULL//SET** (Berlin; a collective) | 8 | 7 | 5 | 3 | `#0b0b0e` / `#6aff3a` / `#ff2a8a` / `#6aff3a` | **N//S GHOSTLINE:** a faceted stealth wedge, no fins, 2 flat slot engines | \"No sponsor. No logo. No comment.\" |\n\nCraft geometry parameters (ShipKit). Lengths in u; the full length is 96 u for all designs, so they share collision.\n\n| Craft | Hull sections (half-width w, height h at 0 / 20 / 40 / 60 / 80 / 100 % of length) | Wings (span, sweep) | Fins | Engines (count, radius) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FJORD | w 2/9/14/16/14/10, h 2/6/9/9/8/6 | span 30, sweep 40° | 2 canted 20° | 2 × r5 |\n| ANVIL | w 10/16/18/18/18/16, h 3/6/7/7/7/6, plus 2 nose pods r5 at ±14 | span 22, sweep 10° | 0 | 3 × r4 |\n| TSUBAME | w 1/6/10/12/10/8, h 2/5/7/8/7/5, plus canards (span 10 at 25 %) | span 36, sweep 50° | 1 tall | 1 × r7 |\n| SAETTA | w 1/4/8/12/14/12, h 1/4/6/8/9/8 | span 20, sweep 30° (rear) | 2 low | 1 × r9 |\n| VOLCÁN | two booms w 6 at ±15, a pod w 7 in the centre (front 70 %) | span 34, straight, joining the booms | 2 on the booms | 2 × r7 |\n| GHOSTLINE | a faceted wedge: w 4/12/18/20/20/18, h 2/4/6/6/5/3 (flat-shaded facets) | none (the wedge is the wing) | 0 | 2 slots 14 × 3 |\n\n**Pilots** (2 per team, 12 in all). Each has two Humanoid rigs: helmeted for the race and podium cards, bare-headed\nfor portraits. Common rig options: `{ size: 1.3, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth:\nprimary, coat: secondary, pants: accent, trim: secondary, glove: accent, boot: '#1a1a20' } }` and the helmet\n`hat: { style: 'helmet', color: secondary }`. Voice `f0` is for §3.10. `skill` is an offset on the difficulty's AI\nskill.\n","numLines":120,"startLine":1226,"totalLines":2077}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014mXYhukzBSH4a3cZF85yGg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
