{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TQqTeSvmQPwzPhnKprUnmN","type":"tool_result","content":"1346\t\n1347\t| # | Pilot | Team | Look (hair, skin) | Voice f0 | skill | aggression | Banter line |\n1348\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1349\t| 1 | INGRID VALE | Kestrel | ponytail, `#f0d080` / `#f2d0b8` | 210 | +0.01 | 0.8 | \"Clean lines. Clean wins.\" |\n1350\t| 2 | TOMAS BREKKE | Kestrel | short, `#6a4a30` / `#e8c8a8` | 120 | 0 | 0.7 | \"Holding position.\" |\n1351\t| 3 | AMARA OKAFOR | Hammerhead | short, `#1a1410` / `#8a5a3a` | 200 | +0.01 | 1.0 | \"Shield's fine. Is yours?\" |\n1352\t| 4 | DAYO ADEYEMI | Hammerhead | bald / `#6a4028` | 105 | 0 | 1.2 | \"Coming through. Literally.\" |\n1353\t| 5 | RIN TAKAHARA | Sora-Tek | long, `#14141a` / `#f0d4b8` | 230 | +0.02 | 0.7 | \"Too wide. Again.\" |\n1354\t| 6 | KENJI MORI | Sora-Tek | spiky, `#202028` / `#e8c8a0` | 130 | 0 | 0.9 | \"Apex. Apex. Apex.\" |\n1355\t| 7 | LUCA FERRANTE | Volta Nero | short, `#2a1a12` / `#e0b890` | 125 | +0.02 | 1.0 | \"Watch the straight. Watch it go.\" |\n1356\t| 8 | GIULIA MARCHETTI | Volta Nero | long, `#5a3420` / `#f0c8a0` | 215 | +0.01 | 1.1 | \"Ciao. Behind you.\" |\n1357\t| 9 | VALENTINA SOTO | Caldera | ponytail, `#2a1810` / `#d8a880` | 205 | +0.01 | 1.2 | \"Hot engine. Hotter temper.\" |\n1358\t| 10 | MATEO ARAYA | Caldera | short, `#1a1008` / `#c89870` | 115 | 0 | 1.0 | \"Launching.\" |\n1359\t| 11 | KAI-ZERO | NULL//SET | hood (`hood: true`) and visor, `#0b0b0e` / `#c8b8a8` | 140, bitcrushed | +0.03 | 1.3 | \"Rookies make the best wreckage.\" |\n1360\t| 12 | HEX | NULL//SET | spiky, `#ff2a8a` / `#e8d0c0` | 175 | +0.02 | 1.2 | \"Signal lost. Yours.\" |\n1361\t\n1362\t**The race field.** The player plus 7 AI. Every team is represented, the rival is always present, and the player's\n1363\tteammate is included. Grid order for the AI is by skill, slowest first; the player starts 5th on a first attempt and\n1364\t8th on a retry (an arcade convention).\n1365\t\n1366\t**Principals** (portraits, briefings): DIRECTOR SOLVEIG HALE (Kestrel, f0 180), CHIEF EMEKA OBI (Hammerhead, 100),\n1367\tDR. HARUKA ISE (Sora-Tek, 190), SIGNOR ARMANDO VELLUTI (Volta Nero, 110), INGENIERA PAZ ROJAS (Caldera, 170), THE ADMIN\n1368\t(NULL//SET, 90, bitcrushed; their portrait is a pixel glitch mask, a drawn function).\n1369\t\n1370\t**The rival** is KAI-ZERO, unless the player races for NULL//SET; then it is LUCA FERRANTE. Lines use `{$rival}` and\n1371\t`{$rivalTeam}` (E.Dialog vars).\n1372\t\n1373\t**ORACLE**, the Authority's race control, has as its portrait a drawn emblem: a triangle eye in a hexagon, cycling\n1374\twhite and cyan.\n1375\t\n1376\t### 4.2 Speed classes\n1377\t\n1378\t| Class | Top (m/s) | Top (u/s) | km/h | Unlock | Ideal-line lap estimate: Solenne / Karakum / Meridian / Borealis |\n1379\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1380\t| SPARK | 90 | 1440 | 324 | from the start | 45.9 / 53.8 / 47.8 / 59.4 s |\n1381\t| FLARE | 115 | 1840 | 414 | Season tier 1 | 37.3 / 43.3 / 38.1 / 47.7 s |\n1382\t| STORM | 140 | 2240 | 504 | Season tier 2 | 31.8 / 36.7 / 32.2 / 40.3 s |\n1383\t| SINGULARITY | 170 | 2720 | 612 | a Grand Prix medal | 27.5 / 31.4 / 27.5 / 34.4 s |\n1384\t\n1385\tThe estimates come from the planning script (App. C): `alat = 40 m/s² × (top/90)^1.5`, thrust `0.55·top`, airbrake\n1386\tdeceleration 28 m/s², on a line about 15 % wider than the centre line. Real AI laps should land within ±25 % of\n1387\tthem, which is a test (§7). Displayed speeds with boosts reach about 830 km/h at SINGULARITY.\n1388\t\n1389\t**Medal targets** (TIME TRIAL 3 laps, HOT LAP 1 lap) are **measured, not guessed**. In M12, run\n1390\t`node tools/medals.mjs`: the player bot at skill 1.0, 3 runs per track and class, no rubber band. Then\n1391\tgold = best × 1.04, silver = × 1.10, bronze = × 1.20, rounded to 0.1 s. Write the numbers into\n1392\t`07-data-tracks.js`. The test suite checks that every medal number exists and that the bot earns gold.\n1393\t\n1394\t### 4.3 Tracks (`07-data-tracks.js`): layouts checked during planning\n1395\t\n1396\tMetres, x east, y south, z up, origin `[2048, 2048, 0]`, driving order. The `cp` indices below refer to these arrays.\n1397\t`tools/trackcheck.mjs` must reproduce the numbers in each heading. They were computed with the App. A spline at a 2 m\n1398\tresample.\n1399\t\n1400\t#### PORT SOLENNE: tier 1, beginner. 3.84 km · tightest 56 m (lighthouse hairpin) · slopes ±15 % · 1 drop jump\n1401\t\n1402\t> *Old stone, new money. The harbour lights are on a sponsorship contract.* Golden hour on a Mediterranean resort\n1403\t> city: a seafront main straight, a climb through cliff villas, a tunnel under the old town, the Harbour Step, the\n1404\t> marina, and a hairpin around the lighthouse pier.\n1405\t\n1406\t```js\n1407\tpoints: [[0,0,3],[300,0,3],[600,0,4],[790,-50,7],[890,-210,14],[905,-420,24],[820,-600,32],[640,-690,36],[420,-670,38],\n1408\t  [220,-705,36],[40,-645,30],[-110,-565,25.5],[-176,-470,23.6],[-188,-440,23.8],[-205,-375,15],[-195,-250,10],[-255,-120,6],\n1409\t  [-320,60,4],[-300,260,3],[-200,340,3],[-100,280,3],[-80,120,3],[-40,35,3]],\n1410\twidth: 28 (cp 18–20: w 30), start: 230,\n1411\tjumps: [{ from: 12, to: 14, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE HARBOUR STEP' }],   // lip 23.6 m, lower deck 15.0 m: an 8.6 m step, 0.65 s air at every speed\n1412\ttunnels: [{ a: { cp: 7, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 40 }, style: 'stone' }],  // under the old town, about 436 m\n1413\tspeedPads: [{ cp: 1, d: 120, u: 0 }, { cp: 4, d: 80, u: -4 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 16, d: 100, u: 0 }, { cp: 21, d: 30, u: -3 }],\n1414\tweaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 80 }, { cp: 7, d: -60 }, { cp: 11, d: 40 }, { cp: 17, d: 60 }],\n1415\tpit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 259 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },   // sea side of the main straight\n1416\topenEdges: [], banks: [],\n1417\t```\n1418\t\n1419\tControl points along the track (m, raw from cp0): 0, 302, 602, 800, 992, 1204, 1406, 1610, 1832, 2036, 2226, 2398,\n1420\t2514, 2546, 2614, 2740, 2884, 3076, 3280, 3412, 3532, 3696, 3790.\n1421\t\n1422\t- **Theme `coast`:**\n1423\t  - sky `['#2a1a4a', '#c8506a', '#ffb070']`;\n1424\t  - sun low in the west (`dir [-0.8, 0.3, -0.35]`, `#ffc890`, 2.4);\n1425\t  - ambient `['#ffd0c0', '#4a3a5a', 1.6]`;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"58ed42e5-a9c6-47da-bde4-6c6579b145dd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:44:09.537Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n| # | Pilot | Team | Look (hair, skin) | Voice f0 | skill | aggression | Banter line |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | INGRID VALE | Kestrel | ponytail, `#f0d080` / `#f2d0b8` | 210 | +0.01 | 0.8 | \"Clean lines. Clean wins.\" |\n| 2 | TOMAS BREKKE | Kestrel | short, `#6a4a30` / `#e8c8a8` | 120 | 0 | 0.7 | \"Holding position.\" |\n| 3 | AMARA OKAFOR | Hammerhead | short, `#1a1410` / `#8a5a3a` | 200 | +0.01 | 1.0 | \"Shield's fine. Is yours?\" |\n| 4 | DAYO ADEYEMI | Hammerhead | bald / `#6a4028` | 105 | 0 | 1.2 | \"Coming through. Literally.\" |\n| 5 | RIN TAKAHARA | Sora-Tek | long, `#14141a` / `#f0d4b8` | 230 | +0.02 | 0.7 | \"Too wide. Again.\" |\n| 6 | KENJI MORI | Sora-Tek | spiky, `#202028` / `#e8c8a0` | 130 | 0 | 0.9 | \"Apex. Apex. Apex.\" |\n| 7 | LUCA FERRANTE | Volta Nero | short, `#2a1a12` / `#e0b890` | 125 | +0.02 | 1.0 | \"Watch the straight. Watch it go.\" |\n| 8 | GIULIA MARCHETTI | Volta Nero | long, `#5a3420` / `#f0c8a0` | 215 | +0.01 | 1.1 | \"Ciao. Behind you.\" |\n| 9 | VALENTINA SOTO | Caldera | ponytail, `#2a1810` / `#d8a880` | 205 | +0.01 | 1.2 | \"Hot engine. Hotter temper.\" |\n| 10 | MATEO ARAYA | Caldera | short, `#1a1008` / `#c89870` | 115 | 0 | 1.0 | \"Launching.\" |\n| 11 | KAI-ZERO | NULL//SET | hood (`hood: true`) and visor, `#0b0b0e` / `#c8b8a8` | 140, bitcrushed | +0.03 | 1.3 | \"Rookies make the best wreckage.\" |\n| 12 | HEX | NULL//SET | spiky, `#ff2a8a` / `#e8d0c0` | 175 | +0.02 | 1.2 | \"Signal lost. Yours.\" |\n\n**The race field.** The player plus 7 AI. Every team is represented, the rival is always present, and the player's\nteammate is included. Grid order for the AI is by skill, slowest first; the player starts 5th on a first attempt and\n8th on a retry (an arcade convention).\n\n**Principals** (portraits, briefings): DIRECTOR SOLVEIG HALE (Kestrel, f0 180), CHIEF EMEKA OBI (Hammerhead, 100),\nDR. HARUKA ISE (Sora-Tek, 190), SIGNOR ARMANDO VELLUTI (Volta Nero, 110), INGENIERA PAZ ROJAS (Caldera, 170), THE ADMIN\n(NULL//SET, 90, bitcrushed; their portrait is a pixel glitch mask, a drawn function).\n\n**The rival** is KAI-ZERO, unless the player races for NULL//SET; then it is LUCA FERRANTE. Lines use `{$rival}` and\n`{$rivalTeam}` (E.Dialog vars).\n\n**ORACLE**, the Authority's race control, has as its portrait a drawn emblem: a triangle eye in a hexagon, cycling\nwhite and cyan.\n\n### 4.2 Speed classes\n\n| Class | Top (m/s) | Top (u/s) | km/h | Unlock | Ideal-line lap estimate: Solenne / Karakum / Meridian / Borealis |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SPARK | 90 | 1440 | 324 | from the start | 45.9 / 53.8 / 47.8 / 59.4 s |\n| FLARE | 115 | 1840 | 414 | Season tier 1 | 37.3 / 43.3 / 38.1 / 47.7 s |\n| STORM | 140 | 2240 | 504 | Season tier 2 | 31.8 / 36.7 / 32.2 / 40.3 s |\n| SINGULARITY | 170 | 2720 | 612 | a Grand Prix medal | 27.5 / 31.4 / 27.5 / 34.4 s |\n\nThe estimates come from the planning script (App. C): `alat = 40 m/s² × (top/90)^1.5`, thrust `0.55·top`, airbrake\ndeceleration 28 m/s², on a line about 15 % wider than the centre line. Real AI laps should land within ±25 % of\nthem, which is a test (§7). Displayed speeds with boosts reach about 830 km/h at SINGULARITY.\n\n**Medal targets** (TIME TRIAL 3 laps, HOT LAP 1 lap) are **measured, not guessed**. In M12, run\n`node tools/medals.mjs`: the player bot at skill 1.0, 3 runs per track and class, no rubber band. Then\ngold = best × 1.04, silver = × 1.10, bronze = × 1.20, rounded to 0.1 s. Write the numbers into\n`07-data-tracks.js`. The test suite checks that every medal number exists and that the bot earns gold.\n\n### 4.3 Tracks (`07-data-tracks.js`): layouts checked during planning\n\nMetres, x east, y south, z up, origin `[2048, 2048, 0]`, driving order. The `cp` indices below refer to these arrays.\n`tools/trackcheck.mjs` must reproduce the numbers in each heading. They were computed with the App. A spline at a 2 m\nresample.\n\n#### PORT SOLENNE: tier 1, beginner. 3.84 km · tightest 56 m (lighthouse hairpin) · slopes ±15 % · 1 drop jump\n\n> *Old stone, new money. The harbour lights are on a sponsorship contract.* Golden hour on a Mediterranean resort\n> city: a seafront main straight, a climb through cliff villas, a tunnel under the old town, the Harbour Step, the\n> marina, and a hairpin around the lighthouse pier.\n\n```js\npoints: [[0,0,3],[300,0,3],[600,0,4],[790,-50,7],[890,-210,14],[905,-420,24],[820,-600,32],[640,-690,36],[420,-670,38],\n  [220,-705,36],[40,-645,30],[-110,-565,25.5],[-176,-470,23.6],[-188,-440,23.8],[-205,-375,15],[-195,-250,10],[-255,-120,6],\n  [-320,60,4],[-300,260,3],[-200,340,3],[-100,280,3],[-80,120,3],[-40,35,3]],\nwidth: 28 (cp 18–20: w 30), start: 230,\njumps: [{ from: 12, to: 14, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE HARBOUR STEP' }],   // lip 23.6 m, lower deck 15.0 m: an 8.6 m step, 0.65 s air at every speed\ntunnels: [{ a: { cp: 7, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 40 }, style: 'stone' }],  // under the old town, about 436 m\nspeedPads: [{ cp: 1, d: 120, u: 0 }, { cp: 4, d: 80, u: -4 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 16, d: 100, u: 0 }, { cp: 21, d: 30, u: -3 }],\nweaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 80 }, { cp: 7, d: -60 }, { cp: 11, d: 40 }, { cp: 17, d: 60 }],\npit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 259 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },   // sea side of the main straight\nopenEdges: [], banks: [],\n```\n\nControl points along the track (m, raw from cp0): 0, 302, 602, 800, 992, 1204, 1406, 1610, 1832, 2036, 2226, 2398,\n2514, 2546, 2614, 2740, 2884, 3076, 3280, 3412, 3532, 3696, 3790.\n\n- **Theme `coast`:**\n  - sky `['#2a1a4a', '#c8506a', '#ffb070']`;\n  - sun low in the west (`dir [-0.8, 0.3, -0.35]`, `#ffc890`, 2.4);\n  - ambient `['#ffd0c0', '#4a3a5a', 1.6]`;","numLines":80,"startLine":1346,"totalLines":2078}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TQqTeSvmQPwzPhnKprUnmN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
