{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3KwwDDHtCZc5SF8oLt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ScCxSk2WsKQ7gGJ7xY1vta","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nreps=[\n(\"#### PORT SOLENNE: tier 1, beginner. 3.84 km · tightest 56 m (lighthouse hairpin) · slopes ±15 % · 1 drop jump\",\n \"#### PORT SOLENNE: tier 1, beginner. 3.84 km · tightest 56 m (lighthouse hairpin) · slopes ±5 % (−15 % only inside the jump) · 1 drop jump\"),\n(\"width: 28 (cp 18–20: w 30), start: 230,\",\n \"width: 28, widths: { 18: 30, 19: 30, 20: 30 }, start: 230,   // widths: per control point, metres (the hairpin is wider)\"),\n(\"\"\"**The race field.** The player plus 7 AI. Every team is represented, the rival is always present, and the player's\nteammate is included. Grid order for the AI is by skill, slowest first; the player starts 5th on a first attempt and\n8th on a retry (an arcade convention).\"\"\",\n \"\"\"**The race field.** The player plus 7 AI. Every team is represented, the rival is always present, and the player's\nteammate is included. AI grid order is by skill, fastest at the front. The player starts **8th, at the back**, as in\nthe source. In VERSUS the two humans start 7th and 8th.\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  points: [[x, y, z], ...],        // or [x, y, z, { w, bank, tag }]; a closed loop in driving order\"\"\",\n \"\"\"  points: [[x, y, z], ...],        // a closed loop in driving order\n  widths: { 18: 30 },              // optional per control point width overrides (metres), interpolated between points\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    n=s.count(a); assert n==1,(n,a[:60]); s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Fix Solenne slopes, widths syntax and grid order"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5656,"