{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012YuSkvuEHDhWBnM6ka3DeE","type":"tool_result","content":"1426\t  - ambient `['#ffd0c0', '#4a3a5a', 1.6]`;\n1427\t  - fog `#e89878`, near 12000 u, far 26000 u.\n1428\t- **Terrain:** the sea to the south (local y > 60: height −4 m, under a water plane at 0 m with gradient bands and a\n1429\t  sun-glint strip), a beach, then hills rising north to 120 m (noise). The old town plateau covers the tunnel at about\n1430\t  55 m.\n1431\t- **Scenery:**\n1432\t  - the promenade with 60 palm pylons and 14 sponsor boards along the main straight;\n1433\t  - crowd stands at the start;\n1434\t  - a glass pit building;\n1435\t  - 300 old-town houses (white, ochre and pink boxes with terracotta roofs) on the hill;\n1436\t  - cliff villas with pools;\n1437\t  - harbour cranes;\n1438\t  - 40 marina boats (hull and mast);\n1439\t  - the lighthouse on the pier (red and white rings, a rotating beam light, a landmark for the hairpin);\n1440\t  - a Ferris wheel turning slowly behind the marina;\n1441\t  - beach umbrellas;\n1442\t  - the landmark arch \"SOLENNE 2161\" at cp3.\n1443\t- **Music:** `solenne`.\n1444\t\n1445\t#### KARAKUM SPIRE: tier 1, intermediate. 4.59 km · tightest 55 m · a gorge **gap** jump · a spiral that passes over its own track (24.5 m clearance)\n1446\t\n1447\t> *A canyon the colour of rust, a spire nobody climbs, and a gorge that keeps what it catches.* Noon in a red-rock\n1448\t> desert: canyon-floor straights, a plateau with an open edge, the gorge jump (it needs 270 km/h), a tunnel through a\n1449\t> mesa, a 28°-banked spiral climbing around the Spire, over its own entry, and a long dive home.\n1450\t\n1451\t```js\n1452\tpoints: [[0,0,0],[0,-330,0],[30,-575,2],[130,-740,8],[295,-820,18],[490,-820,29],[620,-778,32],[720,-712,36.5],[742,-696,37.5],\n1453\t  [765,-680,28],[840,-610,21],[905,-525,16],[935,-360,11],[905,-195,9],[885,-65,7],[870,65,9],[790,165,15],[675,130,21],[655,15,26],\n1454\t  [740,-50,30],[855,-50,32],[985,30,30],[1035,180,22],[945,310,14],[740,355,8],[490,345,4],[245,345,2],[50,295,0],[-25,165,0]],\n1455\twidth: 26, start: 200,\n1456\tjumps: [{ from: 7, to: 9, kind: 'gap', name: 'THE GORGE', minSpeed: 75 }],   // cp8 is a virtual apex inside the gap (not drawn); 57 m gap\n1457\ttunnels: [{ a: { cp: 11, d: 60 }, b: { cp: 13, d: 40 }, style: 'rock' }],   // through the mesa, about 316 m\n1458\tspeedPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 6, d: 40, u: -3 }, { cp: 6, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 13, d: 60, u: 0 }, { cp: 20, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 24, d: 120, u: -4 }],\n1459\tweaponPads: [{ cp: 3, d: 40 }, { cp: 10, d: 60 }, { cp: 14, d: 60 }, { cp: 22, d: 60 }, { cp: 26, d: 60 }],\n1460\tpit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 10 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 0 }, side: 'left', w: 8 },\n1461\topenEdges: [{ a: { cp: 5, d: 0 }, b: { cp: 6, d: 60 }, side: 'left' }],   // the plateau rim: fall into the canyon\n1462\tbanks: [{ from: 15, to: 20, deg: 28 }],                                    // the Spire spiral\n1463\t```\n1464\t\n1465\tControl points along the track: 0, 330, 578, 773, 958, 1155, 1292, 1412 (lip), 1439 (virtual), 1469 (far edge),\n1466\t1572, 1680, 1848, 2016, 2148, 2279, 2411, 2536, 2657, 2767, 2883, 3038, 3200, 3362, 3574, 3825, 4070, 4274, 4427.\n1467\t\n1468\t**Overpass:** raw s ≈ 2208 (lower, under the spiral exit) and ≈ 2928 (upper). **Gorge** (App. C):\n1469\t- 45–60 m/s hit the far wall: a rescue;\n1470\t- 75 m/s just clears;\n1471\t- 90 m/s lands 18 m past the far edge at −13°;\n1472\t- 170 m/s lands 129 m past at −10°.\n1473\t\n1474\t- **Theme `desert`:**\n1475\t  - sky `['#3a78d8', '#9cc8f0', '#f0e0c0']`;\n1476\t  - sun high (`[-0.3, 0.2, -0.93]`, `#fff2d0`, 3.0);\n1477\t  - fog `#e8d0a0`, near 14000, far 30000.\n1478\t- **Terrain:** a meandering canyon floor along the low sections, mesas (flat tops 40–80 m with strata walls: World3D\n1479\t  `rock: { colors: ['#b85a30', '#d8884a', '#8a3a20', '#e8b070'], band: 48 }`), the gorge cut −60 m under the jump with\n1480\t  a thin river (an emissive blue strip), and dunes outside.\n1481\t- **Scenery:**\n1482\t  - **the Spire:** a 220 m stacked rock column at local (762, 72) inside the spiral (tapering cylinders, strata\n1483\t    colours);\n1484\t  - 24 wind turbines with turning rotors on the plateaus;\n1485\t  - solar fields;\n1486\t  - carved mesa portals;\n1487\t  - canyon-wall banners;\n1488\t  - a half-buried old craft wreck as a landmark at the gorge;\n1489\t  - dust devils (particles);\n1490\t  - heat haze.\n1491\t- **Music:** `karakum`.\n1492\t\n1493\t#### MERIDIAN STACK: tier 2, advanced. 4.18 km · tightest 52 m · the Stack **drop** · a figure-eight crossover (31.9 m clearance) · night\n1494\t\n1495\t> *Three hundred storeys of people who have never seen the ground. Tonight they watch you fall past their windows.* A\n1496\t> vertical megacity at night: an elevated start, the Stack Drop between towers, neon tunnels through buildings, a low\n1497\t> pass under its own upper deck, and a long climb back to the sky deck.\n1498\t\n1499\t```js\n1500\tpoints: [[0,0,42],[250,-40,42],[480,-160,40],[615,-300,37],[650,-395,36.2],[653,-425,36.4],[655,-490,22],[630,-585,17],\n1501\t  [460,-700,15],[240,-680,13],[100,-540,11],[0,-360,10],[-100,-180,10],[-260,-40,12],[-480,0,18],[-680,-80,24],[-780,-280,30],\n1502\t  [-700,-480,36],[-500,-560,40],[-300,-480,42],[-160,-300,42],[-60,-120,42]],\n1503\twidth: 24, start: 190,\n1504\tjumps: [{ from: 4, to: 6, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE STACK DROP' }],   // cp5 virtual; lip 36.2 m to a lower deck at 22.0 m: a 14.2 m step\n1505\ttunnels: [{ a: { cp: 8, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 80 }, style: 'neon' }, { a: { cp: 13, d: 50 }, b: { cp: 14, d: 40 }, style: 'neon' }],\n1506\tspeedPads: [{ cp: 1, d: 60, u: 0 }, { cp: 3, d: 50, u: 0 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 12, d: 30, u: 0 }, { cp: 17, d: 60, u: -3 }, { cp: 20, d: 60, u: 0 }],\n1507\tweaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40 }, { cp: 7, d: 60 }, { cp: 12, d: 120 }, { cp: 15, d: 60 }, { cp: 19, d: -40 }],\n1508\tpit: { a: { cp: 19, d: 35 }, b: { cp: 20, d: 126 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },   // on the sky deck, ending before the crossover\n1509\topenEdges: [], banks: [],\n1510\t```\n1511\t\n1512\tControl points along the track: 0, 258, 518, 714, 815 (lip), 846 (virtual), 912 (far edge), 1012, 1220, 1446, 1646,\n1513\t1852, 2058, 2272, 2498, 2718, 2946, 3165, 3385, 3605, 3833, 4039.\n1514\t\n1515\t**Overpass:** raw s ≈ 2082 (low, z ≈ 10 m) under s ≈ 3983 (high, z ≈ 42 m). **The drop** (App. C): every speed\n1516\tlands. Slow craft land hard (45 m/s: −37°, damage); fast ones smoothly (140 m/s: −12°). The drop sits on a 19°\n1517\tcurve, so the lower deck follows the plan path (§3.1).\n1518\t\n1519\t- **Theme `city`:**\n1520\t  - sky `['#05030f', '#1a0f3a', '#3a1a5a']`;\n1521\t  - moonlight `#8090ff`, 0.5;\n1522\t  - ambient `['#3a3a8a', '#100818', 1.0]`;\n1523\t  - fog `#1a1035`, near 6000, far 22000;\n1524\t  - bloom strong.\n1525\t- **Terrain:** flat street level at −40 m, dark concrete.\n1526\t- **Scenery:**\n1527\t  - 260 megatowers (60–350 m, window-grid emissive textures in three palettes);\n1528\t  - neon signs and holo billboards (hue-cycling) with the sponsor list;\n1529\t  - maglev rails with trains moving on loops;\n1530\t  - sweeping searchlights;\n1531\t  - flying traffic lanes (small emissive craft on paths);\n1532\t  - **the Meridian Spire** (a 500 m tower with a beacon) next to the crossover;\n1533\t  - rooftop helipads with blinking lights;\n1534\t  - light rain.\n1535\t- **Music:** `meridian`.\n1536\t\n1537\t#### BOREALIS VAULT: tier 3, expert. 5.03 km · tightest 44 m (switchbacks) · climbs to +11 % · the Vault **drop** (17.2 m) · a 490 m ice tunnel\n1538\t\n1539\t> *Minus forty, plus aurora. The Authority recommends not stopping.* An arctic research basin at night: a station\n1540\t> plateau start, sweeping descents, the Vault drop, the ice tunnel, a frozen lake with an open edge, and a brutal\n1541\t> switchback climb under the aurora.\n1542\t\n1543\t```js\n1544\tpoints: [[0,0,110],[-350,0,110],[-650,60,104],[-850,220,92],[-905,420,80],[-892,478,76.5],[-878,524,77.2],[-870,552,77.6],\n1545\t  [-852,612,60],[-800,690,53],[-600,770,47],[-380,800,38],[-150,760,30],[60,820,22],[260,950,14],[480,1000,10],[700,960,10],\n1546\t  [880,860,12],[1000,700,18],[1020,520,30],[930,380,44],[1000,250,58],[900,120,72],[720,140,84],[560,60,96],[380,0,106],[190,-15,110]],\n1547\twidth: 26, start: 200,\n1548\tjumps: [{ from: 6, to: 8, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE VAULT' }],   // cp7 virtual; lip 77.2 m, lower deck 60.0 m; a ski-jump lip at +1.7 %\n1549\ttunnels: [{ a: { cp: 12, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 14, d: 60 }, style: 'ice' }],\n1550\tspeedPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 5, d: 15, u: 0 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: -3 }, { cp: 15, d: 100, u: 0 }, { cp: 24, d: 60, u: 3 }, { cp: 26, d: 80, u: 0 }],\n1551\tweaponPads: [{ cp: 3, d: 40 }, { cp: 11, d: 60 }, { cp: 14, d: 100 }, { cp: 17, d: 40 }, { cp: 22, d: 40 }],\n1552\tpit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 1, d: -10 }, side: 'left', w: 8 },\n1553\topenEdges: [{ a: { cp: 15, d: 0 }, b: { cp: 16, d: 100 }, side: 'right' }],   // the frozen lake\n1554\tbanks: [{ from: 19, to: 22, deg: 26 }],                                        // the switchbacks\n1555\t```\n1556\t\n1557\tControl points along the track: 0, 350, 658, 918, 1126, 1186, 1234 (lip), 1264 (virtual), 1330 (far edge), 1424,\n1558\t1642, 1864, 2098, 2318, 2558, 2784, 3010, 3216, 3418, 3602, 3772, 3924, 4094, 4278, 4458, 4648, 4840.\n1559\t\n1560\t**The Vault** (App. C): slow craft land hard (45 m/s: −40°); 115–170 m/s land 31–111 m past the far edge at −12 to\n1561\t−15°. Air time is about 1.0–1.2 s, room for two rolls.\n1562\t\n1563\t- **Theme `arctic`:**\n1564\t  - sky `['#020814', '#0a2a4a', '#1a4a6a']`;\n1565\t  - moon `#a0c8ff`, 0.9;\n1566\t  - fog `#9ab8d8`, near 9000, far 26000.\n1567\t- **Terrain:** snowy ridges (`E.noise2` octaves), a glacier valley, the frozen lake (flat at 8 m) around local\n1568\t  (480, 1000), and dark rock strata on the steep parts.\n1569\t- **Scenery:**\n1570\t  - the research station at the start (domes, a radar dish turning, masts with blinking red lights);\n1571\t  - ice spikes;\n1572\t  - **aurora ribbons:** 5 tall translucent emissive strips, animated in waves, high in the sky;\n1573\t  - snowfall near the camera;\n1574\t  - the ice tunnel (translucent blue walls with inner glow);\n1575\t  - lake cracks (decals);\n1576\t  - a frozen-in icebreaker ship as the landmark.\n1577\t- **Music:** `borealis`.\n1578\t\n1579\t**Grid, sectors, records:** automatic (§3.1). **Overclock skin:** any track (§3.7).\n1580\t\n1581\t### 4.4 Weapon icons and pickup look\n1582\t\n1583\t24 × 24 pixel icons (`E.sprite` strings or px drawing, shaded with `E.tones`), each in its §3.4 colour on a dark\n1584\trounded tile:\n1585\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"f4bec9d8-bbc5-426f-b6ec-604cf431f788","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:44:24.194Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"  - ambient `['#ffd0c0', '#4a3a5a', 1.6]`;\n  - fog `#e89878`, near 12000 u, far 26000 u.\n- **Terrain:** the sea to the south (local y > 60: height −4 m, under a water plane at 0 m with gradient bands and a\n  sun-glint strip), a beach, then hills rising north to 120 m (noise). The old town plateau covers the tunnel at about\n  55 m.\n- **Scenery:**\n  - the promenade with 60 palm pylons and 14 sponsor boards along the main straight;\n  - crowd stands at the start;\n  - a glass pit building;\n  - 300 old-town houses (white, ochre and pink boxes with terracotta roofs) on the hill;\n  - cliff villas with pools;\n  - harbour cranes;\n  - 40 marina boats (hull and mast);\n  - the lighthouse on the pier (red and white rings, a rotating beam light, a landmark for the hairpin);\n  - a Ferris wheel turning slowly behind the marina;\n  - beach umbrellas;\n  - the landmark arch \"SOLENNE 2161\" at cp3.\n- **Music:** `solenne`.\n\n#### KARAKUM SPIRE: tier 1, intermediate. 4.59 km · tightest 55 m · a gorge **gap** jump · a spiral that passes over its own track (24.5 m clearance)\n\n> *A canyon the colour of rust, a spire nobody climbs, and a gorge that keeps what it catches.* Noon in a red-rock\n> desert: canyon-floor straights, a plateau with an open edge, the gorge jump (it needs 270 km/h), a tunnel through a\n> mesa, a 28°-banked spiral climbing around the Spire, over its own entry, and a long dive home.\n\n```js\npoints: [[0,0,0],[0,-330,0],[30,-575,2],[130,-740,8],[295,-820,18],[490,-820,29],[620,-778,32],[720,-712,36.5],[742,-696,37.5],\n  [765,-680,28],[840,-610,21],[905,-525,16],[935,-360,11],[905,-195,9],[885,-65,7],[870,65,9],[790,165,15],[675,130,21],[655,15,26],\n  [740,-50,30],[855,-50,32],[985,30,30],[1035,180,22],[945,310,14],[740,355,8],[490,345,4],[245,345,2],[50,295,0],[-25,165,0]],\nwidth: 26, start: 200,\njumps: [{ from: 7, to: 9, kind: 'gap', name: 'THE GORGE', minSpeed: 75 }],   // cp8 is a virtual apex inside the gap (not drawn); 57 m gap\ntunnels: [{ a: { cp: 11, d: 60 }, b: { cp: 13, d: 40 }, style: 'rock' }],   // through the mesa, about 316 m\nspeedPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 6, d: 40, u: -3 }, { cp: 6, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 13, d: 60, u: 0 }, { cp: 20, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 24, d: 120, u: -4 }],\nweaponPads: [{ cp: 3, d: 40 }, { cp: 10, d: 60 }, { cp: 14, d: 60 }, { cp: 22, d: 60 }, { cp: 26, d: 60 }],\npit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 10 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 0 }, side: 'left', w: 8 },\nopenEdges: [{ a: { cp: 5, d: 0 }, b: { cp: 6, d: 60 }, side: 'left' }],   // the plateau rim: fall into the canyon\nbanks: [{ from: 15, to: 20, deg: 28 }],                                    // the Spire spiral\n```\n\nControl points along the track: 0, 330, 578, 773, 958, 1155, 1292, 1412 (lip), 1439 (virtual), 1469 (far edge),\n1572, 1680, 1848, 2016, 2148, 2279, 2411, 2536, 2657, 2767, 2883, 3038, 3200, 3362, 3574, 3825, 4070, 4274, 4427.\n\n**Overpass:** raw s ≈ 2208 (lower, under the spiral exit) and ≈ 2928 (upper). **Gorge** (App. C):\n- 45–60 m/s hit the far wall: a rescue;\n- 75 m/s just clears;\n- 90 m/s lands 18 m past the far edge at −13°;\n- 170 m/s lands 129 m past at −10°.\n\n- **Theme `desert`:**\n  - sky `['#3a78d8', '#9cc8f0', '#f0e0c0']`;\n  - sun high (`[-0.3, 0.2, -0.93]`, `#fff2d0`, 3.0);\n  - fog `#e8d0a0`, near 14000, far 30000.\n- **Terrain:** a meandering canyon floor along the low sections, mesas (flat tops 40–80 m with strata walls: World3D\n  `rock: { colors: ['#b85a30', '#d8884a', '#8a3a20', '#e8b070'], band: 48 }`), the gorge cut −60 m under the jump with\n  a thin river (an emissive blue strip), and dunes outside.\n- **Scenery:**\n  - **the Spire:** a 220 m stacked rock column at local (762, 72) inside the spiral (tapering cylinders, strata\n    colours);\n  - 24 wind turbines with turning rotors on the plateaus;\n  - solar fields;\n  - carved mesa portals;\n  - canyon-wall banners;\n  - a half-buried old craft wreck as a landmark at the gorge;\n  - dust devils (particles);\n  - heat haze.\n- **Music:** `karakum`.\n\n#### MERIDIAN STACK: tier 2, advanced. 4.18 km · tightest 52 m · the Stack **drop** · a figure-eight crossover (31.9 m clearance) · night\n\n> *Three hundred storeys of people who have never seen the ground. Tonight they watch you fall past their windows.* A\n> vertical megacity at night: an elevated start, the Stack Drop between towers, neon tunnels through buildings, a low\n> pass under its own upper deck, and a long climb back to the sky deck.\n\n```js\npoints: [[0,0,42],[250,-40,42],[480,-160,40],[615,-300,37],[650,-395,36.2],[653,-425,36.4],[655,-490,22],[630,-585,17],\n  [460,-700,15],[240,-680,13],[100,-540,11],[0,-360,10],[-100,-180,10],[-260,-40,12],[-480,0,18],[-680,-80,24],[-780,-280,30],\n  [-700,-480,36],[-500,-560,40],[-300,-480,42],[-160,-300,42],[-60,-120,42]],\nwidth: 24, start: 190,\njumps: [{ from: 4, to: 6, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE STACK DROP' }],   // cp5 virtual; lip 36.2 m to a lower deck at 22.0 m: a 14.2 m step\ntunnels: [{ a: { cp: 8, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 80 }, style: 'neon' }, { a: { cp: 13, d: 50 }, b: { cp: 14, d: 40 }, style: 'neon' }],\nspeedPads: [{ cp: 1, d: 60, u: 0 }, { cp: 3, d: 50, u: 0 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 12, d: 30, u: 0 }, { cp: 17, d: 60, u: -3 }, { cp: 20, d: 60, u: 0 }],\nweaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40 }, { cp: 7, d: 60 }, { cp: 12, d: 120 }, { cp: 15, d: 60 }, { cp: 19, d: -40 }],\npit: { a: { cp: 19, d: 35 }, b: { cp: 20, d: 126 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },   // on the sky deck, ending before the crossover\nopenEdges: [], banks: [],\n```\n\nControl points along the track: 0, 258, 518, 714, 815 (lip), 846 (virtual), 912 (far edge), 1012, 1220, 1446, 1646,\n1852, 2058, 2272, 2498, 2718, 2946, 3165, 3385, 3605, 3833, 4039.\n\n**Overpass:** raw s ≈ 2082 (low, z ≈ 10 m) under s ≈ 3983 (high, z ≈ 42 m). **The drop** (App. C): every speed\nlands. Slow craft land hard (45 m/s: −37°, damage); fast ones smoothly (140 m/s: −12°). The drop sits on a 19°\ncurve, so the lower deck follows the plan path (§3.1).\n\n- **Theme `city`:**\n  - sky `['#05030f', '#1a0f3a', '#3a1a5a']`;\n  - moonlight `#8090ff`, 0.5;\n  - ambient `['#3a3a8a', '#100818', 1.0]`;\n  - fog `#1a1035`, near 6000, far 22000;\n  - bloom strong.\n- **Terrain:** flat street level at −40 m, dark concrete.\n- **Scenery:**\n  - 260 megatowers (60–350 m, window-grid emissive textures in three palettes);\n  - neon signs and holo billboards (hue-cycling) with the sponsor list;\n  - maglev rails with trains moving on loops;\n  - sweeping searchlights;\n  - flying traffic lanes (small emissive craft on paths);\n  - **the Meridian Spire** (a 500 m tower with a beacon) next to the crossover;\n  - rooftop helipads with blinking lights;\n  - light rain.\n- **Music:** `meridian`.\n\n#### BOREALIS VAULT: tier 3, expert. 5.03 km · tightest 44 m (switchbacks) · climbs to +11 % · the Vault **drop** (17.2 m) · a 490 m ice tunnel\n\n> *Minus forty, plus aurora. The Authority recommends not stopping.* An arctic research basin at night: a station\n> plateau start, sweeping descents, the Vault drop, the ice tunnel, a frozen lake with an open edge, and a brutal\n> switchback climb under the aurora.\n\n```js\npoints: [[0,0,110],[-350,0,110],[-650,60,104],[-850,220,92],[-905,420,80],[-892,478,76.5],[-878,524,77.2],[-870,552,77.6],\n  [-852,612,60],[-800,690,53],[-600,770,47],[-380,800,38],[-150,760,30],[60,820,22],[260,950,14],[480,1000,10],[700,960,10],\n  [880,860,12],[1000,700,18],[1020,520,30],[930,380,44],[1000,250,58],[900,120,72],[720,140,84],[560,60,96],[380,0,106],[190,-15,110]],\nwidth: 26, start: 200,\njumps: [{ from: 6, to: 8, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE VAULT' }],   // cp7 virtual; lip 77.2 m, lower deck 60.0 m; a ski-jump lip at +1.7 %\ntunnels: [{ a: { cp: 12, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 14, d: 60 }, style: 'ice' }],\nspeedPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 5, d: 15, u: 0 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: -3 }, { cp: 15, d: 100, u: 0 }, { cp: 24, d: 60, u: 3 }, { cp: 26, d: 80, u: 0 }],\nweaponPads: [{ cp: 3, d: 40 }, { cp: 11, d: 60 }, { cp: 14, d: 100 }, { cp: 17, d: 40 }, { cp: 22, d: 40 }],\npit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 1, d: -10 }, side: 'left', w: 8 },\nopenEdges: [{ a: { cp: 15, d: 0 }, b: { cp: 16, d: 100 }, side: 'right' }],   // the frozen lake\nbanks: [{ from: 19, to: 22, deg: 26 }],                                        // the switchbacks\n```\n\nControl points along the track: 0, 350, 658, 918, 1126, 1186, 1234 (lip), 1264 (virtual), 1330 (far edge), 1424,\n1642, 1864, 2098, 2318, 2558, 2784, 3010, 3216, 3418, 3602, 3772, 3924, 4094, 4278, 4458, 4648, 4840.\n\n**The Vault** (App. C): slow craft land hard (45 m/s: −40°); 115–170 m/s land 31–111 m past the far edge at −12 to\n−15°. Air time is about 1.0–1.2 s, room for two rolls.\n\n- **Theme `arctic`:**\n  - sky `['#020814', '#0a2a4a', '#1a4a6a']`;\n  - moon `#a0c8ff`, 0.9;\n  - fog `#9ab8d8`, near 9000, far 2600