{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015oazBkd5yEsCwLVohj7FqT","type":"tool_result","content":"1705\t\n1706\t**The vertical slice at the end of M5** must already *play* like the game: a full race with AI and weapons on every\n1707\ttrack. If time runs short later, the plan's priorities hold:\n1708\t1. a feature's existence and correctness (§8);\n1709\t2. the playthrough test;\n1710\t3. the look;\n1711\t4. the quantity of content.\n1712\t\n1713\t---\n1714\t\n1715\t## 6. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1716\t\n1717\t| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk (when) |\n1718\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1719\t| 1 | **The 3D stack in one file** (an inline ES module, an import map to the CDN, file://, WebGPU → WebGL 2 fallback, headless Chromium) | Nothing else works if it doesn't. It is new to most builders | **M0 spike first.** Prove the bundle from file:// in Playwright with a picture. If the CDN is blocked in the test environment, retry once, then vendor `three.webgpu.min.js`, `three.core.min.js` (imported by it), `three.tsl.min.js` and `rapier.mjs` as inline modules: rewrite the import map to `data:`/blob URLs made by a tiny classic loader, or inline the files as `<script type=\"module\">` with the specifiers mapped to blob URLs. Keep the CDN as the default (smaller file) |\n1720\t| 2 | **Frame and handedness bugs** (a left-handed engine frame, bank signs, camera roll sign, `toThree`) | Silent wrongness: mirrored steering, banks the wrong way, a camera rolling backwards | Unit tests in M1 (§7.2) before any physics. One `SN.frame` helper, used everywhere. A screenshot check of the roll on the Karakum spiral (M3) |\n1721\t| 3 | **Physics at 3,000 u/s** (tunnelling, jitter on crests, stuck on walls, overpasses confusing the track lookup) | The core feel. Hard to see in code review | Track-space walls are analytic (no tunnelling). Local-only `locate`. Invariant tests over long random-input runs (M2). Dev sliders for live tuning. The App. C jump numbers become tests |\n1722\t| 4 | **AI that finishes on every track** (the jump speeds, hairpins, overpass, open edges, the drop in a curve) | A stuck AI breaks races, attract, the season playthrough and medal calibration | One line/profile generator plus a PD controller, tested on 4 tracks × 4 classes × 4 seeds in M4. A stuck detector, rescue, and a per-track min-speed constraint at the gap |\n1723\t| 5 | **Determinism** (replays, the hub's fair start, hashes) | Any `Math.random`, dt or order dependence breaks replays | §2.8 rules. A lint test that greps the sim files for `Math.random`, `Date.now` and `performance.now`. Hash-equality tests from M4 on |\n1724\t| 6 | **Shader stalls and loading hitches** (World3D compiles on first use) | Visible hitches at GO or on the first weapon | Materials only at world creation. The warm-up frame and `world.prepare()` in loading (§3.7). Frame-time logging in the M3 browser test |\n1725\t| 7 | **Scope** (11 modes, 4 tracks, season, audio, hub) | Running out of time with stubs left (the brief forbids stubs) | Milestone order puts every feature in a minimal complete form before polish. The §8 checklist is the definition of done. Cut quantity, never features |\n1726\t| 8 | **Hub conformance** (card, ready without keys, time-up, end, ghosts) | The hub keeps failing games out of sessions | The Node mock early (M11 start), then the real harness at 1, 2 and 4 players with network faults and host-leave. The session path shares the race code, so it adds little new code |\n1727\t| 9 | **Synth music quality** | Bad music undermines the source's identity | The engine edits (filter env, unison) make house/acid/trance timbres possible. Compose at least 16 bars with A/B sections and use layers. A headless check that songs parse. A listen in the browser (the builder has no ears, so check with `audio.pos` and drift) |\n1728\t| 10 | **Readability at 10 feet** (a 427×240 HUD on a TV) | Tiny text is the default trap | HUD at scale 2 minimum for numbers, the large-HUD option, ≤ 6 items per screen. Screenshots at 1920×1080 scaled down to 50 % must stay legible (📷 M6) |\n1729\t| 11 | **Analog triggers and DualSense mapping** | The engine reads only `pressed` | Engine edit §2.7.3, tested with a stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()` in Playwright (axes and button `value`) |\n1730\t| 12 | **/tmp nearly full** (a shared tmpfs) | Playwright and Chromium need temp space | `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp` for every tool run (§0) |\n1731\t| 13 | **Terrain intersecting the track or tunnels** | The ground poking through decks or tunnel interiors looks broken | The corridor grid carve (§3.7) plus portal frames. 📷 every tunnel portal and every elevated section in M3 |\n1732\t\n1733\t---\n1734\t\n1735\t## 7. Testing (one command)\n1736\t\n1737\t**The command:** `cd SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728 && TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp node tests/run.mjs`.\n1738\tIt runs every suite (Node first, then browser, then the hub harness). It prints **only failures** (suite › test:\n1739\tmessage, plus the snapshot JSON where useful) and **one final line**:\n1740\t`412 passed, 0 failed (node 380, browser 22, hub 10) in 96 s`.\n1741\t- `node tests/run.mjs physics race` runs only the named suites.\n1742\t- `--node` skips the browser and hub suites.\n1743\t- Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (the suites map to files, listed in `tests/run.mjs`).\n1744\t\n1745\t### 7.1 Harness\n1746\t\n1747\t`tests/lib/vm.mjs` follows the handoff's `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`:\n1748\t- a `vm` context with stand-ins `window = ctx`, `addEventListener() {}`, `location: { search: '', hash: '' }`,\n1749\t  `matchMedia`, `navigator: { maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads: () => [] }`;\n1750\t- it runs `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then the `src/` files in manifest order;\n1751\t- `E.current` is the game, and `game.advance(s)` drives it;\n1752\t- scripted input through `game.input.tap/hold/press`, `input.feed` for the mouse, and `SN.vpad` for analog;\n1753\t- assertions through `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n1754\t\n1755\t```js\n1756\tgame.debug = {\n1757\t  snapshot: () => ({ scene, state, mode, track, cls, t, ships: [{ id, p, s, u, h, v, kmh, energy, lap, place, weapon, airborne, finished, elim }],\n1758\t                     player: {...}, hudCallouts: [...], focus: ui.focusId, device: input.lastDevice, attract: bool, dev: bool,\n1759\t                     season: { medals, unlocked }, hub: { connected, sent, progressCount } }),\n1760\t  teleport(s, u = 0, v = 0), give(weapon), setEnergy(x), finishNow(), events: () => race.events.slice(),\n1761\t  race: () => race, track: () => track, tune: SN.Tune\n1762\t};\n1763\t```\n1764\t\n1765\t### 7.2 Node suites (fast, about 60 s in all)\n1766\t\n1767\t- **unit:**\n1768\t  - math and frames (8 headings), bank sign, `toThree` mapping;\n1769\t  - the spline: closure, arc length, knot s;\n1770\t  - each TrackDef validates;\n1771\t  - feature s-values; `query` returns the right deck at overpasses;\n1772\t  - the racing line inside the bounds; speed profile ≤ top;\n1773\t  - Tune def/reset;\n1774\t  - the input mapping: double-tap, flick, ramped keys;\n1775\t  - the hash is stable;\n1776\t  - **lint:** the sim files contain no `Math.random`, `Date.now`, `performance.now`, `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`\n1777\t    or `window.open`, and no file contains TODO.\n1778\t- **physics:**\n1779\t  - every feel target in §3.2;\n1780\t  - jumps: Karakum's gap at 70 / 80 / 90 / 140 m/s (fails at 70, clears at ≥ 80, landing window as App. C ±15 %), drops\n1781\t    land at 45 and 170 m/s;\n1782\t  - long random-input soak (10 simulated minutes, 4 tracks): no NaN, never `|u| > hw` on walled decks, never `h < 0`;\n1783\t  - overpass: a craft on the upper deck stays on it (its s stays in the upper range);\n1784\t  - pads, pit recharge, side-shift, roll ok/botch, rescue after an open-edge fall;\n1785\t  - launch boost window.\n1786\t- **race:**\n1787\t  - 4 tracks × 4 classes × 2 seeds of 8 AI: all finish, no stuck, rescues ≤ 1 per craft, lap times within ±25 % of\n1788\t    §4.2;\n1789\t  - positions sorted by progress; wrong way; final-lap event; results;\n1790\t  - determinism (2 runs, equal hash); replay re-sim equals the hash.\n1791\t- **weapons:** every row of §3.4, each in a fixed two-craft setup, plus AI usage counts.\n1792\t- **modes:** time trial (+ ghost round trip), hot lap (flying start, best lap), snipeout (scoring, respawn, the target\n1793\t  ends it), overclock (zones, tempo events, end), academy (the bot passes 11 drills), versus (2 viewports, half-keys\n1794\t  labels), grand prix (points table, ties).\n1795\t- **flow:**\n1796\t  - title → menu → setup → race → results → replay → menu;\n1797\t  - pause menu items present (Restart, Camera, How to play, Dev mode, Quit) and absent in a session;\n1798\t  - settings keys exist;\n1799\t  - glyph labels per device and setting;\n1800\t  - touch-only notice;\n1801\t  - attract timing and exit;\n1802\t  - dev sliders and reset; each cheat.\n1803\t- **season:** §7.4.\n1804\t- **audio:** song parsing, event → sound map, `Voice` durations, the music director's layer changes (headless:\n1805\t  `audio.pos`).\n1806\t- **hub (mock):** §7.6.\n1807\t\n1808\t### 7.3 The player bot (`tests/lib/bot.mjs`)\n1809\t\n1810\t`bot.drive(playerIndex, { skill: 1, weapons: true, rolls: true })`. Each step it computes `SN.AI.controls(ship, race)`\n1811\tfor the human's craft and writes them into `SN.vpad[i]`. Edge actions (fire, absorb, side-shift) go through\n1812\t`input.tap`, so the human path (mapping, double-tap, flick) is exercised. `bot.menu(path)` navigates screens by\n1813\twidget id: it taps the arrows to reach the focus, then confirm.\n1814\t\n1815\t### 7.4 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (the season suite and the `playthrough` test)\n1816\t\n1817\tOne test plays the game end to end, headless, on fixed seeds, asserting along the way:\n1818\t1. Boot → title.\n1819\t2. Wait 10 s → attract (assert it is running, weapons seen, at least 2 tracks across the playlist with\n1820\t   `game.advance(120)`) → a key press → title.\n1821\t3. → menu → ACADEMY (the bot passes the drills) → SEASON: prologue → E1…E10 in order, each via the season hub, bot\n1822\t   driving, ≥ bronze (retry up to 3 times, asserting progress), the briefings advanced by taps.\n1823\t4. Promotions unlock FLARE and STORM.\n1824\t5. GP: 4 races; assert the points and the standings screen."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"df58ef6c-5a1d-4f0a-894b-b7e4ffcdda7f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:45:05.632Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**The vertical slice at the end of M5** must already *play* like the game: a full race with AI and weapons on every\ntrack. If time runs short later, the plan's priorities hold:\n1. a feature's existence and correctness (§8);\n2. the playthrough test;\n3. the look;\n4. the quantity of content.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk (when) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | **The 3D stack in one file** (an inline ES module, an import map to the CDN, file://, WebGPU → WebGL 2 fallback, headless Chromium) | Nothing else works if it doesn't. It is new to most builders | **M0 spike first.** Prove the bundle from file:// in Playwright with a picture. If the CDN is blocked in the test environment, retry once, then vendor `three.webgpu.min.js`, `three.core.min.js` (imported by it), `three.tsl.min.js` and `rapier.mjs` as inline modules: rewrite the import map to `data:`/blob URLs made by a tiny classic loader, or inline the files as `<script type=\"module\">` with the specifiers mapped to blob URLs. Keep the CDN as the default (smaller file) |\n| 2 | **Frame and handedness bugs** (a left-handed engine frame, bank signs, camera roll sign, `toThree`) | Silent wrongness: mirrored steering, banks the wrong way, a camera rolling backwards | Unit tests in M1 (§7.2) before any physics. One `SN.frame` helper, used everywhere. A screenshot check of the roll on the Karakum spiral (M3) |\n| 3 | **Physics at 3,000 u/s** (tunnelling, jitter on crests, stuck on walls, overpasses confusing the track lookup) | The core feel. Hard to see in code review | Track-space walls are analytic (no tunnelling). Local-only `locate`. Invariant tests over long random-input runs (M2). Dev sliders for live tuning. The App. C jump numbers become tests |\n| 4 | **AI that finishes on every track** (the jump speeds, hairpins, overpass, open edges, the drop in a curve) | A stuck AI breaks races, attract, the season playthrough and medal calibration | One line/profile generator plus a PD controller, tested on 4 tracks × 4 classes × 4 seeds in M4. A stuck detector, rescue, and a per-track min-speed constraint at the gap |\n| 5 | **Determinism** (replays, the hub's fair start, hashes) | Any `Math.random`, dt or order dependence breaks replays | §2.8 rules. A lint test that greps the sim files for `Math.random`, `Date.now` and `performance.now`. Hash-equality tests from M4 on |\n| 6 | **Shader stalls and loading hitches** (World3D compiles on first use) | Visible hitches at GO or on the first weapon | Materials only at world creation. The warm-up frame and `world.prepare()` in loading (§3.7). Frame-time logging in the M3 browser test |\n| 7 | **Scope** (11 modes, 4 tracks, season, audio, hub) | Running out of time with stubs left (the brief forbids stubs) | Milestone order puts every feature in a minimal complete form before polish. The §8 checklist is the definition of done. Cut quantity, never features |\n| 8 | **Hub conformance** (card, ready without keys, time-up, end, ghosts) | The hub keeps failing games out of sessions | The Node mock early (M11 start), then the real harness at 1, 2 and 4 players with network faults and host-leave. The session path shares the race code, so it adds little new code |\n| 9 | **Synth music quality** | Bad music undermines the source's identity | The engine edits (filter env, unison) make house/acid/trance timbres possible. Compose at least 16 bars with A/B sections and use layers. A headless check that songs parse. A listen in the browser (the builder has no ears, so check with `audio.pos` and drift) |\n| 10 | **Readability at 10 feet** (a 427×240 HUD on a TV) | Tiny text is the default trap | HUD at scale 2 minimum for numbers, the large-HUD option, ≤ 6 items per screen. Screenshots at 1920×1080 scaled down to 50 % must stay legible (📷 M6) |\n| 11 | **Analog triggers and DualSense mapping** | The engine reads only `pressed` | Engine edit §2.7.3, tested with a stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()` in Playwright (axes and button `value`) |\n| 12 | **/tmp nearly full** (a shared tmpfs) | Playwright and Chromium need temp space | `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp` for every tool run (§0) |\n| 13 | **Terrain intersecting the track or tunnels** | The ground poking through decks or tunnel interiors looks broken | The corridor grid carve (§3.7) plus portal frames. 📷 every tunnel portal and every elevated section in M3 |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing (one command)\n\n**The command:** `cd SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728 && TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp node tests/run.mjs`.\nIt runs every suite (Node first, then browser, then the hub harness). It prints **only failures** (suite › test:\nmessage, plus the snapshot JSON where useful) and **one final line**:\n`412 passed, 0 failed (node 380, browser 22, hub 10) in 96 s`.\n- `node tests/run.mjs physics race` runs only the named suites.\n- `--node` skips the browser and hub suites.\n- Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (the suites map to files, listed in `tests/run.mjs`).\n\n### 7.1 Harness\n\n`tests/lib/vm.mjs` follows the handoff's `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`:\n- a `vm` context with stand-ins `window = ctx`, `addEventListener() {}`, `location: { search: '', hash: '' }`,\n  `matchMedia`, `navigator: { maxTouchPoints: 0, getGamepads: () => [] }`;\n- it runs `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then the `src/` files in manifest order;\n- `E.current` is the game, and `game.advance(s)` drives it;\n- scripted input through `game.input.tap/hold/press`, `input.feed` for the mouse, and `SN.vpad` for analog;\n- assertions through `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n\n```js\ngame.debug = {\n  snapshot: () => ({ scene, state, mode, track, cls, t, ships: [{ id, p, s, u, h, v, kmh, energy, lap, place, weapon, airborne, finished, elim }],\n                     player: {...}, hudCallouts: [...], focus: ui.focusId, device: input.lastDevice, attract: bool, dev: bool,\n                     season: { medals, unlocked }, hub: { connected, sent, progressCount } }),\n  teleport(s, u = 0, v = 0), give(weapon), setEnergy(x), finishNow(), events: () => race.events.slice(),\n  race: () => race, track: () => track, tune: SN.Tune\n};\n```\n\n### 7.2 Node suites (fast, about 60 s in all)\n\n- **unit:**\n  - math and frames (8 headings), bank sign, `toThree` mapping;\n  - the spline: closure, arc length, knot s;\n  - each TrackDef validates;\n  - feature s-values; `query` returns the right deck at overpasses;\n  - the racing line inside the bounds; speed profile ≤ top;\n  - Tune def/reset;\n  - the input mapping: double-tap, flick, ramped keys;\n  - the hash is stable;\n  - **lint:** the sim files contain no `Math.random`, `Date.now`, `performance.now`, `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`\n    or `window.open`, and no file contains TODO.\n- **physics:**\n  - every feel target in §3.2;\n  - jumps: Karakum's gap at 70 / 80 / 90 / 140 m/s (fails at 70, clears at ≥ 80, landing window as App. C ±15 %), drops\n    land at 45 and 170 m/s;\n  - long random-input soak (10 simulated minutes, 4 tracks): no NaN, never `|u| > hw` on walled decks, never `h < 0`;\n  - overpass: a craft on the upper deck stays on it (its s stays in the upper range);\n  - pads, pit recharge, side-shift, roll ok/botch, rescue after an open-edge fall;\n  - launch boost window.\n- **race:**\n  - 4 tracks × 4 classes × 2 seeds of 8 AI: all finish, no stuck, rescues ≤ 1 per craft, lap times within ±25 % of\n    §4.2;\n  - positions sorted by progress; wrong way; final-lap event; results;\n  - determinism (2 runs, equal hash); replay re-sim equals the hash.\n- **weapons:** every row of §3.4, each in a fixed two-craft setup, plus AI usage counts.\n- **modes:** time trial (+ ghost round trip), hot lap (flying start, best lap), snipeout (scoring, respawn, the target\n  ends it), overclock (zones, tempo events, end), academy (the bot passes 11 drills), versus (2 viewports, half-keys\n  labels), grand prix (points table, ties).\n- **flow:**\n  - title → menu → setup → race → results → replay → menu;\n  - pause menu items present (Restart, Camera, How to play, Dev mode, Quit) and absent in a session;\n  - settings keys exist;\n  - glyph labels per device and setting;\n  - touch-only notice;\n  - attract timing and exit;\n  - dev sliders and reset; each cheat.\n- **season:** §7.4.\n- **audio:** song parsing, event → sound map, `Voice` durations, the music director's layer changes (headless:\n  `audio.pos`).\n- **hub (mock):** §7.6.\n\n### 7.3 The player bot (`tests/lib/bot.mjs`)\n\n`bot.drive(playerIndex, { skill: 1, weapons: true, rolls: true })`. Each step it computes `SN.AI.controls(ship, race)`\nfor the human's craft and writes them into `SN.vpad[i]`. Edge actions (fire, absorb, side-shift) go through\n`input.tap`, so the human path (mapping, double-tap, flick) is exercised. `bot.menu(path)` navigates screens by\nwidget id: it taps the arrows to reach the focus, then confirm.\n\n### 7.4 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (the season suite and the `playthrough` test)\n\nOne test plays the game end to end, headless, on fixed seeds, asserting along the way:\n1. Boot → title.\n2. Wait 10 s → attract (assert it is running, weapons seen, at least 2 tracks across the playlist with\n   `game.advance(120)`) → a key press → title.\n3. → menu → ACADEMY (the bot passes the drills) → SEASON: prologue → E1…E10 in order, each via the season hub, bot\n   driving, ≥ bronze (retry up to 3 times, asserting progress), the briefings advanced by taps.\n4. Promotions unlock FLARE and STORM.\n5. GP: 4 races; assert the points and the standings screen.","numLines":120,"startLine":1705,"totalLines":2081}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015oazBkd5yEsCwLVohj7FqT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
