{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LjS1w8478LyeToYuDwQwD3","type":"tool_result","content":"1824\t5. GP: 4 races; assert the points and the standings screen.\n1825\t6. The ending lines and the credits play; SINGULARITY is unlocked.\n1826\t7. Then QUICK RACE at SINGULARITY on Borealis; TIME TRIAL Karakum (a ghost saved, then loaded on the next run); HOT\n1827\t   LAP Meridian; SNIPEOUT Solenne; OVERCLOCK to zone 10; VERSUS with `game.addPlayer({ keys: 'right' })` and two\n1828\t   bots; REPLAY of the last race (hash equal).\n1829\t8. The pause menu → Dev mode → slider → reset → close; Settings → Button symbols → Xbox (labels change); About pages\n1830\t   1–5.\n1831\t9. `game.errors.length === 0` throughout.\n1832\t\n1833\t### 7.5 Browser suites (Playwright, Chromium headless; `tests/browser/`)\n1834\t\n1835\t- `bundle loads`: file:// URL; no `pageerror`; `My3D2dge.World3D.backend` is set; the boot completes in < 20 s.\n1836\t- `renders`: in the race, sample the `#view` canvas (`toDataURL` or a screenshot) and require at least 40 % non-black\n1837\t  pixels and > 24 distinct colours; the HUD canvas is drawn.\n1838\t- `input devices`:\n1839\t  - keyboard thrust raises the speed;\n1840\t  - stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()` (a DualSense-like id, standard mapping): ✕ thrust, L2 `value: .5` halves the\n1841\t    airbrake, and prompts show ✕/□/○ glyphs;\n1842\t  - the Xbox setting shows A/X/B;\n1843\t  - the mouse hovers and clicks a menu tile.\n1844\t- `screens`: the flow through the menus with screenshots to `tests/out/` (📷 reviewed by the builder only for look:\n1845\t  layout, legibility, art).\n1846\t- `split screen`: 2 viewports draw two different camera poses (the pixels differ between the halves).\n1847\t- `touch-only`: emulate a phone (`hasTouch`, coarse pointer, no keyboard events) → the notice and the SETTINGS button\n1848\t  are visible, and no engine touch buttons are drawn; after 10 s the attract runs.\n1849\t- **Performance is out of scope** (TASK.md), but log the median frame time per track to `tests/out/perf.json` for\n1850\t  information.\n1851\t\n1852\t### 7.6 AI Hub tests\n1853\t\n1854\t- **Node mock** (`tests/hub/mock.mjs`): a fake `AIHub` installed before the game's scripts (`active: true`, `connect`\n1855\t  resolves `info` for seat 1 of 2, events delivered by the test). It asserts:\n1856\t  - no title or menu scenes are entered;\n1857\t  - `ready()` is called exactly once with no input;\n1858\t  - nothing moves before `start`;\n1859\t  - the race begins at `time() ≥ 0`;\n1860\t  - `progress` is called ≥ once a second, with a numeric score and a label;\n1861\t  - `send` is ≤ 20/s, unreliable, ≤ 16 KB;\n1862\t  - an incoming message creates and moves a ghost;\n1863\t  - `leave` removes it;\n1864\t  - `result({ time })` on finish (bot);\n1865\t  - `time-up` before the finish → `result({ score })` once;\n1866\t  - `end` → input ignored, music stopped, no further `send`;\n1867\t  - `card` events: Enter → `answer('ready')`, △ → `answer('more')`.\n1868\t- **Real harness** (`tests/hub/hub.test.mjs`):\n1869\t  1. Copy the bundle into a scratch dir inside `tests/out/hub/` with the pinned `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and\n1870\t     `round.js`.\n1871\t  2. Spawn `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there, and parse the port from its first output line.\n1872\t  3. Fetch `/<bundle>.html` and confirm its `<title>` is `Snipeout HD` (it is our page).\n1873\t  4. Open `harness.html?game=<bundle>.html&players=2&auto=1` in Playwright, wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]`\n1874\t     (timeout 240 s), and read `window.__hubCheck`. Require `pass === true`, and print the failed checks otherwise.\n1875\t  5. Repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, and with `&scenario=host-leave`.\n1876\t  6. Kill the server **by its PID** (the child process you spawned).\n1877\t\n1878\t### 7.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge)\n1879\t\n1880\tPer track:\n1881\t- grid at the countdown;\n1882\t- chase cam mid-corner (bank and roll);\n1883\t- cockpit;\n1884\t- tunnel;\n1885\t- jump in flight;\n1886\t- overpass from below and above (Karakum, Meridian);\n1887\t- a weapon effect (each weapon once across tracks);\n1888\t- the Overclock skin at zone 1 and zone 20;\n1889\t- split screen.\n1890\t\n1891\tScreens: title, attract with DEMO, every menu screen, team select (each craft), results with podium, the season hub,\n1892\ta briefing with portrait, the dev panel (each tab), About pages, the touch-only notice, the hub card.\n1893\t\n1894\tReview them for: legibility at 10 feet (view at 50 %), contrast, colour-only information, a HUD clear of the corner,\n1895\tnothing clipped at 4:3, 16:9 or 21:9 (`expand: true` sizes: 1024×768, 1280×720, 2560×1080).\n1896\t\n1897\t---\n1898\t\n1899\t## 8. Definition of done: every TASK.md requirement, where it lives, how it is proven\n1900\t\n1901\t| TASK.md requirement | Where in the game | Proof |\n1902\t| --- | --- | --- |\n1903\t| Genre and perspective that fit the source | anti-gravity combat racing; chase, far and cockpit cams plus TV cameras (§1, §3.6) | 📷 M3 |\n1904\t| Title: a riff picked by a real RNG | **Snipeout HD** (§0, `secrets.randbelow`) | — |\n1905\t| One HTML file named `SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728.html` (CDN dependencies allowed) | `tools/bundle.mjs` (§2.3) | browser: bundle loads |\n1906\t| Dev files in the subfolder; bundle in the root | §2.2 | — |\n1907\t| Built on the handoff; engine changes allowed | §2.1, §2.7 (marked edits) | About → engine changes |\n1908\t| Art: the engine's native style plus new assets that feel like the source | pixel-res World3D, toon/lambert, pixel HUD/fonts; new craft, tracks, neon, sponsors (§3.7, §4) | 📷 |\n1909\t| Animation: the engine's system plus new animations | rigs (cards, poses `cheer` / `wave` / `hips`, portraits that talk), tweens/scripts; new procedural craft animation (roll, flaps, glow, trails, barrel roll, explosions, drone), HUD/menu tweens (§3.7, §3.8) | 📷 |\n1910\t| Audio all in code; gibberish voices | the synth plus edits, 6 songs, SFX, hums, `SN.Voice` (§3.10) | audio suite |\n1911\t| Online: AI Hub integration, and multiplayer for the game on its own | ghost-mode sessions (§3.16); local 2P split-screen VERSUS | hub mock + real harness; versus test |\n1912\t| Feature-complete demo, long enough to show every mechanic | 11 modes, the season with a GP and an ending, the academy (§1, §3.3, §4.5) | the playthrough §7.4 |\n1913\t| Dev mode from the pause menu; live sliders and reset | §3.15 | flow: dev |\n1914\t| Attract mode: 10 s idle, AI demo, any input exits, may cheat | §3.14 | flow: attract |\n1915\t| Narrative tone like the source | §3.11, §4.5 | review |\n1916\t| 10-foot, controller-first, DualSense standard mapping | §3.9; analog triggers (§2.7.3) | browser: input devices |\n1917\t| Keyboard native, PC keys; mouse aims, looks, clicks; hover moves focus | §1 controls; mouse menus, fire/absorb, click-to-follow in replays, drag-rotate in team select | flow + browser |\n1918\t| Prompts follow the last device; PlayStation default; Settings option for Xbox | `55-glyphs.js`; `glyphs` default and option in Settings (§2.7.1) | flow + browser |\n1919\t| No dense web-style data screens | ≤ 6 items, big type, one row per craft (§3.9) | 📷 |\n1920\t| Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus a settings button, attract runs | §3.9 / §3.14 | browser: touch-only |\n1921\t| No TODOs, placeholders, stubs | bundle lint, unit lint (§2.3, §7.2) | tests |\n1922\t| Testing: headless scripts, `game.advance` / `game.debug`, a scripted whole-game playthrough, one command, failures only plus a one-line count | §7 | `node tests/run.mjs` |\n1923\t| Servers on 127.0.0.1 port 0, our page confirmed, stopped by PID | §7.6 | hub test |\n1924\t| Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About/Credits screen | §3.18 | About pages; reply |\n1925\t| `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape, parses | `tools/exit-interview.mjs` (§3.18) | the script checks `JSON.parse` |\n1926\t\n1927\t---\n1928\t\n1929\t## Appendix A: reference code (use as is)\n1930\t\n1931\t**Centripetal Catmull-Rom (closed) and the arc-length resample.** This is the code the planning checker used. The §4.3\n1932\tnumbers come from it.\n1933\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"ebdd0362-4bad-4557-b17a-f114a287df9d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:45:12.894Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/work/PLAN.md","content":"5. GP: 4 races; assert the points and the standings screen.\n6. The ending lines and the credits play; SINGULARITY is unlocked.\n7. Then QUICK RACE at SINGULARITY on Borealis; TIME TRIAL Karakum (a ghost saved, then loaded on the next run); HOT\n   LAP Meridian; SNIPEOUT Solenne; OVERCLOCK to zone 10; VERSUS with `game.addPlayer({ keys: 'right' })` and two\n   bots; REPLAY of the last race (hash equal).\n8. The pause menu → Dev mode → slider → reset → close; Settings → Button symbols → Xbox (labels change); About pages\n   1–5.\n9. `game.errors.length === 0` throughout.\n\n### 7.5 Browser suites (Playwright, Chromium headless; `tests/browser/`)\n\n- `bundle loads`: file:// URL; no `pageerror`; `My3D2dge.World3D.backend` is set; the boot completes in < 20 s.\n- `renders`: in the race, sample the `#view` canvas (`toDataURL` or a screenshot) and require at least 40 % non-black\n  pixels and > 24 distinct colours; the HUD canvas is drawn.\n- `input devices`:\n  - keyboard thrust raises the speed;\n  - stubbed `navigator.getGamepads()` (a DualSense-like id, standard mapping): ✕ thrust, L2 `value: .5` halves the\n    airbrake, and prompts show ✕/□/○ glyphs;\n  - the Xbox setting shows A/X/B;\n  - the mouse hovers and clicks a menu tile.\n- `screens`: the flow through the menus with screenshots to `tests/out/` (📷 reviewed by the builder only for look:\n  layout, legibility, art).\n- `split screen`: 2 viewports draw two different camera poses (the pixels differ between the halves).\n- `touch-only`: emulate a phone (`hasTouch`, coarse pointer, no keyboard events) → the notice and the SETTINGS button\n  are visible, and no engine touch buttons are drawn; after 10 s the attract runs.\n- **Performance is out of scope** (TASK.md), but log the median frame time per track to `tests/out/perf.json` for\n  information.\n\n### 7.6 AI Hub tests\n\n- **Node mock** (`tests/hub/mock.mjs`): a fake `AIHub` installed before the game's scripts (`active: true`, `connect`\n  resolves `info` for seat 1 of 2, events delivered by the test). It asserts:\n  - no title or menu scenes are entered;\n  - `ready()` is called exactly once with no input;\n  - nothing moves before `start`;\n  - the race begins at `time() ≥ 0`;\n  - `progress` is called ≥ once a second, with a numeric score and a label;\n  - `send` is ≤ 20/s, unreliable, ≤ 16 KB;\n  - an incoming message creates and moves a ghost;\n  - `leave` removes it;\n  - `result({ time })` on finish (bot);\n  - `time-up` before the finish → `result({ score })` once;\n  - `end` → input ignored, music stopped, no further `send`;\n  - `card` events: Enter → `answer('ready')`, △ → `answer('more')`.\n- **Real harness** (`tests/hub/hub.test.mjs`):\n  1. Copy the bundle into a scratch dir inside `tests/out/hub/` with the pinned `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and\n     `round.js`.\n  2. Spawn `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there, and parse the port from its first output line.\n  3. Fetch `/<bundle>.html` and confirm its `<title>` is `Snipeout HD` (it is our page).\n  4. Open `harness.html?game=<bundle>.html&players=2&auto=1` in Playwright, wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]`\n     (timeout 240 s), and read `window.__hubCheck`. Require `pass === true`, and print the failed checks otherwise.\n  5. Repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, and with `&scenario=host-leave`.\n  6. Kill the server **by its PID** (the child process you spawned).\n\n### 7.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge)\n\nPer track:\n- grid at the countdown;\n- chase cam mid-corner (bank and roll);\n- cockpit;\n- tunnel;\n- jump in flight;\n- overpass from below and above (Karakum, Meridian);\n- a weapon effect (each weapon once across tracks);\n- the Overclock skin at zone 1 and zone 20;\n- split screen.\n\nScreens: title, attract with DEMO, every menu screen, team select (each craft), results with podium, the season hub,\na briefing with portrait, the dev panel (each tab), About pages, the touch-only notice, the hub card.\n\nReview them for: legibility at 10 feet (view at 50 %), contrast, colour-only information, a HUD clear of the corner,\nnothing clipped at 4:3, 16:9 or 21:9 (`expand: true` sizes: 1024×768, 1280×720, 2560×1080).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Definition of done: every TASK.md requirement, where it lives, how it is proven\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Where in the game | Proof |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Genre and perspective that fit the source | anti-gravity combat racing; chase, far and cockpit cams plus TV cameras (§1, §3.6) | 📷 M3 |\n| Title: a riff picked by a real RNG | **Snipeout HD** (§0, `secrets.randbelow`) | — |\n| One HTML file named `SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728.html` (CDN dependencies allowed) | `tools/bundle.mjs` (§2.3) | browser: bundle loads |\n| Dev files in the subfolder; bundle in the root | §2.2 | — |\n| Built on the handoff; engine changes allowed | §2.1, §2.7 (marked edits) | About → engine changes |\n| Art: the engine's native style plus new assets that feel like the source | pixel-res World3D, toon/lambert, pixel HUD/fonts; new craft, tracks, neon, sponsors (§3.7, §4) | 📷 |\n| Animation: the engine's system plus new animations | rigs (cards, poses `cheer` / `wave` / `hips`, portraits that talk), tweens/scripts; new procedural craft animation (roll, flaps, glow, trails, barrel roll, explosions, drone), HUD/menu tweens (§3.7, §3.8) | 📷 |\n| Audio all in code; gibberish voices | the synth plus edits, 6 songs, SFX, hums, `SN.Voice` (§3.10) | audio suite |\n| Online: AI Hub integration, and multiplayer for the game on its own | ghost-mode sessions (§3.16); local 2P split-screen VERSUS | hub mock + real harness; versus test |\n| Feature-complete demo, long enough to show every mechanic | 11 modes, the season with a GP and an ending, the academy (§1, §3.3, §4.5) | the playthrough §7.4 |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu; live sliders and reset | §3.15 | flow: dev |\n| Attract mode: 10 s idle, AI demo, any input exits, may cheat | §3.14 | flow: attract |\n| Narrative tone like the source | §3.11, §4.5 | review |\n| 10-foot, controller-first, DualSense standard mapping | §3.9; analog triggers (§2.7.3) | browser: input devices |\n| Keyboard native, PC keys; mouse aims, looks, clicks; hover moves focus | §1 controls; mouse menus, fire/absorb, click-to-follow in replays, drag-rotate in team select | flow + browser |\n| Prompts follow the last device; PlayStation default; Settings option for Xbox | `55-glyphs.js`; `glyphs` default and option in Settings (§2.7.1) | flow + browser |\n| No dense web-style data screens | ≤ 6 items, big type, one row per craft (§3.9) | 📷 |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus a settings button, attract runs | §3.9 / §3.14 | browser: touch-only |\n| No TODOs, placeholders, stubs | bundle lint, unit lint (§2.3, §7.2) | tests |\n| Testing: headless scripts, `game.advance` / `game.debug`, a scripted whole-game playthrough, one command, failures only plus a one-line count | §7 | `node tests/run.mjs` |\n| Servers on 127.0.0.1 port 0, our page confirmed, stopped by PID | §7.6 | hub test |\n| Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About/Credits screen | §3.18 | About pages; reply |\n| `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape, parses | `tools/exit-interview.mjs` (§3.18) | the script checks `JSON.parse` |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: reference code (use as is)\n\n**Centripetal Catmull-Rom (closed) and the arc-length resample.** This is the code the planning checker used. The §4.3\nnumbers come from it.\n","numLines":110,"startLine":1824,"totalLines":2081}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LjS1w8478LyeToYuDwQwD3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
