{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016wJqprtJoQpcBLtyoCVQmi","type":"tool_result","content":"# SNIPEOUT HD\n  2082 162820 PLAN.md\nfences: 40\n33:3. A system must be complete before it is pretty. The brief forbids TODOs, placeholders and stubs in the delivered\n248:  source contains `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX` or `placeholder`, and that no `<script src=` remains. It prints the file size.\n1705:| **M12** | Polish and ship | scenery density, effects, juice (shake, flashes, rumble via `input.rumble`), the balance pass with the sliders, medal calibration (`tools/medals.mjs`), the About pages filled, `exit-interview.json`, the final bundle | the full `node tests/run.mjs` passes; `tools/bundle.mjs` passes its checks (no TODO, an identical hub client); `node engine/handoff/tools/check.mjs ../<bundle>.html` gives no errors (it will list the CDN files as external, which is expected); 📷 the final screenshot set (§7.7) |\n1778:    or `window.open`, and no file contains TODO.\n1923:| No TODOs, placeholders, stubs | bundle lint, unit lint (§2.3, §7.2) | tests |\n28:## 0. How to use this plan\n48:## 1. The game on one page\n103:## 2. Tech stack and architecture\n105:### 2.1 Stack (pinned)\n144:### 2.2 Dev folder layout\n201:### 2.3 The page and the bundle\n250:### 2.4 Units, axes, conventions (bugs hide here: unit-test them first)\n273:### 2.5 Modules and their public surfaces\n311:### 2.6 Scenes (engine scenes) and the flow\n335:### 2.7 Engine changes (make them in M0–M2; mark each `// SNIPEOUT EDIT:`)\n367:### 2.8 Determinism rules\n379:## 3. Systems\n381:### 3.1 Track system (`20-track.js`)\n467:### 3.2 Craft physics and handling (`25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js`)\n607:### 3.3 Race director and modes (`40-race.js`)\n651:### 3.4 Weapons and pickups (`30-weapons.js`, `06-data-weapons.js`)\n687:### 3.5 AI pilots (`35-ai.js`)\n738:### 3.6 Cameras and the TV director (`60-render.js`)\n781:### 3.7 Rendering (`60-render.js`, `62-shipkit.js`, `64-trackmesh.js`, `66-scenery.js`, `68-fx.js`)\n897:### 3.8 HUD (`70-hud.js`): pixel art at game resolution, anchored to `r.W × r.H`\n928:### 3.9 Front-end, UI and UX: 10-foot and controller-first (`75-ui.js`, `55-glyphs.js`, `01-input.js`)\n1009:### 3.10 Audio (`50-audio.js`, `10-data-music.js`): all synthesized, no files\n1094:### 3.11 Narrative and writing style (`09-data-story.js`)\n1126:### 3.12 Season, progression, saves (`08-data-season.js`, `78-season-ui.js`)\n1147:### 3.13 Replays, ghosts, records (`45-replay.js`)\n1160:### 3.14 Attract mode (`85-attract.js`)\n1181:### 3.15 Dev mode and live tuning (`80-dev.js`, `SN.Tune` in `00-core.js`)\n1198:### 3.16 Multiplayer: local split screen and AI Hub sessions\n1254:### 3.17 Settings: the game's own, beside the engine's standard ones\n1275:### 3.18 About / Credits and the exit interview (`11-data-about.js`)\n1317:## 4. Content\n1319:### 4.1 Teams, craft, pilots, principals (`05-data-teams.js`)\n1380:### 4.2 Speed classes\n1398:### 4.3 Tracks (`07-data-tracks.js`): layouts checked during planning\n1584:### 4.4 Weapon icons and pickup look\n1605:### 4.5 Season events, story beats, academy drills, radio (`08-data-season.js`, `09-data-story.js`)\n1661:### 4.6 Sponsors and signage (`66-scenery.js` canvas textures)\n1685:## 5. Build order and milestones\n1716:## 6. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1736:## 7. Testing (one command)\n1746:### 7.1 Harness\n1766:### 7.2 Node suites (fast, about 60 s in all)\n1809:### 7.3 The player bot (`tests/lib/bot.mjs`)\n1816:### 7.4 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (the season suite and the `playthrough` test)\n1834:### 7.5 Browser suites (Playwright, Chromium headless; `tests/browser/`)\n1853:### 7.6 AI Hub tests\n1880:### 7.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge)\n1901:## 8. Definition of done: every TASK.md requirement, where it lives, how it is proven\n1931:## Appendix A: reference code (use as is)\n1993:## Appendix B: gibberish voice (`SN.Voice`)\n2019:## Appendix C: planning-script results (`tools/trackcheck.mjs` must reproduce them)\n2034:## Appendix D: AI Hub session skeleton (`90-hub.js`)\n2058:## Appendix E: World3D facts learned in planning (saves the builders an afternoon)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f","uuid":"f0056cdb-8b30-4b39-abcd-17fe8747c8db","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:45:42.116Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# SNIPEOUT HD\n  2082 162820 PLAN.md\nfences: 40\n33:3. A system must be complete before it is pretty. The brief forbids TODOs, placeholders and stubs in the delivered\n248:  source contains `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX` or `placeholder`, and that no `<script src=` remains. It prints the file size.\n1705:| **M12** | Polish and ship | scenery density, effects, juice (shake, flashes, rumble via `input.rumble`), the balance pass with the sliders, medal calibration (`tools/medals.mjs`), the About pages filled, `exit-interview.json`, the final bundle | the full `node tests/run.mjs` passes; `tools/bundle.mjs` passes its checks (no TODO, an identical hub client); `node engine/handoff/tools/check.mjs ../<bundle>.html` gives no errors (it will list the CDN files as external, which is expected); 📷 the final screenshot set (§7.7) |\n1778:    or `window.open`, and no file contains TODO.\n1923:| No TODOs, placeholders, stubs | bundle lint, unit lint (§2.3, §7.2) | tests |\n28:## 0. How to use this plan\n48:## 1. The game on one page\n103:## 2. Tech stack and architecture\n105:### 2.1 Stack (pinned)\n144:### 2.2 Dev folder layout\n201:### 2.3 The page and the bundle\n250:### 2.4 Units, axes, conventions (bugs hide here: unit-test them first)\n273:### 2.5 Modules and their public surfaces\n311:### 2.6 Scenes (engine scenes) and the flow\n335:### 2.7 Engine changes (make them in M0–M2; mark each `// SNIPEOUT EDIT:`)\n367:### 2.8 Determinism rules\n379:## 3. Systems\n381:### 3.1 Track system (`20-track.js`)\n467:### 3.2 Craft physics and handling (`25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js`)